VALUES
	(2,2,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','69.3.70.44','2005-07-02 13:21:21','2005-07-02 20:21:21','i think our hesitancy to relinquish any power whatsoever will eventually lead to the u.s. taking what will become a historically embarrassing fall in the next few decades.',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(3,2,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-02 13:35:42','2005-07-02 20:35:42','Our own hubris? Probably. I think the entertainment industry likes to harp on that idea (note themes in Batman Begins and Episode III).',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(4,6,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','67.160.12.204','2005-07-03 19:32:18','2005-07-04 02:32:18','What about providing a service?',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1; .NET CLR 1.1.4322)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5,6,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-03 19:33:58','2005-07-04 02:33:58','I lumped that into \"charge a usage fee\"...assuming that the fee was for a service ;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(6,8,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','69.3.70.44','2005-07-03 20:36:15','2005-07-04 03:36:15','The \"smaller headlights below real headlights\" are foglights. The problem is that they can be added pretty cheaply onto most cars (Focuses included).\r\n\r\nI had no idea this crap was going on -- don\'t the over-zealous, ticket-you-for-going-28-in-a-25-zone Medina police ever run into this guy?',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(7,6,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','69.3.70.44','2005-07-03 20:40:20','2005-07-04 03:40:20','I guess that makes sense, but I feel like \"usage\" isn\'t a completely accurate category for things like design, consulting, accounting, etc.',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(8,8,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-03 23:18:29','2005-07-04 06:18:29','You would think. But they tend to park their cars at various intersections and then leave them without anyone in it. I seroiusly want to move one a couple blocks over sometime and see how long it takes them to realize that a cop car was actually \"stolen.\"',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(9,6,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-03 23:29:45','2005-07-04 06:29:45','fixed',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(10,2,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','69.3.70.44','2005-07-04 03:28:11','2005-07-04 10:28:11','I don\'t even know if it\'s all hubris. Part of me thinks that all we want to do is <i>not</i> lose our position as \"Country of Super Ridiculous Power #1\" but in doing so, we\'re clutching onto our old ways so tightly that we don\'t change with the times. I mean, look at all the \"traditional values\" that the conservative right (the folks in power, somehow) are fighting tooth and nail to hang on to. Sometimes it seems to me that all our regression and stagnance as a country is in an attempt to reach back at the shining moments of our nation (post WWII, greatest generation, etc.). Unfortunately, such a reach just ends up being a pathetic, counter-productive struggle that prevents us from adapting and makes us seem like arrogant dickwads.',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(11,2,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-04 03:35:44','2005-07-04 10:35:44','Amazing how we can simultaneously be the most advanced and most regressed nation in the world, no? \r\n\r\nHappy 4th.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(12,9,'Natalie Glance','nglance@intelliseek.com','http://www.blogpulse.com','64.158.138.50','2005-07-04 17:49:49','2005-07-05 00:49:49','Hi Jason,\r\n\r\nHere\'s a quick trick for finding all of your posts on BlogPulse: search for\r\n\r\nurl:\"http://www.jason-preston.com\"\r\n\r\nYes, this is arcane and currently undocumented on the site.  (\"url\" means the url of one\'s blog.)  We\'ll soon be rolling out new functionality that makes this more transparent.....\r\n\r\nIf you search simply for http://www.jason-preston.com, you will get all posts linking to your blog, *excluding* your own posts.  We call links from your blog to itself self-links.  There\'s no one linking to your blog yet, but that\'s not surprising as your blog is so new.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.7) Gecko/20050414 Firefox/1.0.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(13,9,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-04 19:19:09','2005-07-05 02:19:09','Ok, cool, that does work. Thanks!\r\n\r\nYou know, I think the next big step in web site optimization is going to be blog search optimization, as more and more companies adopt blogs for an actual web presence. \r\n\r\nThat\'s going to make it harder for individual bloggers to get noticed, I bet.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(14,17,'Tinu','tinu@freetraffictip.com','','172.198.72.144','2005-07-11 12:46:50','2005-07-11 19:46:50','Well amen. This is a really good, user-friendly explanation of why podcasting is so fantastic. Found you through the podcasting technorati tag... and . In the words of Arnold? I\'ll be back. :)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.7) Gecko/20050414 Firefox/1.0.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(15,17,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-11 12:53:15','2005-07-11 19:53:15','Technorati is a wonderful thing...\r\n\r\nyou have a blog of your own somewhere?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(16,17,'Tinu','tinu@freetraffictip.com','http://www.freetraffictip.com','172.198.72.144','2005-07-11 13:10:16','2005-07-11 20:10:16','Yeah. The one I own is at www.freetraffictip.com - I also contribute to websearch.about.com and blog.rssapplied.com . And yes. Technorati is its own heaven. It was on the fritz recently but they seem to be cleaning up their issues. Good thing too because I\'ve been waiting to do an article on them for one of my blogs.\r\n\r\nNice to e-meet you Jason.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.7) Gecko/20050414 Firefox/1.0.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(17,17,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-11 13:18:21','2005-07-11 20:18:21','Neat. I\'ve been trying to get around to making a podcast for a while, but I don\'t want to solo the project, and I\'m kind of waiting until my other stuff gets off the ground, too ;)\r\n\r\nNice to e-meet you, too.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(18,17,'Tinu','tinu@freetraffictip.com','http://www.freetraffictip.com','172.198.72.144','2005-07-11 14:18:36','2005-07-11 21:18:36','Yeah, I know what you mean. I did what I was calling a mini-cast, but I stopped because I wanted to do a \"real\" show. And now people are asking me, hey, WTF happened to your podcast show. So I realized, if having a really professional show is slowing me down there, especially now that I\'m showing up in iTunes and on Odeo, I need to keep pushing out new content until I have time to do something snazzier, or outsource the project. :-D \r\n\r\nLet me know when it goes up, maybe there\'s something you know that I don\'t, that my listeners would want to hear about... and I can interview you.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.7) Gecko/20050414 Firefox/1.0.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(20,17,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-11 22:31:01','2005-07-12 05:31:01','I\'ll let you know, absolutely. My first cast is likely going to be more like college radio. Just going to try for a small college audience, do some nicely illegal mixes and campus news, that type of thing. \r\n\r\nThe point is more to learn by doing than to amass a huge audience, I guess. \r\n\r\nI\'d be more than happy to do an interview for you if you ever come up with a topic I\'m qualified to speak on.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(21,31,'Tinu','tinu@freetraffictip.com','http://www.freetraffictip.com','172.197.109.172','2005-07-12 08:34:17','2005-07-12 15:34:17','Haha... But I read it!  And I\'m a good audience member - I comment. :)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.7) Gecko/20050414 Firefox/1.0.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(22,31,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-12 12:31:23','2005-07-12 19:31:23','It\'s true! Comments are what I miss most about livejournal.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(23,54,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','69.3.70.43','2005-07-22 23:50:20','2005-07-23 06:50:20','holy crap, i think i might be able to take credit for that!',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(24,50,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','69.3.70.43','2005-07-22 23:54:56','2005-07-23 06:54:56','\"tiger\" sounds like a really horrible cologne? i think it\'s somewhat reminiscent of that word associated with a large feline with stripes.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.9) Gecko/20050711 Firefox/1.0.5','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(25,54,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-23 02:36:05','2005-07-23 09:36:05','You rock! You don\'t work for me, so it\'s not illegal!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.10) Gecko/20050716 Firefox/1.0.6','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(26,50,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-23 18:36:13','2005-07-24 01:36:13','but as a product?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.10) Gecko/20050716 Firefox/1.0.6','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(27,35,'Jason-Preston.com &raquo; Google Homepage','','http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=60','216.119.127.83','2005-07-25 21:21:41','2005-07-26 04:21:41','[...] Remember when I posted about howcustomized Google was better than My Yahoo!? I had one real complaint about how the Google homepage was set up, and my prayers have been answered. [...]',0,'1','The Incutio XML-RPC PHP Library -- WordPress/1.5.1.3','pingback',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(28,61,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','66.167.252.175','2005-07-26 07:40:33','2005-07-26 14:40:33','Spoiler!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.9) Gecko/20050711 Firefox/1.0.5','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(31,64,'Robert R. Fox','rrfox@arclight.net','','12.104.153.15','2005-07-27 11:01:39','2005-07-27 18:01:39','And what would you name an OS?  Rock? Paper? Elephant?  Please post an interesting alternative.  Any way, Tiger is just a memorable label.  The REAL official name is \"Mac OS X version 10.4\".  Look under the menu item \"About This Mac\" no mention of Tiger anywhere.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/412.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/412.2','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(32,64,'tommyboy','tommyboy@mailinator.com','','67.171.175.74','2005-07-27 11:10:27','2005-07-27 18:10:27','I dissagree.  I don\'t see how naming a the operating system after cats is \"posh\" or euphemistic.  Its just a branding/marketing choice that is no different than Ford naming their cars with \"f\" names: Focus, Fairlane, Fiesta, etc.  or, say, horse names: mustang, maverick, pinto.  What\'s the big deal?  I see no pretentiousness in the cat names.  They are nice names. Fun names.  And besides, if I remember correctly, these were just internal project names that were not orignally intended to be product names.  But because Jaguar was so well received in discussions before its release, Apple decided to stick with the name.  In contrast, the name Longhorn apparently did sit so well with the public.  Anyway, if you read this \"poshness\" into the cat names and find them annoying, I think its just your head/your attitude, something that you are projecting onto the names.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/412.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/412.2','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(30,61,'adlin.com &raquo; Blog Archive &raquo; Proof That I&#8217;m Psychic, Kinda','','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com/?p=23','72.10.58.3','2005-07-26 08:33:26','2005-07-26 15:33:26','[...] After reading Jason Preston&#8217;s post about Steve Jobs&#8217; Stanford commencement speech, I got to thinking about some of the many cool things that Apple has done. I thought about Mac&#8217;s early role in the history of personal computing, about my Apple-dominated childhood (Oregon Trail, anyone?), about my insatiable desire to be one of the cool kids and own my very own iPod. I caught myself drooling over Apple&#8217;s impeccable design sense. I realized how much progress there&#8217;s been since the days of boot-disks. [...]',0,'1','The Incutio XML-RPC PHP Library -- WordPress/1.5.1.2','pingback',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(33,64,'Van Secrist','vans@mac.com','','24.55.29.197','2005-07-27 11:13:10','2005-07-27 18:13:10','Hey Jason, I enjoyed reading your viewpoint. Though, I think you might be mistaken about the use of the word euphemistic. Dictionary.com says this:\r\n\r\neuphemistic\r\n\r\nadj : of an inoffensive substitute for offensive terminology; \"`peepee\' is a common euphemistic term\" [syn: inoffensive] [ant: dysphemistic]\r\n\r\nPerhaps a better way to phrase it might be \"Apple has a tendency for hyperbole.\" Or Apple is so pretentious.\r\n\r\nNow, to your naming point, is Apple really any different than any other company? A quick look at car model names makes my point: Jaguar, Thunderbird, Cougar, etc. Apple needs a name for their operating system that doesn\'t elicit a yawn, but rather, excitement. \"Mac OS X 10.4\" is about as exciting as a license plate. As you stated, the cat names are used to embue their characteristics on the OS. I might agree with you if they named it \"the Ultimate OS\" or some such nonsense. This, of course, is ridiculous as it doesn\'t allow room for growth. Perhaps some of Apple\'s other actions are coloring your perceptions.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/312.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/312','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(34,64,'David','seattleda@yahoo.com','','204.147.223.1','2005-07-27 11:18:39','2005-07-27 18:18:39','Tiger\'s official name is MacOS 10.4.  Tiger is just the nick name.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.0; en-US; rv:1.7.8) Gecko/20050511 Firefox/1.0.4','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(35,64,'M','m@dotcom.com','','70.71.1.182','2005-07-27 13:59:51','2005-07-27 20:59:51','I believe the \'marketing names\' are to help distinguish between \'versions\' of Mac OS X. \r\n\r\nA single point upgrade in Classic Mac OS wouldn\'t warrant $129. Who would pay to upgrade from 8.5 to 8.6?\r\n\r\nPerhaps if the product were Mac OSX v1.0 - 1.1 thru to 4.0 - 4.x that would seem easier to reconcile. But, it would be more difficult for Apple to market.\r\n\r\nRemember, the underlining core OS kernal hasn\'t changed much since 10.0 (aka OSX 1.0 ;-), only \'really cool\' features have been added or upgraded.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en-us) AppleWebKit/312.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/312','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(36,64,'popemark','popemark@mac.com','http://homepage.mac.com/popemark/iblog/index.html','17.102.123.54','2005-07-27 15:45:48','2005-07-27 22:45:48','M, I take issue with your assertion that \"the underlying core kernal [sic] hasn\'t changed much since 10.0.\" Take, for example, John Siracusa\'s description:\r\n\"The Mac OS X kernel has undergone some very significant changes in Tiger.\" <a href=\"http://arstechnica.com/reviews/os/macosx-10.4.ars/4\" rel=\"nofollow\"> Link to Ars Technica </a>',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/412.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/412.2','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(37,64,'M','m@dotcom.com','','70.71.1.182','2005-07-27 16:13:50','2005-07-27 23:13:50','popemark,\r\n\r\nMy bad. Thanks for the link. \r\n\r\nIn my own feeble way, I was attempting to illustrate the marketing reasons Apple would likely have added \'names\' to the version numbers of OSX. \r\n\r\nBeing the dilitant that I am, I should have left the technical aspect (kernel) out - as it likely wasn\'t necessary to make my point.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en-us) AppleWebKit/312.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/312','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(38,64,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-27 16:52:45','2005-07-27 23:52:45','Very cool points, all around. I think my response is big enough for a post, so that\'s going up in a few minutes. \r\n\r\n - Jason',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.10) Gecko/20050716 Firefox/1.0.6','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(39,64,'Jason-Preston.com &raquo; Follow-up on OS names','','http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=66','216.119.127.83','2005-07-27 17:15:09','2005-07-28 00:15:09','[...] I seem to have struck a chord with my post on Apple&#8217;s image, and I got a lot of really good points in the comments that I hadn&#8217;t really thought about. I&#8217;m gonna go ahead and bring those to the front page. [...]',0,'1','The Incutio XML-RPC PHP Library -- WordPress/1.5.1.3','pingback',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(40,66,'Ben','adlin.com@gmail.com','http://www.pixelumbrella.com/adlin.com','66.167.252.22','2005-07-28 03:00:43','2005-07-28 10:00:43','Jason, I don\'t mean to be too blunt about this, but I think you\'ve gotten to the point where you\'re just being whiny. You\'re being nitpicky about so much stuff that, really, doesn\'t warrant such a full frontal assault.\r\n\r\nRe: \"Designer brand\"\r\nOf course it\'s the designer brand of computers. But comparing it to Armani and Gucci doesn\'t really work -- there are occasions for which designer clothing brands are appropriate, and they sell well because they\'re both fashionable <em>and</em> well made. For example, I happen to know you wear Rainbow sandals. Why? They cost way more than a pair of Old Navy flip-flops. But they\'re made well and last forever. Trendy? Sure. But do they pull their weight? Absolutely. What would you have them do? Keep a top-notch OS and just start designing ugly computers? I think I know you well enough to know that you understand how important image can be.\r\n\r\nRe: \"Image-centric\"\r\nSure, Apple is image-centric. But at the same time, they\'re performance-centric and stability-centric and ease-of-use-centric. If you\'ve got those bases covered, why not make something that\'s purty, too?\r\n\r\nRe: \"Mac OS X: Dashboard\"\r\nSo you\'re suggesting they pick one (of many) new feature and make that the <em>entire</em> title&gt;?! That\'s like remodeling your entire kitchen and calling it, \"The Preston Kitchen: New Subzero.\" While Dashboard is certainly an important new feature in Tiger (oooh! I said it!), naming the entire OS after that one feature doesn\'t really showcase the many areas in which Tiger\'s improved upon things (assuming, of course, you agree Tiger improved on things, aside from adding Dashboard).\r\n\r\nYou\'re a very no-nonsense person, I think. You\'re not a big fan of flashiness or show or anything else. You\'re a meat-and-potatoes-with-white-bread guy. You like things simple, clean, and free of frill. While, in my opinion, this is reason enough for you to indeed <em>like</em> Apple (have you seen how simple their style is?), you\'ve classified their style as \"shallow\" and \"artsy,\" thereby making it anti-you. Nevertheless, understand that some people <em>like</em> things to be easier and more stylish, even if it means paying more money. Others appreciate Apple\'s stability or clean bill of virus-health. I guess my point is this: you can rant about Apple\'s names or design or anything all you want, but you\'re not going to change the fact that Macs are better choices for some people.\r\n\r\nConsider the soapbox stepped off of. And yes, a preposition is what I ended that sentence with.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.10) Gecko/20050716 Firefox/1.0.6','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(41,66,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-28 12:11:51','2005-07-28 19:11:51','<b>I have never once said that it is a bad choice to purchase or use a Mac, nor am I going to.</b><br /><br />\r\n.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI have not even said that other people should not prefer to use Macs, or (I don\'t think) ever said that anyone is actually *wrong* to prefer them. Please understand that all I am doing is trying to explain why <i>I</i> find new OS names annoying (yes, Vista is crap too). <br /><br />\r\n.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI think that, if anything, I\'ve steadily grown to dislike macs throughout this summer simply because every time the topic comes up, someone says:<br /><br />\r\n \"Jason, you hate macs. How come you don\'t recognize their \'easier and more stylish\' interface and the fact that every one of them is the most powerful computer in the world?\"<br /><br />\r\n.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe way computers are today, the largest difference between brands is product support. Most computers will do most things you\'d want them to, so picking what you use is essentially a matter of preference. <br /><br />\r\n.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIn fact, I think I might just close the subject, because one of the things that\'s most annoying to me is when other people tell me that my <i>preference</i> is wrong. And the more I hear, the more I hate.<br /><br />\r\n\r\n',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.10) Gecko/20050716 Firefox/1.0.6','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(44,68,'The Ferrett','iamferrettsannoyance@yahoo.com','','67.86.67.231','2005-07-29 06:24:41','2005-07-29 13:24:41','I, on the other hand, will lord it over Derek.  \r\n\r\n- The Ferrett\r\n\r\nP.S. - I don\'t see myself as a techie blog, but it\'s good to see that someone thinks that.  Try Eric Meyer at meyerweb.com for an example of a TECHIE techie blog.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.10) Gecko/20050716 Firefox/1.0.6','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(42,68,'Derek','dsteer@oxy.edu','http://showerman.blogspot.com','65.113.35.193','2005-07-28 16:53:29','2005-07-28 23:53:29','Fuck you for not liking my blog the most. You are a tasteless snob.\r\n\r\n-Derek',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(43,68,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2005-07-28 19:03:38','2005-07-29 02:03:38','The invention of the \"your blog\" joke:\r\n\r\nYour blog is a tasteless snob!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.10) Gecko/20050716 Firefox/1.0.6','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
