	(215,343,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','139.184.30.18','2005-12-10 09:27:07','2005-12-10 16:27:07','I think that Winamp actually has some plugins that will let you do that, and I imagine there\'s software to help do that otherwise. Problem is that I like iTunes best as a media player, and the things I\'ve tried tend to screw up the iPod/iTunes duality. \r\n\r\nJust for the record, I did not comment and then answer my own question. But I am really curious about how that happened. And who it really is.',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.0; .NET CLR 1.1.4322)','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
