	(335,400,'p.s. shes into some hard kinky shit','jra6@pitt.edu','','130.49.190.14','2006-01-15 17:56:04','2006-01-16 00:56:04','From what I can remember, you were always a snob....\n\nTherefore lets do some math...\n\nJason Preston   Foreign Countries = Unequivocal Snob  (Your formula)\n\nAlgebra two has taught me...\n\nJason Preston  = Unequivocal Snob - Foreign Countries\n\nSince you mainly were in the UK...we can do some substitution\n\nJason Preston = Unequivocal Snob - Foreign U.K.\n\nSince I am lazy we are going to switch to shorthand also, AND lets substiture bill cosby in for Unequivocal because he is an unequivocal genius \n\nTherefore,  Jason Preston = (Bill Cosby) (S) - (F)(U)(K)\n\nDo some crazy ass calculus and we end up with....\n\nJason Prestons Fuks Bill Cosby =  0 face',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.5) Gecko/20051012 Netscape/8.0.4','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(336,400,'p.s. shes into some hard kinky shit','jra6@pitt.edu','','130.49.190.14','2006-01-15 17:57:52','2006-01-16 00:57:52','From what I can remember, you were always a snob....\n\nTherefore lets do some math...\n\nAnd the plus sign doesnt work on your page for some reason...\n\nJason Preston PLUS Foreign Countries = Unequivocal Snob  (Your formula)\n\nAlgebra two has taught me...\n\nJason Preston  = Unequivocal Snob - Foreign Countries\n\nSince you mainly were in the UK...we can do some substitution\n\nJason Preston = Unequivocal Snob - Foreign U.K.\n\nSince I am lazy we are going to switch to shorthand also, AND lets substiture bill cosby in for Unequivocal because he is an unequivocal genius \n\nTherefore,  Jason Preston = (Bill Cosby) (S) - (F)(U)(K)\n\nDo some crazy ass calculus and we end up with....\n\nJason Prestons PLUS Fuks PLUS Bill Cosby =  0 face',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.5) Gecko/20051012 Netscape/8.0.4','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(337,400,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','','24.17.244.93','2006-01-15 23:48:33','2006-01-16 06:48:33','I\'m so amazed that you managed to both do calculus and post the same thing twice all in the same day. That\'s being an idiot savant?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.12) Gecko/20050915 Firefox/1.0.7 (ax)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(338,400,'Colin','czepeda@iwu.edu','http://colinzepeda.wordpress.com','198.178.132.253','2006-01-16 12:02:51','2006-01-16 19:02:51','Spicier there? You\'re kidding, right? Aside from the odd vindaloo action, NOTHING in the UK is spicier!\n\nAlso, I almost ordered chips at a hot dog place once. And I am now a self-affirmed expert on Europe. Try me.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8) Gecko/20051111 Firefox/1.5','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(339,400,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-01-16 15:04:54','2006-01-16 22:04:54','I totally meant \"there\" to literally mean \"somewhere not here\" -- not the UK in particular. \n\nFor example, \"Japan,\" \"Russia,\" and \"Nepal\" are all examples of \"there\" in this usage.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8) Gecko/20051111 Firefox/1.5','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
