	(531,504,'JÃ³nas','jonasmalinowski@gmail.com','http://sverigepojke.blogspot.com','130.208.131.158','2006-03-03 22:58:57','2006-03-04 05:58:57','perhaps that is the way of the world. Big, evil corporations.  \n\nHave you seen the documentary Corporation?  It tells you all about evil. You should check it out, that is if you are against evil corporations, like starbucks for example.  \"We proudly support Africa\" the banner said at the Starbucks in Borders, Brighton.  Now how in the world does a company support a whole continent? Are they maybe trying to be all gracious and giving money to starving children, which is all good, but pretty hipoctitical when they aren\'t paying the farmers who grow the coffee beans for their work.  \n\nYup, evil corporations are everywhere. Be aware!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; is-is) AppleWebKit/417.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/417.8','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(537,499,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','134.69.172.139','2006-03-04 14:44:56','2006-03-04 21:44:56','Unfortunately that app is only for OS X. I have heard of a winamp plugin but I don\'t think it works very well. \n\nI <em>have</em> however, heard of people having success with <a href=\"http://www.engadget.com/2004/11/02/how-to-get-music-off-your-ipod/\" rel=\"nofollow\">this method</a> over at engadget.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.1) Gecko/20060111 Firefox/1.5.0.1','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
