	(603,523,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','24.193.235.253','2006-03-15 18:11:03','2006-03-16 01:11:03','\"Changing\" the permalinks doesn\'t invalidate the old number based links. I changed about six months into blogging and nothing broke. All it does is add redirects to your .htaccess file and start using the nice links internally.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.11.4-21.10-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.0 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(604,523,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','71.121.97.104','2006-03-15 23:26:55','2006-03-16 06:26:55','Oh! Good to know.\n\nNow I need to root through the Codex and figure out how to change it ;)\n\nThanks.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.1) Gecko/20060111 Firefox/1.5.0.1','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(605,523,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','24.193.235.253','2006-03-16 04:53:29','2006-03-16 11:53:29','If your .htaccess file is not available for writing, the Permalinks section of the admin panel will provide you with the text for cutting and pasting. I went with the defaults it offered and have been quite happy.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.11.4-21.10-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.0 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(606,523,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','71.121.97.104','2006-03-16 19:05:39','2006-03-17 02:05:39','Clearly I\'m not understanding something. Whenever I try to use one of the options in the permalinks folder it destroys all my links to individual posts. \r\n\r\nI\'m assuming this means something is going on with the .htaccess file, but I can\'t seem to find that on my server, let alone modify it to make it work. I suppose if I could find it I could set 777 (isn\'t that full read/write?) permission for it...\r\n\r\nI\'ll get to the bottom of this!',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 7.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1; Maxthon; .NET CLR 1.1.4322)','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
