	(779,607,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','24.193.235.253','2006-05-02 05:35:25','2006-05-02 12:35:25','I once mailed an envelope to the US from Germany with a US address in the same city as the return address and no postage. By the time it reached the destination city, they went ahead a delivered it to the recipient.\r\n\r\nWho wondered why I\'d mailed him an empty envelope.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.11.4-21.11-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.0 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(782,607,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','134.69.232.23','2006-05-02 14:21:16','2006-05-02 21:21:16','I love that they wouldn\'t check for the postage until after it made it across the sea...it can\'t possibly have looked like it came from the return addres. \n\nHooray mail.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.2) Gecko/20060308 Firefox/1.5.0.2','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
