	(2815,670,'Svein KÃ¥re','skgunnarson@gmail.com','http://dionaea.com/blog','83.108.72.10','2006-06-06 04:14:04','2006-06-06 11:14:04','Your problem with refresh is easily solved: In preferences, click Advances -&gt; History, and set \'Check documents\' to \'Always\'\r\n\r\nLinks for new windows to open in tabs: See if (in preferences -&gt; Advanced -&gt; Tabs) the option is checked for \'Open windows instead of tabs\' - it shouldn\'t be by default.\r\n\r\nIn the advanced section you can also change the shortcuts/hotkeys to suit you. :)',0,'1','Opera/8.54 (Windows NT 5.1; U; nn)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(2829,670,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-06-06 15:36:01','2006-06-06 22:36:01','Refresh solution and tabs issue worked like a charm! Thank you --\r\n\r\nI tried changing the shortcuts, but I can\'t figure out what I\'ve done wrong (it doesn\'t work yet) - \r\n\r\nI changed the value:\r\n\r\nshift ctrl enter     Go\r\n\r\nto\r\n\r\nctrl enter            Go\r\n\r\nSince I want ctrl click to open the link in a new background tab (a la firefox) - but I just typed it in. Is there another way I\'m supposed to do that?\r\n\r\nIf you don\'t know, no worries ;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1; U; en) Opera 9.00','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(2833,670,'Svein KÃ¥re','skgunnarson@gmail.com','http://dionaea.com/blog','83.108.181.113','2006-06-06 17:19:03','2006-06-07 00:19:03','I haven\'t really looked into changing the hotkeys myself, so I can\'t tell you how to do it. However, if you ask at the forums at my.opera.com, I\'m sure there are someone there who knows - there are many there who really know how to tweak Opera.\r\n\r\nGood luck. :)',0,'1','Opera/8.54 (Windows NT 5.1; U; nn)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(3174,708,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-06-26 16:14:16','2006-06-26 23:14:16','schwing!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060508 Firefox/1.5.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(2937,687,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','24.193.235.253','2006-06-16 02:57:08','2006-06-16 09:57:08','Make sure you know what sort of lamp life you can expect and how much replacement lamps are going to be. They\'re usually several hundred dollars.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.13-4-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.2 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(2946,687,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-06-16 12:20:10','2006-06-16 19:20:10','Yeah, I looked at those. The lamps cost around $400 and the life on the 7800 model is only around 3,000 hours (I say only, but, is that good? I don\'t know). \n\nIn any case, I think I\'m going to check out some retailers where I\'d be able to see the projector before I drop that much cash. I actually prefer a legitimate TV to a projector, but there\'s no way I can travel with one. \n\nI think that when I buy this thing I\'ll resell it when the bulb dies.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060508 Firefox/1.5.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
