	(3306,728,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-07-03 18:37:49','2006-07-04 01:37:49','Hahaha you guys rock. \n\nIt\'s just frustrating to switch computers mid-post, ya know? ;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060508 Firefox/1.5.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(3386,734,'Josh','josh@joshourisman.com','http://www.joshourisman.com','72.18.249.233','2006-07-07 14:02:58','2006-07-07 21:02:58','Wow, at first I thought you were talking about their Hybrid SUV. I had assumed that when the sedan one came out it would be more in line with other car hybrids. But wow, that\'s just crazy. My _Camaro_ gets 28 MPG.\n\nDamn, I had big hopes for this car, a good luxury hybrid could do a lot to bring hybrids even more into the mainstream. Give a few away to some musicians and get them in music videos and you\'ve got an instant hit (of course you\'d have to offer a budget version too...).\n\nAlthough were I to get a Lexus, I\'d definitely go with the 450h.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(3415,734,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-07-09 13:00:08','2006-07-09 20:00:08','Yeah, my parents actually drive one of those - it works really well and we haven\'t had any problems with it so far. \n\nIronically, the 450h gets better mileage than my Civic (well, in the City - I still beat them on the highway).',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060508 Firefox/1.5.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(3431,738,'Teresa Valdez Klein','teresa@blogbusinesssummit.com','http://www.blogbusinesssummit.com','71.102.97.242','2006-07-10 15:58:09','2006-07-10 22:58:09','Hi Jason,\r\n  Actually, having two copies of your content out there on the Web confuses and pisses off the search engines and results in overall lower PageRank, or <a href=\"http://inflighthq.com/archives/2005/11/who_moved_my_sk.htm\" rel=\"nofollow\">so I\'ve read</a>.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) NetNewsWire/2.0.1','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(3434,738,'Jason','xwing@seanet.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-07-10 19:05:30','2006-07-11 02:05:30','Even if it\'s just a 100 words and a link? I should look into this... (thanks)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060508 Firefox/1.5.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(3489,747,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','24.193.235.253','2006-07-16 06:00:21','2006-07-16 13:00:21','You hate it, yet it\'s quite good? Color me confused!\n\nOh.. do you mean you hate Hamlet the character? Then it can\'t be too good. When portrayed well, Hamlet should be quite sympathetic. Tell me, is (was) it funny? I consider Hamlet to be one of the finest dark comedies ever written.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.13-4-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.2 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(3490,747,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','209.91.62.197','2006-07-16 09:27:01','2006-07-16 16:27:01','My fault: the play is called <a href=\"http://www.shakespearefest.org/I Hate Hamlet.htm\" rel=\"nofollow\">I Hate Hamlet</a>\n\nAnd for reference, Hamlet is one of my favorite plays - along with Death of a Salesman and Rosencranz and Gildenstern are dead (I guess I\'m a bit morbid with my taste, huh?)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060508 Firefox/1.5.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(3503,752,'Jeremy','jziskind@ucla.edu','','165.235.122.19','2006-07-18 16:06:52','2006-07-18 23:06:52','I can\'t comment on Adelphia\'s ball suckage, but I did subscribe to DirecTV over the past year. $42 a month split amongst four of us wasn\'t terrible, but I personally only watch maybe 5-6 channels out of all the crap they have, and when I would find an interesting sounding show it wouldn\'t be available under the basic cable plan I chose. I think your best bet would be to download the episodes of your favorite shows off the internet. Our friend that lived down the hall was basically the downloading Jesus.',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.0; .NET CLR 1.1.4322)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(3505,750,'Niero','mrdestructoid@gmail.com','http://www.destructoid.com','67.35.67.181','2006-07-18 18:19:56','2006-07-19 01:19:56','Thanks for spreading the word about the contest man, really appreciate it.  Like it says on the site, we\'re dying to get on the map and aren\'t beneath bribing people!!!!\n\nIts been expensive and only 1/1022 people that come to that page actually sign up (I attribute this to all the bullsh1t contests out there where you have to sign up for a credit card, etc - people are cynical) but its still the only kind of marketing I can afford.  When I have $14,000 month to spend on full page ads on EGM I wanna do that too, but for now buying a DS for some guy I\'ve never met every month is the only thing my disposable income can bare :)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060508 Firefox/1.5.0.4','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
