	(3596,706,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','66.167.136.82','2006-07-22 22:54:53','2006-07-23 05:54:53','Given your tendency to market-analyze <em>everything</em>, I think this is an absurdly superficial exploration of why Apple users enjoy talking about the computers they use. People who talk about their Macs aren\'t just part of a massive marketing conspiracy, they\'re just people who have a passion for products that are simple, elegant, and get the job done. It\'s admittedly a bit cultish, but that shouldn\'t detract from the reason <em>why</em> it\'s garnered so much support from consumers.\n\nThink about your favorite sweatshirt, Jason. It\'s a red hooded sweatshirt with a gigantic Nintendo logo on the front. Do you wear it because you\'re hoping that by showing your support, you\'ll move others to buy Nintendo products? Are you just a pawn in some big consumer-driven advertising ploy? Or do you wear it simply because you think it\'s an innovative, creative company that makes some pretty sweet-ass products?\n\nIf you had fans of Flicker posting your arrow logo all over, I feel like you\'d be really proud that you created a product that drove people to spread the word. While you\'d probably be stoked that the support would lead to more traffic, I think you might also feel the pride that comes with creating something that others <em>want</em> to tell their friends about.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(3601,414,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','66.167.136.82','2006-07-23 03:50:17','2006-07-23 10:50:17','Not long until you and I sit down for a cup of tea... <em>in England</em>.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
