	(4292,809,'Ethan','eambabo@gmail.com','http://www.rabidspacedog.com','75.38.109.161','2006-09-10 22:34:12','2006-09-11 05:34:12','Ahab! Ahab! Ahab!\n\nI could just tell you this by walking four feet to the living room, but it\'s fun this way too. \n\n(Thanks for HD goodness)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X Mach-O; en-US; rv:1.8.0.6) Gecko/20060728 Firefox/1.5.0.6','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(4297,809,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.38.109.161','2006-09-11 10:00:49','2006-09-11 17:00:49','Haha! Looks like I\'m going to try setting up a copy of BeyondTV - see if I can\'t get the program guide working.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.6) Gecko/20060728 Firefox/1.5.0.6','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(4402,823,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-09-20 07:45:02','2006-09-20 14:45:02','whoa there, cynical critic.\n\n1 - it\'s still as closed as you want it to be. sure, people can get accounts without going to a .edu institution, but it doesn\'t mean strangers can do anything but find out you have a profile.\n\n2 - this isn\'t really a problem with facebook, it\'s a problem with you graduating. after that point, it\'ll be a way to keep in touch with people; \"holy shit, bob\'s in japan?\" also, arguably, having it \"open\" will allow you to add friends that you know from <em>outside</em> of school, say, those that you meet while living in l.a. or seattle.\n\ni\'m not smitten with facebook, but i feel like there was a little clarification needed.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(4403,821,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-09-20 07:48:07','2006-09-20 14:48:07','walking shark? that\'s not news!! haven\'t you ever seen <em>sherman\'s lagoon</em>?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(4404,823,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.42.96','2006-09-20 09:33:13','2006-09-20 16:33:13','re 1: It\'s annoying to me that there are people at my own school whose profiles I can\'t see - that\'s not keeping the network closed, that\'s eliminating the point of facebook because they\'ve changed it so that <a href=\"http://www.forbes.com/digitalentertainment/2006/09/11/facebook-opens-up-cx_rr_0911facebook.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">everyone can get in</a>. \n\nre 2: I see your point, and I understand it, but on a practical level I never use facebook except to double-check someone\'s name.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(4415,823,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-09-21 02:27:59','2006-09-21 09:27:59','re: re: 1: okay, you\'re saying two different things. are you angry that you can\'t see profiles of people at your own school? that\'s because they have been given the option to hide their profiles from people they\'re not yet friends with (which i think is a good option to have). just add them as a friend. or, on the other hand, are you angry that they\'re allowing everyone in? in this case, i feel like your frustration is also misplaced â€“ this is the feature that will actually allow you to facebook friends who don\'t go to a .edu institution (which may solve your problem in #2). it\'s not like those creepsters will be able to look at your profile at all unless <em>you</em> say it\'s okay.\n\ni agree it\'s lost some of the coolness factorâ€”\"oh, sorry, it\'s only for college students,\"â€”but i don\'t see how this is leading facebook to \"crapland.\"\n\nand personally, i\'m in favor of being able to quickly contact people who might have changed their phone numbers or addresses or emails after graduating. calling it \"an unfortunate yearbook where people get uglier all the time so you canâ€™t pretend people never change\" seems like you\'re pining over headshots of hotties (which, although probably quite popular with facebook, isn\'t exactly what it was designed for).',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(4418,823,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.42.96','2006-09-21 10:03:37','2006-09-21 17:03:37','Meh. We have different opinions, and clearly use facebook for different things.\n\nI think it\'s turning into Myspace, and I hate Myspace.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(4440,825,'Jeremy','jziskind@gmail.com','','67.155.138.170','2006-09-25 07:00:13','2006-09-25 14:00:13','My e-mail is quite fast, easy-to-use, and reliable. It might be time to switch who you\'re using.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.0; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(4441,825,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.42.96','2006-09-25 09:45:58','2006-09-25 16:45:58','Who i\'m using is gmail, oxy, and jason-preston.com. \n\nOxy is the least reliable of all, because their mail system goes down like once every ten minutes. \n\nGmail is pretty good, but I still run into problems occasionally. \n\nJason-Preston.com works excellently except that most places assume my e-mail is spam because it\'s not a big-time mailserver. \n\nHaving shitloads and shitloads of spam floating around the internet has made it really expensive to run a mail service effectively (block spam, let the real mail through).',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(4577,845,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','24.193.235.253','2006-10-04 13:47:32','2006-10-04 20:47:32','Those assholes.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.21-0.13-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.2 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(4807,848,'Hillary','hillary.a.preston@dartmouth.edu','','129.170.202.3','2006-10-09 18:32:54','2006-10-10 01:32:54','Funny, I had an incredibly UNproductive Sunday.  I basically sat on my butt all day and napped/ate.  I\'m glad at least one other person got a good amount of things done.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5423,840,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-10-14 10:50:04','2006-10-14 17:50:04','3.  Makes me actively search for a better alternative.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5460,853,'Hannah','hbyrd@uvm.edu','','69.160.169.152','2006-10-16 20:17:28','2006-10-17 03:17:28','Dearest Love,\n\nThings could be worse.  This weekend a friend of mine microwaved another friend\'s brand new chocolate phone while under the influence of alcohol.  This same friend proceeded to pass out and piss in a bed that was not her own.  She was asked not to return.\n\nWhenever you are telephonically reconnected, you should give me a call so I can hear the sweet dulcet tones of your voice.\n\nLove,\nHannah',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5483,853,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-10-17 10:13:13','2006-10-17 17:13:13','Dude, you\'re getting love-letter comments. Please chill about the phone. :)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5484,853,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.38.110.31','2006-10-17 11:04:31','2006-10-17 18:04:31','Hannah rocks so hard',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(5487,854,'Josh','josh@joshourisman.com','http://www.joshourisman.com','66.30.27.222','2006-10-17 13:46:50','2006-10-17 20:46:50','For a second I thought you were talking about Douglas Adams, and so was going to recommend a recent biography of him by Neil Gaiman, because in it there\'s a quote from Douglas Adams that just might reveal what his magic chicken nugget of humor was. Unfortunately I only read half the book while sitting around in a Border\'s one day and keep forgetting to go back and actually buy the book so I can finish it.\n\nActually, I still recommend it, it\'s this one: http://www.amazon.com/Dont-Panic-Douglas-Hitchhikers-Galaxy/dp/1840237422/sr=8-3/qid=1161117029/ref=pd_bbs_sr_3/104-6428137-0553528?ie=UTF8',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5489,856,'Josh','josh@joshourisman.com','http://www.joshourisman.com','66.30.27.222','2006-10-17 18:22:20','2006-10-18 01:22:20','It\'s nice to imagine that such an invent would inspire humanity to come together. In reality, I suspect, it would cause massive global war as the various countries fight over who \'owns\' the aliens. Hopefully they don\'t have the technology to just vaporize us all from space. Cause that\'s what I\'d do if I were them....\n\nAlso, we know of over 200 extra-solar planets: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extra-solar_planets',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N');
