	(5493,856,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.38.110.31','2006-10-18 01:13:25','2006-10-18 08:13:25','Apparently I ought to do more fact-checking on wikipedia...\n\n;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(5511,341,'Sal','sal@yahoo.com','','69.229.110.137','2006-10-19 00:30:37','2006-10-19 07:30:37','Just got season 3 on DVD!!! \r\n\r\nGREATEST SHOW EVER!!!!!!!!!',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5512,341,'Sal','sal@yahoo.com','','69.229.110.137','2006-10-19 00:31:53','2006-10-19 07:31:53','Any news on the life of this show???????????\r\n\r\nwhatevasl@yahoo.com',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5582,859,'Teresa Valdez Klein','teresa@blogbusinesssummit.com','http://www.blogbusinesssummit.com','71.112.112.231','2006-10-23 12:09:29','2006-10-23 19:09:29','Where there\'s a Wil, there\'s a way. Wil Wheaton, that is. He once <a href=\"http://wilwheaton.typepad.com/wwdnbackup/2006/09/apple_gave_me_b.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">lost all his iTunes files</a> and had them restored <i>gratis</i> by Apple. And that\'s not just because he used to be Wesley Crusher. Apparently, it\'s a standard practice for Apple.\r\n\r\nYou should try to find a woman named Kate who works with the iTunes store. She\'s the person who helped Wil.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) NetNewsWire/2.0.1','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5592,859,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.38.6.70','2006-10-23 18:57:13','2006-10-24 01:57:13','Cool, thanks for the link & tip. I found some sort of \"report a problem with a purchase\" thing on the support website. But it didn\'t seem to do anything and has since disappeared. \n\nI guess I\'ll try calling a physical apple store, since I can\'t find a number to call online anywhere.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(5608,861,'Teresa Valdez Klein','teresa@blogbusinesssummit.com','http://www.blogbusinesssummit.com','64.81.189.204','2006-10-24 22:59:25','2006-10-25 05:59:25','Oh...I thought you had tried that already. Otherwise I would have mentioned it. ;-)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) NetNewsWire/2.0.1','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5611,861,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','64.81.189.204','2006-10-25 08:19:28','2006-10-25 15:19:28','Yeah, no worries. I\'m really smart in some ways and exceptionally stupid in others.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X Mach-O; en-US; rv:1.8.0.5) Gecko/20060723 Firefox/1.5.0.5','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(5612,863,'Easton Ellsworth','easton@knowmoremedia.com','http://www.businessblogwire.com','68.98.96.128','2006-10-25 09:47:18','2006-10-25 16:47:18','I\'m jealous - hope you enjoy the conference.  If you see Tim Stay there, say hi - he\'s my boss at Know More Media :) - or also Diane Ensey, one of our authors.  Keep us all posted on what you get out of it.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5617,863,'Jeremy','jziskind@gmail.com','','67.155.138.170','2006-10-25 13:51:10','2006-10-25 20:51:10','Hey Jason, I\'m hoping Teresa\'s fiance Andy is joking on his latest blog entry when he writes about the Unlawful Internet Gaming Act. I\'m about 95% certain he is, but I just wanted to make sure since it\'s an issue I\'m very passionate about.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.0; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5621,863,'Teresa Valdez Klein','teresa@blogbusinesssummit.com','http://www.blogbusinesssummit.com','64.81.189.204','2006-10-25 15:35:16','2006-10-25 22:35:16','<strong>Jeremy:</strong> Andy is always joking.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5638,868,'Janet','janet@janetleejohnson.com','http://www.janetleejohnson.com','64.81.189.204','2006-10-26 11:38:22','2006-10-26 18:38:22','You did a fantastic job of capturing the points he so generously delivered.  Because of the two-laptops?  I want to know your system!',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1; .NET CLR 1.1.4322)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5640,868,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','64.81.189.204','2006-10-26 12:05:20','2006-10-26 19:05:20','It must be the two laptops. It lets me ignore one of them.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(5646,868,'Sparkplug 9 &gt;&gt; bizhack','','http://www.sparkplug9.com/bizhack/index.php/2006/10/26/calacanis-most-of-us-suck/','64.13.192.13','2006-10-26 18:58:23','2006-10-27 01:58:23','<strong>Calacanis: most of us suck</strong>\n\nQuick question: are you in the Technorati Top 100? If not, I hate to break the news, but you suck. If it makes you feel any better, I suck too.\nWhy?\nWell, according to Jason Calacanis&#8217; recent keynote at Blog Business Summit, if you don&#8217;t ra...',0,'1','WordPress/2.0.4','trackback',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5647,868,'John Koetsier','john@sparkplug9.com','http://sparkplug9.com/bizhack/','216.232.0.194','2006-10-26 19:00:16','2006-10-27 02:00:16','I like Calacanis - I think he\'s got guts, tries stuff, and succeeds or fails in interesting ways.\n\nBut I really don\'t think his comment around non-A-listers sucking was called for.\n\nI don\'t see anything in your post about that comment ... did you leave it out on purpose, or did you have a completely different take on it?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X Mach-O; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060929 Firefox/1.5.0.7 Flock/0.7.6','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5648,868,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','24.41.60.9','2006-10-26 22:18:17','2006-10-27 05:18:17','I heard it differently: Calacanis was saying two different things. \n\nFirst he was saying that there <em>are no</em> A-listers. That that whole \"A-list\" idea is a hangover from a medium other than blogging. \n\nThen he was saying that instead of an A-list, there are bloggers who are good, and bloggers who suck. If you\'re a good blogger, your blog will grow. If you\'re not, practice will make you better. \n\nI\'m not a great blogger, but I blog a lot, and over time - more people have found my blog. \n\nI have another theory on that, actually, but I\'m going to write that up in a few days. That\'s just my take on what Calacanis said.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.7) Gecko/20060909 Firefox/1.5.0.7','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(5668,874,'A quick How-To: Get your short numerical permalink from Wordpress at Jason-Preston.com','','http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/10/27/a-quick-how-to-get-your-short-numerical-permalink-from-wordpress/','216.119.127.83','2006-10-27 16:15:25','2006-10-27 23:15:25','[...] http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=874 [...]',0,'1','Incutio XML-RPC -- WordPress/2.0.2','pingback',0,0,NULL,'Y'),
	(5681,883,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','68.163.50.17','2006-10-29 04:15:01','2006-10-29 11:15:01','I call it tach-blogging (as in tachyon particles) and I use that feature a <em>lot</em>.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.21-0.25-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.5 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5688,888,'Taran','cnd@knowprose.com','http://www.knowprose.com','201.238.82.234','2006-10-29 13:57:01','2006-10-29 20:57:01','Good points, but it\'s a matter of how the presence is done. \n\nAnd as far as the operating system question: \nhttp://scobleizer.wordpress.com/2006/03/27/second-life-is-an-os/\n\nIt is lacking in certain regards, though.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.4) Gecko/20060516 SeaMonkey/1.0.2 Mnenhy/0.7.4.0','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5697,888,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.38.6.70','2006-10-29 20:31:38','2006-10-30 03:31:38','Apparently Scoble and I think alike ;)\n\nYes there are problems, but what if Linden Labs took it to the OS level in 10 years and one-upped MS for the desktop? That would be huge.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(5782,901,'Blog Business Summit','','http://blogbusinesssummit.com/2006/11/sharing_is_cari.htm','208.113.133.22','2006-11-02 13:28:49','2006-11-02 20:28:49','<strong>Sharing is Caring: Facebook Goes After Del.icio.us</strong>\n\nI couldn&#8217;t agree more with my colleague Jason Preston&#8217;s assessment that Facebook stands to take a big gust of wind out of Del.icio.us&#8217; sails with its&#8217; new â€œshareâ€ feature. I particularly like the feature because it allows us...',0,'1','MovableType/3.2','trackback',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5838,624,'Azzurra','Azzurra7519@yahoo.com','','195.225.176.13','2006-11-04 15:53:43','2006-11-04 22:53:43','Buon luogo, congratulazioni, il mio amico!',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1;SV1)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5879,907,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','68.236.44.160','2006-11-05 04:10:53','2006-11-05 11:10:53','\"And for a moment, why, I even touched the sky and at least I left some stories they could tell, I did!\"\n\nIf I know anything about you at all it\'s this: your experience with Flicker Gaming is going to be tossed around the rock tumbler of your brain until it shines with gemtastic beauty and is fit to be setting in your next work.\n\nI was sorry to see that Flicker Gaming would be shutting down. I look forward to seeing where you move on to from here.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.21-0.25-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.5 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(5896,907,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.34.54','2006-11-05 11:58:05','2006-11-05 18:58:05','Thanks a bunch buddy, it was great to have you along for most of the ride. \n\nBy the way, you get about a million points for the Nightmare quote ;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(6059,912,'Blog Business Summit','','http://blogbusinesssummit.com/2006/11/deleting_blog_p.htm','71.112.85.173','2006-11-07 14:51:31','2006-11-07 21:51:31','<strong>Deleting Blog Posts? Is it Ever OK?</strong>\n\n',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','trackback',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6165,911,'Morgan','morgan@geekstress.com','http://geekstress.com','68.65.195.85','2006-11-08 11:02:12','2006-11-08 18:02:12','In his defense Tony does call himself the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luddite\" title=\"Luddite on Wikipedia\" rel=\"nofollow\">Luddite</a>.  Most of his rants sit somewhere uncomfortably between a humanist and an anti technology crazy-pants.  Always good for getting a computer geek fired up.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.8) Gecko/20061025 Firefox/1.5.0.8','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6166,915,'Morgan','morgan@geekstress.com','http://geekstress.com','68.65.195.85','2006-11-08 11:08:12','2006-11-08 18:08:12','I\'ve yet to see any hard standard to value art stand up to more than one or two examples.  Its best to judge it one piece at a time.  And we can all argue and bicker and flame war about it.  More fun that way.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.8) Gecko/20061025 Firefox/1.5.0.8','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6167,915,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-11-08 11:22:13','2006-11-08 18:22:13','Lemme guess, this was a topic of discussion in a Fineman class?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6177,915,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.34.54','2006-11-08 14:54:37','2006-11-08 21:54:37','Morgan: I\'m totally with you - art is all over the place for everyone and sometimes it\'s just fun to get people mad about it. \n\nBen: Nope, just me trying to be like Scott Adams ;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(6178,911,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.34.54','2006-11-08 14:56:33','2006-11-08 21:56:33','I know, but, Luddite or not, it\'s a bit presumptuous to judge a graphic novel one hasn\'t read by nothing other than a general sense of the genre. \n\nAnd music...doesn\'t have to be MP3s or other technology - his point seems to be that people shouldn\'t have broad tastes?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(6228,917,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','68.236.44.160','2006-11-09 03:48:28','2006-11-09 10:48:28','Best. Sitcom. Ever.\n\nWell, since Soap.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.21-0.25-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.5 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6390,922,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','68.236.44.160','2006-11-10 12:37:59','2006-11-10 19:37:59','In the code, replace CCCCCC with FFFFFF and MMMM with 1106 and you\'re set!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.21-0.25-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.5 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6732,919,'Adam Levine','adam.levine@gamerandy.com','http://www.gamerandy.com','24.7.84.154','2006-11-15 12:15:00','2006-11-15 19:15:00','Come up with a good idea for a show, and I\'m in ;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.0.8) Gecko/20061025 Firefox/1.5.0.8','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6818,948,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-11-19 10:51:49','2006-11-19 17:51:49','Ethan\'s camping out? I love that guy.\n\nEnjoy your Wii. Can\'t wait to try it out come January!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6822,948,'Hillary','Hillary.A.Preston@Dartmouth.edu','','129.170.244.51','2006-11-19 15:42:25','2006-11-19 22:42:25','Sounds like Conrad got one last night too.  I\'m definitely going to be trying it out tomorrow when I get home.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(6831,950,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','68.236.44.160','2006-11-20 04:33:50','2006-11-20 11:33:50','It\'s a blast, isn\'t it? I think even the boxing will be good once I get the hang of it. Evidently fatigue is a concern, which explains why every punch doesn\'t register.\n\nAnyway, make sure you guys swing by MBB, grab and register my friend code!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Konqueror/3.5; Linux 2.6.16.21-0.25-smp; X11; i686; en_US) KHTML/3.5.5 (like Gecko)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(7005,953,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-11-21 05:32:59','2006-11-21 12:32:59','Does this mean you\'re in Bellevue for Thanksgiving?\n\nEnjoy some pumpkin pie (and play some Wii) for me.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(7021,954,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-11-21 19:17:55','2006-11-22 02:17:55','If it <em>were</em> Sunday, what would your Sunday post be this week?\n\nMaybe I have to wait until Sunday.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(7022,954,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.40.70','2006-11-21 19:31:13','2006-11-22 02:31:13','Yep, you have to wait until Sunday.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
