	(7443,991,'Conrad','Conrady82@gmail.com','http://www.Conrad-Preston.com','24.41.60.9','2006-12-07 19:01:02','2006-12-08 02:01:02','oh yeah that sucks, that happened to me when i had it on auto-update it just started erasing all my songs when i plugged it in, you have to put it on manual update and just highlight all your songs on your desktop with shift click stuff then drag them to your ipod in the itunes interface',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(7445,995,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','134.69.2.254','2006-12-07 19:32:16','2006-12-08 02:32:16','Fortunately, I haven\'t started working on mine yet since it\'s not due until April! \r\n\r\nWhen I do, however, I\'m pretty sure I\'m going to double-triple back it up on like thirteen DVDs and an abacus.',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET CLR 2.0.50727)','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(7447,995,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-12-07 20:16:09','2006-12-08 03:16:09','While I think the article\'s entertaining, I feel like he\'s inferring that the iPhone will be a \"failure\" simply because it won\'t enjoy the same overwhelming success that the iPod has. Doesn\'t Kanellos (the author) realize that Apple is used to being the minority? Even though most people use Windows, it\'s tough to argue that OSX has been a <em>failure</em>.\n\nRegarding design, I think he\'s especially off. Yeah, other mobile phone companies dump tons of money into design, but don\'t other computer companies do that, too? I hate to be a fanboy, but Apple has Johnathan Ive. And while Kanellos (the author of the article) doesn\'t seem to be impressed by that, it\'s hard to debate the fact that Apple takes the cake when it comes to trendsetting design.\n\nIn terms of quality, I\'m curious to see how the iPhone will do. Things could go either way. I\'ve had a number of fairly successful phones (hell, I even have a RAZR), and most of them have ended up tweaking out in not-so-acceptable ways. I imagine the iPhone will be <em>at least</em> that reliable.\n\nEither way, I\'m excited to see what it looks like. Also, if it plays really well with OSX applications, I might be tempted to fork over the doughâ€”actually, $250 is probably too much for me to spend on a phone (unless there are some serious T-Mobile rebates in the works).',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(7470,996,'Teresa Valdez Klein','tsv02001@alumni.pomona.edu','http://teresacentric.com','71.112.125.241','2006-12-08 14:43:35','2006-12-08 21:43:35','Yay! Finals are done.\n\nWhen do you come home? I want to hang! Let\'s go out and have some great drinks.\n\n-T',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en-US; rv:1.8.1) Gecko/20061010 Firefox/2.0','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(7599,999,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','82.215.29.193','2006-12-12 15:56:33','2006-12-12 22:56:33','Jesus Christ. I love my Mac, but are you kidding me? That argument is so embarrassing. I don\'t like <em>those</em> Mac users; they\'re giving the rest of us a bad name.\n\nThat said, I\'m all about having some Macs at Oxy (good company isn\'t the only reason I like being in the newspaper/publications room). And while, sadly, I couldn\'t agree with you more on reasons (1) and (4), but regarding (2), doesn\'t Apple offer some pretty beefy servers? (apple.com/server)\n\nBut yeah. (1) and (4). They\'re pretty compelling arguments you make.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/418.9.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
