	(19051,1141,'fester','ifester@gmail.com','','24.18.237.179','2007-03-02 21:28:14','2007-03-03 04:28:14','I think you have officially made me paranoid about my own blog.\n\nFor the record, we weren\'t blogging back when I was Burkdall\'s student, so I\'ve never formally deconstructed my - or anyone else\'s - blog.  I agree with you that a effective post title is important, but it depends on what you intend for the blog. For instance - I have a very insular blog on livejournal.  I have a specific list of people who regularly read my blog and whose blogs I read in turn.  In this case the post titles really don\'t matter.  I generally read the post regardless of the title. \n\nOn another topic - I agree, there should be a Mario button.  Only I think it should allow  a person to jump really high (IRL) whenever they push the button.  IMHO.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.7.5) Gecko/20041107 Firefox/1.0','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(19617,1146,'Sohail A. Rahim','sohail@lithiumrain.com','http://www.dinner2go.co.uk','84.9.113.158','2007-03-06 11:43:16','2007-03-06 18:43:16','lol. You\'re right.. He\'ll be turning it off quite soon I think.\r\n\r\nI\'ve got a few google alerts and they come in at least two or three a day.. and for some odd reason get filtered out to the junk folder no matter how much I\'ve tried to convince my email program that I really want to see them in my inbox.\r\n\r\nOn that note, can anyone recommend a good server-side (linux ideally) spam filter that doesn\'t chew up genuine mail? The amount of spam I\'ve been getting these past few months is really getting to a point where I want to go out there with a shotgun... ok, not really.. I just want a good filter :-p\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nSohail.\r\n\r\nWebmaster\r\nwww.dinner2go.co.uk',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1; .NET CLR 1.0.3705; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET CLR 2.0.50727)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
