	(28691,1184,'Hillary','hillary.a.preston@dartmouth.edu','','146.129.249.98','2007-04-09 09:45:36','2007-04-09 16:45:36','I tend to have epiphanies while I\'m involved in a conversation.  I\'ll be talking about something random that happens to trigger another thought and I\'ll get sidetracked.  Then I have to mention it or the thought goes away, and I end up seeming like a total space cadet...',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 7.0; Windows NT 5.2; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; InfoPath.1; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 1.0.3705)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(28699,1184,'phil','phil4d@mac.com','','198.174.97.16','2007-04-09 10:30:31','2007-04-09 17:30:31','Either driving or in the shower. I shower first thing in the morning so my brain is just coming up to speed... or, at least, idle... but frequently the back-burner subjects resolve themselves under running water.\n\n\n        phil',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/419 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(28992,1184,'Teresa','tsv02001@gmail.com','http://teresacentric.com','71.112.111.105','2007-04-10 08:59:57','2007-04-10 15:59:57','I\'m a car epiphanizer as well, but I don\'t write things down. This brain is like a steel trap.\n\nNow what were we talking about?',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en-US; rv:1.8.1.3) Gecko/20070309 Firefox/2.0.0.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(29016,1184,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.38.5','2007-04-10 11:56:38','2007-04-10 18:56:38','Haha the weird thing is that I remember the most random things, and forget the important ones.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en-US; rv:1.8.1.3) Gecko/20070309 Firefox/2.0.0.3','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(29251,1132,'Twitter re-visited at [Jason Preston]','','http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/04/11/twitter-re-visited/','216.119.127.83','2007-04-11 10:40:51','2007-04-11 17:40:51','[...] A month or so ago I posted that I didn&#8217;t really understand what all the fuss was about Twitter. I poked my head in to the question a little bit and then decided to leave it alone. [...]',0,'1','Incutio XML-RPC -- WordPress/2.1','pingback',0,0,NULL,'Y'),
	(29326,1192,'Michael Strickland','morigawa@gmail.com','http://www.540mbps.com/','67.142.130.34','2007-04-11 18:22:06','2007-04-12 01:22:06','I\'d have to agree. Plus, I feel like one of the appealing aspects of blogging and reading blogs is the anonymity associated with it. A lot of people have great things to add to the discussion who just don\'t want to sign their name.',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1; .NET CLR 1.0.3705; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; Media Center PC 4.0)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(29330,1192,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.22.38.5','2007-04-11 19:43:00','2007-04-12 02:43:00','I think part of this anonymity ethos is that the internet is still in many ways a new place for people, and privacy, especially in an age where identity theft is huge, is a big concern for many people. \n\nThat said, i don\'t think anyone should be able to harrass someone or post baseless accusations from a shield of cowardice. It\'s a fine line, and I think it\'s the responsibility of everyone who runs a blog to establish their own policy towards anonymity for their own site.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en-US; rv:1.8.1.3) Gecko/20070309 Firefox/2.0.0.3','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(29390,1195,'Corvus','manbytesblog@pjsattic.com','http://blog.pjsattic.com/corvus','67.93.219.138','2007-04-12 07:20:43','2007-04-12 14:20:43','The storytelling whitepaper I\'m working on is going to touch on this a bit. Thanks for providing me with more data for the feed!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1.3) Gecko/20070309 Firefox/2.0.0.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
