	(33217,825,'Blog Business Summit &raquo; Is E-mail a Broken Business Communication Tool?','','http://blogbusinesssummit.com/2007/04/is-e-mail-a-broken-business-communication-tool.htm','208.113.133.22','2007-04-26 10:50:18','2007-04-26 17:50:18','[...] My colleague Jason Preston has been arguing that e-mail is a broken system for quite some time now. I&#8217;m starting to agree with him. I have a number of e-mails in my inbox that I never quite get around to replying to. That&#8217;s not to say that I&#8217;m not paying attention. I do try to stay on top of all the projects I&#8217;m involved with. [...]',0,'1','Incutio XML-RPC -- WordPress/2.1.2','pingback',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(35232,1221,'phil ford','phil4d@mac.com','','216.243.131.31','2007-05-01 17:26:38','2007-05-02 00:26:38','I forwarded your earlier complaint about frequent MacBook Pro crashes to my friend MicroMat Tech 3... He suggested you post your questions at the MacFixit Forum. I didn\'t look to see if there were similar problems but you could...\n\nSince changing various Macs to OS X we haven\'t had a single computer crash. On occasion an application will crash but never the whole system.\n\nGood luck.\n\n    phil ford',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/312.8.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/312.6','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(35466,1223,'Hillary','hillary.a.preston@dartmouth.edu','','146.129.249.98','2007-05-02 14:36:11','2007-05-02 21:36:11','This sounds like the same craziness that happened every year at Bellevue High.  Except they at least said that the tickets were only needed if it ended up raining and they had to go inside.  But since it\'s Seattle I remember there was always someone running around trying to trade for extra tickets just in case (=me).',0,'1','Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 7.0; Windows NT 5.2; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; InfoPath.1; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 1.0.3705)','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(35977,1223,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','75.62.139.123','2007-05-04 07:10:45','2007-05-04 14:10:45','I think graduation is historically held in the Greek Bowl, and I think it pretty consistently fills up. As such, it\'s hard for me to blame Oxy for not giving out more tickets.\n\nAlso, multiply the size of the graduating class by ten, and imagine packing those people into the Bowl along with faculty, alumni, and whoever else gets tickets somehow. That\'s a lot of people.\n\nEven with the current number of tickets, people still clamor to snatch up good seat locationsâ€”and they start staking claims hours before the ceremony begins.\n\nSo is Oxy being stingy? I don\'t think so. But could there be a better way of distributing tickets than giving each student ten and letting an invisible hand sort things out? Almost certainly.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/419 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(35978,1221,'Ben','badlin@oxy.edu','http://www.adlin.com','75.62.139.123','2007-05-04 07:16:48','2007-05-04 14:16:48','Yeah, I have yet to crash my system as a whole, though once in a while an application will poop out. But I\'ve got a PPC, not Intel.\n\nStill, my shot-in-the-dark guess is that it\'s more a hardware issue than a system issue.\n\nGood luck.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; PPC Mac OS X; en) AppleWebKit/419 (KHTML, like Gecko) Safari/419.3','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
