	(41758,1249,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','75.38.30.150','2007-05-24 12:51:06','2007-05-24 19:51:06','Clearly \"meaning\" isn\'t something that\'s just inherent in the media - people take on all different kinds of meanings based on their previous experience. That\'s totally fine, in fact, I think that\'s probably why I enjoy a lot of \"mindless entertainment.\"\n\nWhat amuses me is that lots of people refuse to admit that a movie like Bad Boys II connects with them on some level, simply because they can\'t consciously ascribe meaning to it. If your subconscious is telling you it\'s entertaining, it probably is.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en-US; rv:1.8.1.3) Gecko/20070309 Firefox/2.0.0.3','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
