	(58429,1269,'Phil','locphil19@hotmail.com','','88.153.139.183','2007-07-06 21:46:14','2007-07-07 04:46:14','What hd antenna did you get? are you happy with the results. I am considering buying an off-air antenna for HDTV, all my channels are in the UHF band. Looks like CM4228 is the best candidate, it has great reviews (http://www.hdtvantennalabs.com/antennas/ChannelMaster-CM4228.html). But it is so damn large! I need something smaller that will work for me.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US; rv:1.8.1.4) Gecko/20070515 Firefox/2.0.0.4','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
	(58726,1269,'Jason','j@jason-preston.com','http://','24.41.60.9','2007-07-07 12:03:50','2007-07-07 19:03:50','The one we got is a Terk TV55 (http://www.sparco.com/cgi-bin/wfind2?spn=P18879), which is a lot smaller, but frankly I\'ve been a little underwhelmed by its performance. We did stick it in our attic, though, rather than outdoors, so it\'s possible that we\'d get better reception if we\'d bothered to mount it on the roof.\n\nAlso, I think the strength of the HD signals varies a lot from area to area. I got several channels fairly well in LA just putting a small indoor HD-antenna ($20) on the bookshelf, but up here we\'re having trouble getting more than three channels with the big one in the attic (and the indoor antenna gets no signals here).\n\nIt\'s also easy to set up and probably quite returnable if you buy it in a store. So it might be worth picking up on the off chance that it works really well for you, and you just saved yourself a bunch of hassle.\n\nGood luck!\n\n - Jason',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X; en-US; rv:1.8.1.4) Gecko/20070515 Firefox/2.0.0.4','',0,1,NULL,'N'),
	(58786,1291,'Ajay','ajayvideogamer@gmail.com','','71.138.248.168','2007-07-07 14:52:21','2007-07-07 21:52:21','I\'ve been interested in the orange box since Valve first announced it, just because TF2 and Portal look amazing and really fun and we all know the new installment of Half-Life is going to be good. The only decision for me is whether to get it on 360, rebuying Half-Life 2 and ep. 1, or to just get it for Steam (a more likely option.)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 6.0; en-US; rv:1.8.1.4) Gecko/20070515 Firefox/2.0.0.4','',0,0,NULL,'N'),
