	(793,1,'2006-08-03 18:16:32','2006-08-04 01:16:32','','flicker browsers',0,'','inherit','open','open','','flicker-browsers','','','2006-08-03 18:16:32','2006-08-04 01:16:32','',794,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/08/flicker-browswers.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),
	(794,1,'2006-08-03 18:16:43','2006-08-04 01:16:43','This is partly a product of having a reasonably small audience, partly a product of Firefox\'s growing market share, and partly a product of catering to a growd that just gets it. \r\n\r\nAt Flicker, Firefox still beats out IE as the number one browser that hits our site:\r\n\r\n<img id=\"image793\" src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/08/flicker-browswers.png\" alt=\"flicker browsers\" />','We have smart readers',0,'','publish','open','open','','we-have-smart-readers','','','2006-08-03 18:17:09','2006-08-04 01:17:09','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/03/we-have-smart-readers/',0,'post','',0),
	(795,1,'2006-08-05 14:17:46','2006-08-05 21:17:46','My oldest emal address is from <a href=\"http://www.seanet.com/whatsnew/\">Seanet</a> - leftover from the days when we had dial-up accounts that came with 500k of web space and an e-mail account. \r\n\r\nRecently they \"switched\" spam filters to some new system, but as far as I can tell all they did was switch it off. \r\n\r\nI had ten mail messages in my inbox this morning and 9 of them were spam from my old account. Since they turned it off last week I\'ve gotten an average of 15 spam emails every day, which is up from about 1.\r\n\r\nCome on Seanet, get your act together. ','Spam Spam Spam Spam',0,'','publish','open','open','','spam-spam-spam-spam','','','2006-08-05 14:17:46','2006-08-05 21:17:46','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/05/spam-spam-spam-spam/',0,'post','',0),
	(796,1,'2006-08-06 17:40:04','2006-08-07 00:40:04','<img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" id=\"image797\" src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/08/editor.jpg\" alt=\"editor\" />Writing to grow and atract an audience (what I do on <a href=\"http://www.flickergaming.net\">Flicker Gaming</a>) is a hell of a lot different from writing for my own gratification (largely what I do here). It forces me to play editor, which means trying to pick and write about things that people will want to read. \r\n\r\nIn other words, I\'m trying to figure out what people want to know before they know they want to know it. \r\n\r\nIt\'s turning out to be pretty damn tricky. At the moment, the best method I have is to take a guess, write it up, and put it out there. We tag a lot of things on Digg, so I actually have a quantitative list of each post\'s popularity: the number of diggs. \r\n\r\nSooner or later I\'ll get a good feel for what people really like to read, and that will make Flicker even better. ','Playing editor',0,'','publish','open','open','','playing-editor','','','2006-08-06 17:42:08','2006-08-07 00:42:08','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/06/playing-editor/',0,'post','',0),
	(797,1,'2006-08-06 17:41:31','2006-08-07 00:41:31','','editor',0,'','inherit','open','open','','editor','','','2006-08-06 17:41:31','2006-08-07 00:41:31','',796,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/08/editor.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(798,1,'2006-08-06 20:22:36','2006-08-07 03:22:36','Went to see the Blue Angels today at Seafair. Took some cool pictures.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/jasonp107/208679749/\" title=\"Photo Sharing\"><img src=\"http://static.flickr.com/84/208679749_755325d976.jpg\" width=\"500\" height=\"333\" alt=\"Blue Angels over Mt Raineer\" /></a>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/jasonp107/208679714/\" title=\"Photo Sharing\"><img src=\"http://static.flickr.com/59/208679714_42a72e4e9a.jpg\" width=\"500\" height=\"333\" alt=\"Blue Angels in a stack\" /></a>','Blue Angels at Seafair',0,'','publish','open','open','','blue-angels-at-seafair','','','2006-08-06 20:22:36','2006-08-07 03:22:36','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/06/blue-angels-at-seafair/',0,'post','',0),
	(799,1,'2006-08-07 11:36:01','2006-08-07 18:36:01','Did anyone else notice that the photo service <a href=\"http://www.flickr.com\">FlickR</a> has moved from being a \"beta\" service to a \"gamma\" service?\r\n\r\nI think that\'s pretty clever. ','FlickR in Gamma',0,'','publish','open','open','','flickr-in-gamma','','','2006-08-07 11:36:01','2006-08-07 18:36:01','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/07/flickr-in-gamma/',0,'post','',0),
	(800,1,'2006-08-07 18:29:07','2006-08-08 01:29:07','<object width=\"425\" height=\"350\"><param name=\"movie\" value=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/uEYCN3hVTYI\"></param><embed src=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/uEYCN3hVTYI\" type=\"application/x-shockwave-flash\" width=\"425\" height=\"350\"></embed></object>\r\n\r\nYou can find part 2 and part 3 on Youtube. ','I\'m not really sure where this came from but it\'s awesome',0,'','publish','open','open','','im-not-really-sure-where-this-came-from-but-its-awesome','','','2006-08-07 18:29:07','2006-08-08 01:29:07','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/07/im-not-really-sure-where-this-came-from-but-its-awesome/',0,'post','',0),
	(801,1,'2006-08-07 18:47:14','2006-08-08 01:47:14','It occurs to me as I look at photos like <a href=\"http://wvs.topleftpixel.com/archives/photos_people/060805_1639.shtml\">this one</a> and <a href=\"http://wvs.topleftpixel.com/archives/photos_skyscapes/060803_1637.shtml\">this one</a> that finding the right shot is only half the work in making a good photo. \r\n\r\nThe rest is in drawing out the right colors and mood - in digital photography, this means good use of photoshop and RAW conversion tools. ','Shooting is only half',0,'','publish','open','open','','shooting-is-only-half','','','2006-08-07 18:47:14','2006-08-08 01:47:14','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/07/shooting-is-only-half/',0,'post','',0),
	(802,1,'2006-08-10 19:00:32','2006-08-11 02:00:32','Assuming nothing really drastic happens before Saturday, I\'ll be on a plane to Amsterdam with my friend <a href=\"http://www.adlin.com\">Ben</a>. \r\n\r\nGetting ready for the trip is more trouble than I\'d like it to be, but I\'m sure I\'ll enjoy the trip. Posting will be light, but I\'ll do what I can. ','Getting ready to travel',0,'','publish','open','open','','getting-ready-to-travel','','','2006-08-10 19:00:32','2006-08-11 02:00:32','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/10/getting-ready-to-travel/',0,'post','',0),
	(806,1,'2006-08-31 09:29:22','2006-08-31 16:29:22','I\'m sure that by the year 2012 I will have grown to hate this page. It sits there with a queue of drafts listed garishly across the top and a huge title that says \"Write Post.\"\r\n\r\nSome days I just go nuts and write fifteen new posts about who knows what (and ironically, those are usually the days where I make myself write something pointless in the morning), and there are other days where I stare blankly back at the page.\r\n\r\nStupid blogger\'s block.','Sometimes it stares at me',0,'','publish','open','open','','sometimes-it-stares-at-me','','','2006-08-31 09:30:23','2006-08-31 16:30:23','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/31/sometimes-it-stares-at-me/',0,'post','',0),
	(803,1,'2006-08-11 21:36:55','2006-08-12 04:36:55','<a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photo_zoom.gne?id=212131390&size=s\"><img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\"http://static.flickr.com/62/212131390_891e39a4df_m.jpg\"></a><a href=\"http://waltercrespo.blogspot.com/\">Some people</a> are figuring out that tagging things in our Linkbox is a great way to draw some attention to themselves and drive a little traffic their way. \r\n\r\nLike all social tagging services, our Linkbox lets anyone have a real voice on OUR FRONT PAGE. Smart site owners know that letting someone else do the work to build up an audience and then basically advertising relevant content for free can really pay off. \r\n\r\nSometimes we even pull <a href=\"http://www.flickergaming.net/index.php/2006/08/11/bully-trailer/\">main page posts</a> from what gets seeded there. \r\n\r\nSo do yourself a favor and give the linkbox a whirl. \r\n\r\n','Get yo\'self some traffic with the Linkbox',0,'','publish','open','open','','get-yoself-some-traffic-with-the-linkbox','','','2006-08-11 21:36:55','2006-08-12 04:36:55','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/11/get-yoself-some-traffic-with-the-linkbox/',0,'post','',0),
	(804,1,'2006-08-17 07:11:51','2006-08-17 14:11:51','I\'m sitting in a pub in Brighton right now taking advantage of the free wireless network on my phone. Ben, who i an traveling with, is writing a massive email about our trip which i will ironically only be able to read once i get back home. <br /><br />So far the trip has been extremely fun, and it\'s been very refreshing to be away from all sorts of technology and the internet all week. I thing sometimes people today forget that vacation is supposed to be a removal from everything they are used to doing on a daily basis. I am looking forward to sitting on the beach in Nice next week and very intentionally not worrying about the blogoshere, flicker gaming, or anything else i worry about on a regular basis. <br /><br />I promise to take some really pretty pictures and share some stories later, but don\'t be surprised if i don\'t post again until i get back.','hello from england',0,'','publish','open','open','','hello-from-england','','','2006-08-17 07:11:51','2006-08-17 14:11:51','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/17/hello-from-england/',0,'post','',2),
	(805,1,'2006-08-29 23:05:54','2006-08-30 06:05:54','Hooray for getting in and trying to set up stuff that doesn\'t work. \r\n\r\nFor some reason, turning off my media center for two days has broken the remote control. And my e-mail doesn\'t work on any of my computers. \r\n\r\nlKJSDfpoaihds;lkahsdg','Nothing works',0,'','publish','open','open','','nothing-works','','','2006-08-29 23:05:54','2006-08-30 06:05:54','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/29/nothing-works/',0,'post','',1),
	(807,1,'2006-08-31 09:38:35','2006-08-31 16:38:35','<a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/88375037@N00/216169920/\"><img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\"http://static.flickr.com/66/216169920_006ddde0b6_m.jpg\"></a>I think it might just be one of the side effects of international travel and two weeks of vacation, but I\'m feeling utterly and completely disorganized. \r\n\r\nPart of it has to be the two-tiered moving in that\'s going on right now (I\'m semi-moved in but the person who was subletting from me for the summer still hasn\'t moved out), and part of it is just trying to get back in the loop of school, Flicker, real work, and friends I haven\'t seen in several months. \r\n\r\nRegardless, it\'s going to feel really good when I get everything settled into my room and into some sort of ruitine so that I can sit down and really re-organize my thoughts. \r\n\r\nThere\'s a lot I need to be doing right now, so I wish I could get myself un-cluttered and motivated. Scratch that. I <em>need</em> to get myself un-cluttered and motivated.','Feeling disorganized',0,'','publish','open','open','','feeling-disorganized','','','2006-08-31 09:39:50','2006-08-31 16:39:50','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/08/31/feeling-disorganized/',0,'post','',0),
	(808,1,'2006-09-08 11:20:14','2006-09-08 18:20:14','We just made lists in groups of what we each thought the top three security threats to the world were. The lists looked like this:\r\n\r\n1. Environment\r\n2. Lack of Education / Social Inequality\r\n3. Fatal Diseases / AIDS\r\n\r\n1. Global Warming\r\n2. Poverty\r\n3. Use of Force\r\n\r\n1. Poverty \r\n2. Environment (Global Warming + Resource Depletion)\r\n3. Disease\r\n\r\n1. Social/Economic Inequality\r\n2. Intra-state conflict\r\n3. Environment\r\n\r\nI remember hearing about a poll of the American people where they were asked if they felt safer than they did in September of 2001. Most people said no. \r\n\r\nI\'d probably say no too, it\'s just that now I\'m afraid of my government instead of the \"other guys.\"','Top human security threats',0,'','publish','open','open','','top-human-security-threats','','','2006-09-08 11:20:14','2006-09-08 18:20:14','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/08/top-human-security-threats/',0,'post','',0),
	(809,1,'2006-09-08 12:56:28','2006-09-08 19:56:28','Building, setting up, and actually getting my home-brewed media center to work has been a pretty ridiculous amount of work. \r\n\r\nSince I couldn\'t get Windows Media Center Edition to actually install on my computer, I bought and have been using <a href=\"http://www.sagetv.com\">SageTV</a>, and so far it\'s been working pretty well. \r\n\r\nThe problem is that, for some reason, it\'s the only application that won\'t correctly play HDTV. It\'s eons slower than the other two programs I have that can view HDTV. \r\n\r\nOne of the other programs that works with HDTV is <a href=\"http://www.snapstream.net\">BeyondTV</a>, basically a porgram that does what SageTV does, but that I originally tossed out because their Program Guide was buggy as hell (there\'s no point in having a program that records shows if it doesn\'t know when the shows you want to record are being broadcast). But it does play HDTV. \r\n\r\nSage has a perfectly working program guide, but doesn\'t really work with HDTV (crashes and runs slow). \r\n\r\nSo unless the SageTV support crew can fix the problem, I should probably either return the $100 HDTV card (which I don\'t want to do because I want to have HDTV) or get the BeyondTV program guide working and shell out the $100 for that program, or get Windows MCE installed properly (which probably involves completely reformatting my hard drive and starting over and i don\'t have the discs down here for that), or find another program I didn\'t know about before. \r\n\r\nNo matter what it\'s going to be a pain in the ass. \r\n\r\nEDIT: Apparently I was wrong about my limited options. A simple Wikipedia search led me to the following options to explore:\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GB-PVR\">GB-PVR</a>\r\n<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MediaPortal\">Media Portal</a>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.gallm.com/default.aspx\">Got All Media</a>\r\n<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Showshifter\">Show Shifter</a>\r\n<a href=\"http://go.connect.yahoo.com/go/tv/features\">Yahoo! Go TV</a>\r\n\r\nOr, if I want to install Linux, \r\n<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MythTV\">MythTV</a>\r\n\r\nNow I need to figure out which ones sport HDTV capabilities.','HDTV will be the death of me',0,'','publish','open','open','','hdtv-will-be-the-death-of-me','','','2006-09-08 13:18:43','2006-09-08 20:18:43','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/08/hdtv-will-be-the-death-of-me/',0,'post','',2),
	(810,1,'2006-09-11 10:40:00','2006-09-11 17:40:00','<a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/72131699@N00/221594347/\"><img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\"http://static.flickr.com/63/221594347_ec777b4c47_m.jpg\"></a>To a large extent I feel like all the movies and media coverage about september 11th, especially since we\'re...let\'s see...five years down the road, belittles the event and the people who died and the people who did heroic things to make sure fewer people died. \r\n\r\nSo I tend to want to ignore the September 11th hullabaloo, but <a href=\"http://5tephe.livejournal.com/47777.html\">this is a pretty good idea</a>:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>Make today not about the death, and destruction, and violence, and intolerance, but about the gift that you can make, yourself, right now.\r\n\r\nGo out today and do something tangible, that makes the world better.\r\n\r\nVisit someone in hospital, give blood, make a $5 donation to a charity, bake a cake for a neighbour, fix up that hole in your mother-in-law\'s fence...</blockquote>\r\n\r\nSo I\'m down. Who else?','Make the world better day',0,'','publish','open','open','','make-the-world-better-day','','','2006-09-11 10:40:00','2006-09-11 17:40:00','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/11/make-the-world-better-day/',0,'post','',0),
	(811,1,'2006-09-11 21:50:38','2006-09-12 04:50:38','<a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/mhanlen1/2028907/\"><img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\"http://static.flickr.com/2/2028907_4b0e78eb10_m.jpg\"></a>After my post the other day about how much of a headache getting HDTV working has been, I got an e-mail from Rakesh at Snapstream (the people that make BeyondTV). He was extremely nice and offered to provide me with a copy of <a href=\"http://www.snapstream.com/products/beyondtv/\">BeyondTV</a> to see if I couldn\'t get the program guide working and finally get settled in with my PVR package. \r\n\r\nSince I\'m still not able to get SageTV working properly (the folks at SageTV support have been reasonably but not extremely helpful), I told him I\'d give it a shot. \r\n\r\nI downloaded the trial version again today and I\'ve got it mostly set up and...surprise surprise, the HDTV runs smoothly like I expected it to. I\'ve also, at the moment, got the program guide working the way I\'d like it to. \r\n\r\nIt seems like the trick to getting it to run properly is to have a snapstream.net account <em>before</em> you do the install and setup. For some reason, at lest on my system, that jogged the program so it actually downloaded the data. \r\n\r\nIn short, I\'m looking forward to getting the product in full and starting to play with the interface. \r\n\r\nSo for now I\'ve got my HDTV (and it looks pretty) coming in just fine and my regular TV coming in poorly over an antenna. Thursday the satellite install is supposed to happen, at which point the last step is trying to get BeyondTV to play nice with my DishNetwork reciever. \r\n\r\nMy guess is that\'s going to be the last significant hurdle to my setup. I\'ll let you guys know how the satellite install goes, and once I\'ve got it all set up I might give a little tour of my setup just because...well I\'ll be proud of it. ','BeyondTV to the rescue',0,'','publish','open','open','','beyondtv-to-the-rescue','','','2006-09-11 21:50:38','2006-09-12 04:50:38','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/11/beyondtv-to-the-rescue/',0,'post','',0),
	(813,1,'2006-09-13 13:20:29','2006-09-13 20:20:29','','10m.jpg',0,'','inherit','open','open','','10mjpg','','','2006-09-13 13:20:29','2006-09-13 20:20:29','',814,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/09/10m.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(812,1,'2006-09-12 16:41:23','2006-09-12 23:41:23','\r\n <a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/jasonp107/241894942/\" title=\"photo sharing\"><img align=\"right\" src=\"http://static.flickr.com/81/241894942_cd8a2ad57d_m.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></a>\r\n \r\nProbably the coolest picture ever taken of me ever. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis is at the top of Beachy Head in Hove, UK - a bunch of 400 foot chalk-white cliffs on the sea-side.\r\n<br clear=\"all\" />','The Jump',0,'','publish','open','open','','the-jump','','','2006-09-12 16:47:58','2006-09-12 23:47:58','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/12/the-jump/',0,'post','',0),
	(814,1,'2006-09-13 13:20:50','2006-09-13 20:20:50','<img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" id=\"image813\" src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/09/10m.jpg\" alt=\"10m.jpg\" />Apparently <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0387808/\">this movie</a> is out on some extremely limited release because it\'s offensive and hilarious. \r\n\r\nAt least, I think that\'s the reason. \r\n\r\nI went to see it last week with my flatmate Ethan, and frankly it\'s hilarious - I\'d say it\'s better than Talladega Nights, which as we all know is obligated by pop culture to be funny. \r\n\r\nEssentially, Idiocracy is the story of an average guy who gets accidentally catapaulted 500 years into the future (in an army experiment gone awry). The future, however, is not all it\'s cracked up to be - it\'s populated by morons and idiots who are essentially caricatures of the morons and idiots today. \r\n\r\nFrom there on out, the entire movie is an expository criticism of dumb humor presented brilliantly through dumb humor. The most frustrating thing is that it\'s hilarious while laughing at you for thinking it\'s hilarious. \r\n\r\nGo check it out if you can. ','Idiocracy - or, that movie you should see',0,'','private','open','open','','idiocracy-or-that-movie-you-should-see','','','2006-09-14 10:06:18','2006-09-14 17:06:18','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/13/idiocracy-or-that-movie-you-should-see/',0,'post','',0),
	(815,1,'2006-09-15 09:27:06','2006-09-15 16:27:06','I\'m a huge Star Wars fan. I have been since I was about 10 and I first saw the movies. But the things is, I\'m really a huge fan of the original theatrical release of each movie - not the special edition. \r\n\r\nSo it was with great reluctance that I shelled out the $50 for Lucas\'s boxed set of Star Wars DVDs when they first came out. \r\n\r\nLucas insisted that this was <em>the</em> version of the movies, and that he wasn\'t going to go releasing any other riff raff, so either take \'em or don\'t. Well I took \'em. It\'s a lot better than not having them. \r\n\r\nAnd yesterday I found the original theatrical release versions at Target. Sure, they\'re not in a boxed set, but all three movies were there. So now I have three copies of each Star Wars movie, because there\'s the special edition box set, and then the new copies which come each with one disk of the special edition and one disk of the original theatrical release. \r\n\r\nLucas is a bastard, but there\'s really nothing I can do about it. ','Lucas is a bastard, but there\'s really nothing I can do about it',0,'','publish','open','open','','lucas-is-a-bastard-but-theres-really-nothing-i-can-do-about-it','','','2006-09-15 09:27:06','2006-09-15 16:27:06','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/15/lucas-is-a-bastard-but-theres-really-nothing-i-can-do-about-it/',0,'post','',0),
	(816,1,'2006-09-15 13:16:36','2006-09-15 20:16:36','I remember liking the tabbing option on live.com and now Google has added a tab feature to their customized homepage. \r\n\r\nI\'m going to have to add some tabs and check out how well I like it. \r\n\r\nThing is, I rarely use the Google home anymore because I keep getting automatically signed out when I switch computers. ','Tabs on the Google homepage?',0,'','publish','open','open','','tabs-on-the-google-homepage','','','2006-09-15 13:16:36','2006-09-15 20:16:36','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/15/tabs-on-the-google-homepage/',0,'post','',0),
	(817,1,'2006-09-15 16:27:45','2006-09-15 23:27:45','I just realized that the whole Star Wars DVD bastardness is going to happen all over again when the new HD DVD / Blu Ray thing get figured out. \r\n\r\nAnd damnit I\'ll have to have it in HD, too. ','Lucas has two more rounds',0,'','publish','open','open','','lucas-has-two-more-rounds','','','2006-09-15 16:27:45','2006-09-15 23:27:45','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/09/15/lucas-has-two-more-rounds/',0,'post','',0),
