	(991,1,'2006-12-04 20:39:26','2006-12-05 03:39:26','Ummm...excuse me?\r\n\r\nThis is what happens when you double-click on an mp3 file on the desktop?\r\n\r\nI\'ve had a bunch of people tell me to try Windows Media Player 11. I think I\'ll take this opportunity, since iTunes just erased FOUR YEARS OF MUSIC ORGANIZATION.\r\n\r\n(stormcloud)\r\n\r\n[ Edit: six hours later, and I\'m <em>still just as mad</em>. What kind of drunken idiot codes in a feature like \"when you open a music file, <em>delete the entire music library database</em>.\" That\'s retarded. That\'s beyond retarded. Find me one customer who wants all their music data erased when they double-click on an mp3. I dare you. It won\'t happen. Why? Because it\'s retarded! ]\r\n\r\n[ Edit Edit: <strong>FOUR YEARS</strong> of playlists! Including playlists that other people made for me! ]\r\n\r\n[ Edit Edit Edit: I wish WMP11 didn\'t give me horrible claustrophobia a shooting pains up my spine when I looked at its ugly counterintuitive interface. I really want to punish Apple right now. Is Winamp any good yet? ]','iTunes just cleared all my playlists, play counts, ratings, and...everything',0,'','publish','open','open','','itunes-just-cleared-all-my-playlists-play-counts-ratings-andeverything','','','2006-12-05 00:34:53','2006-12-05 07:34:53','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/04/itunes-just-cleared-all-my-playlists-play-counts-ratings-andeverything/',0,'post','',4),
	(992,1,'2006-12-05 18:09:55','2006-12-06 01:09:55','I remembered (as I\'m sure I would have eventually) that all my playlists and ratings and play counts and data and such are on my iPod, intact. \r\n\r\nHowever, I just spent an hour and a half figuring out how to connect the damn ipod to my computer without having iTunes automatically erase my iPod (because I have it set to auto update). I can\'t set it to manually update unless the ipod is connected (WHAT? Whose dumf*&k idea was that?). \r\n\r\nSo i had to create a new iTunes music library (hold shift while opening iTunes) so that it wouldn\'t be associated with this ipod, and it would ASK me before deleting everything. \r\n\r\nHowever, it\'s impossible to get the data (not the songs - THE DATA) from the iPod to iTunes. Seems like a pretty simple and useful feature, right? Not according to Apple. \r\n\r\nSo I\'m actually going to have to PAY $20 TO SOME THIRD PARTY to buy some software that re-loads everything from my iPod to my computer. \r\n\r\nEven better, these programs won\'t just copy the data EITHER. I actually have to DELETE ALL MY MUSIC and reload it entirely from my ipod BECAUSE APPLE IS TOO F$*&ING PROPRIETARY to let me RESTORE MY PLAYLISTS AND RATING DATA to my iTunes library file. \r\n\r\nI don\'t know why I\'m so mad about this. Maybe because it\'s finals and I have two huge tests on Friday and I can\'t concentrate because I don\'t have my music and I\'m really attached to my music. \r\n\r\nIt\'s like when my roommate called Microsoft to have them fix his xbox360, and they told him how they were gonna take great care of him, and then made him pay to ship in the 360 to get it fixed (he still hasn\'t done it). It\'s like, come on, you just told me how great your service was, and now I\'m dropping $20 to ship you something that was broken when I bought it?\r\n\r\nWell, all I hear is how great Apple is and how great their service is and how it\'s all sunshine and roses, and all I got when I called AppleCare (which is hard to figure out how to do in the first place) was \"oh yeah. that can\'t be done.\"\r\n\r\n!!!!!! /rant','Follow up on iTunes idiocy (or Dear Apple, fix your stupid software)',0,'','publish','open','open','','follow-up-on-itunes-idiocy-or-dear-apple-fix-your-stupid-software','','','2006-12-05 18:09:55','2006-12-06 01:09:55','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/05/follow-up-on-itunes-idiocy-or-dear-apple-fix-your-stupid-software/',0,'post','',0),
	(993,1,'2006-12-06 12:52:08','2006-12-06 19:52:08','I\'ve had a somewhat profile at <a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/in/jpreston\">LinkedIn</a> for a while now, and I\'ve been reluctant to fill it out mostly because I feel like I\'ve filled in my \"profile\" on a million other services already now. \r\n\r\nBut LinkedIn is going to be a great tool for keeping track of contacts I make in the work world. It\'s \"gown up\" (read: ugly) enough for some of the more established business generation to get it, unlike <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com\">facebook</a>, and it has some cool things like job listings. \r\n\r\nI imagine that if, for whatever reason, my hopes of continuing to work for <a href=\"http://www.parnassusventures.com\">Parnassus Ventures</a> come May fall through, I\'ll be checking the LinkedIn network for job opportunities. \r\n\r\nThat, or I may just see if I can\'t get my next super secret super cool business idea off the ground. \r\n\r\nps. Feel free to add me on LinkedIn if you\'ve ever met me, digitally or physically. I should grow my network. ','LinkedIn is actually pretty cool',0,'','publish','open','open','','linkedin-is-actually-pretty-cool','','','2006-12-06 12:52:08','2006-12-06 19:52:08','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/06/linkedin-is-actually-pretty-cool/',0,'post','',0),
	(994,1,'2006-12-06 17:35:24','2006-12-07 00:35:24','This will be interesting:\r\n<a href=\"http://avc.blogs.com/a_vc/2006/12/my_new_years_re.html#comments\">\r\nFred abandons MS altogether</a>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.feld.com/blog/archives/002098.html\">Brad goes Vista all the way</a>\r\n\r\nPersonally, I\'m looking at getting a MacBook Pro. I tend to be pretty at-ease in both a windows and an osx environment, so I\'m not too worried about \"switching\" between the two. \r\n\r\nAnd I do think that it\'s important when you use a Mac to use Mac applications - don\'t try to simply mirror your windows apps and workflow, that won\'t cut it, and you\'ll come away frustrated. Practically everything you can do on a PC (except full exchange support) you can do on the Mac with alternate apps.\r\n\r\nI think that Apple has a better laptop experience, and Windows provides a better desktop experience, at least for me. So that\'s what I plan to do. And if I really really want to, I can always install Vista on the MBP. ','OSX and Vista ',0,'','publish','open','open','','osx-and-vista','','','2006-12-06 17:35:24','2006-12-07 00:35:24','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/06/osx-and-vista/',0,'post','',3),
	(995,1,'2006-12-07 15:24:30','2006-12-07 22:24:30','I just wrote a big post about the \"iPhone\" and <a href=\"http://news.com.com/2010-1041_3-6141607.html\">this highly amusing</a> article, but because our school is retarted and still runs what is essentially windows95 on their public computers IE5 erased my post. \r\n\r\nSince I\'m studying for a huge final tomorrow morning I don\'t have time to write it all again, so here\'s the short version:\r\n\r\n<ol><li>He says the iPhone will be a failure.</li>\r\n<li>He\'s a funny guy, the article is hilarious.</li>\r\n<li>The iPhone won\'t be a \"failure,\" it will be just as popular as all other PDA phones except the blackberry.</li>\r\n<li>Insert funny quote to make you <a href=\"http://news.com.com/2010-1041_3-6141607.html\">read the article</a>.</li></ol>\r\n\r\nbleh.','I\'m grinning but i\'m crying',0,'','publish','open','open','','im-grinning-but-im-crying','','','2006-12-07 15:26:01','2006-12-07 22:26:01','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/07/im-grinning-but-im-crying/',0,'post','',3),
	(996,1,'2006-12-08 13:08:37','2006-12-08 20:08:37','I just finished my huge ECLS final, and I think I can literally feel the gigantic knots in my back easing up a little. I have a week until my next (and last) test, and then that\'s it for this semester of school - only one more left. \r\n\r\nI figured out that <a href=\"http://www.yamipod.com/main/modules/home/\">YamiPod</a> is the solution I was looking for - it lifts playlists from your iPod and lets you import them into itues. Go YamiPod!','Solutions',0,'','publish','open','open','','solutions','','','2006-12-08 13:08:37','2006-12-08 20:08:37','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/08/solutions/',0,'post','',1),
	(997,1,'2006-12-09 13:25:52','2006-12-09 20:25:52','Ran across <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uJFVOnWMfIk&eurl=\">this video</a> on YouTube from a few days ago. \r\n\r\n<object width=\"425\" height=\"350\"><param name=\"movie\" value=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/uJFVOnWMfIk\"></param><param name=\"wmode\" value=\"transparent\"></param><embed src=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/uJFVOnWMfIk\" type=\"application/x-shockwave-flash\" wmode=\"transparent\" width=\"425\" height=\"350\"></embed></object>','The breakdancing glitch in Gears of War - worth a chuckle',0,'','publish','open','open','','the-breakdancing-glitch-in-gears-of-war-worth-a-chuckle','','','2006-12-09 13:25:52','2006-12-09 20:25:52','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/09/the-breakdancing-glitch-in-gears-of-war-worth-a-chuckle/',0,'post','',0),
	(998,1,'2006-12-10 17:15:32','2006-12-11 00:15:32','I\'m kind of fascinated by the idea of \"human knowledge.\" I think whoever wrote Men In Black had this same preoccupation:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\r\n                                KAY\r\n		A person is smart. People are dumb.\r\n		Everything they\'ve ever \"known\" has been\r\n		proven to be wrong. A thousand years ago\r\n		everybody knew as a fact, that the earth\r\n		was the center of the universe. Five\r\n		hundred years ago, they knew it was flat.\r\n		Fifteen minutes ago, you knew we humans\r\n		were alone on it. Imagine what you\'ll know\r\n		tomorrow.\r\n</blockquote>\r\n\r\nIt\'s funny that we as a species \"know\" things. Nowadays people make a pretty big deal out of \"well, currently we know that the Earth orbits the Sun, but all we really know is that there\'s some movement going on, or maybe not.\" But it\'s odd that each time around we actually think we got the right answer. \r\n\r\nMy other favorite bit is that the phrase \"we know,\" as in \"we know how to accurately measure the age of carbon based materials,\" actually means \"some guy somewhere knows how to do this, or at least knows how to operate a machine that knows how to do this.\"\r\n\r\nIf the rest of the world died tomorrow, I\'d be so screwed. <em>I</em> don\'t know anything. ','Human knowledge',0,'','publish','open','open','','human-knowledge','','','2006-12-10 17:15:32','2006-12-11 00:15:32','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/10/human-knowledge/',0,'post','',0),
	(999,1,'2006-12-12 11:33:37','2006-12-12 18:33:37','Last week\'s Oxy Weekly, (the newspaper at Occidental College that has never been online, and probably never will be because the weekly staff is actually actively trying <em>not</em> to put it online. Seriously. I\'ve offered to do it like six times, and they just don\'t want it done. Luddites.) Anyway, last Wednesday the feature article was \"should oxy switch to an all-mac campus.\"\r\n\r\nThis is a silly argument to have for a couple of reasons:\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Oxy is broke</li>\r\n<li>Macs aren\'t really \"servers,\" and Oxy needs those</li>\r\n<li>Macs have some weird networking issues because of their stricter permissions setup</li>\r\n<li>Oxy is broke</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\nMy favorite bit though, is that one of the arguments for switching to an all-mac campus is, I shit you not, that anyone who doesn\'t prefer Macs \"has not been exposed to Apple computers and Mac OS X or they have been given misinformation about its capabilities and limitations.\"\r\n\r\nThis is a ridiculous argument, because it says that someone\'s <em>preference</em> is wrong. Imagine this:\r\n\r\nMe: Oh man, I like tuna salad. \r\n\r\nBob: No you fracking <em>don\'t</em>.\r\n\r\nMe: Fracking?\r\n\r\nBob: Shut up, toaster. \r\n\r\nThe whole thing is academic, since basically everyone has their own computer on campus anyway, and those that don\'t aren\'t really complaining too much. Besides, why not just get <em>some</em> Macs, and let people work on whatever they want. ','Macs at Oxy',0,'','publish','open','open','','macs-at-oxy','','','2006-12-12 11:33:37','2006-12-12 18:33:37','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/12/macs-at-oxy/',0,'post','',2),
	(1000,1,'2006-12-12 22:14:20','2006-12-13 05:14:20','I just emailed myself a Word document. I grabbed the file in my Gmail account, and the options were \"View as HTML | Download File.\"\r\n\r\nWhen is Google going to add \"Open in Google Docs?\" Because frankly, that would be a lot more handy for me. ','When is Gmail going to steal Word?',0,'','publish','open','open','','when-is-gmail-going-to-steal-word','','','2006-12-12 22:14:20','2006-12-13 05:14:20','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/12/when-is-gmail-going-to-steal-word/',0,'post','',0),
	(1001,1,'2006-12-13 18:38:56','2006-12-14 01:38:56','I <a href=\"http://www.redherring.com/Article.aspx?a=20173&hed=Yahoo+Dethroned+By+MySpace\">just read</a> that Fox has, with the help of Myspace (OK largely because of Myspace), has dethroned Yahoo! at the top of the list for internet pageviews. \r\n\r\nMy guess is that this shift won\'t be a very permanent one, since Myspace is, in my opinion, on its way out the door already. \r\n\r\nI know tons of people that still use Myspace, but it is by its very nature a fad-like site. I may have to eat these words in five years, but I don\'t think so. \r\n\r\nOK back to studying...','Yahoo! gets knocked off the top of the traffic list...but probably not for long',0,'','publish','open','open','','yahoo-gets-knocked-off-the-top-of-the-traffic-listbut-probably-not-for-long','','','2006-12-13 18:39:33','2006-12-14 01:39:33','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/13/yahoo-gets-knocked-off-the-top-of-the-traffic-listbut-probably-not-for-long/',0,'post','',0),
	(1002,1,'2006-12-14 16:56:07','2006-12-14 23:56:07','OK this is a feature I just found out about (I know, I know...I\'m behind the times), but Google Reader, which I currently use for my RSS addiction, allows me to tag any items I want and \"share\" them.\r\n\r\nThis is really cool, because it\'s like del.icio.us for feed items, and it\'s damn painless. \r\n\r\nI have a little widget I\'ve added to my sidebar that shows my latest five shares. I hope that I remember to use the function enough to make it worthwhile ;)\r\n\r\nIt\'s good because it\'s like recommending some reading without having to either leave my feedreader for del.icio.us or make a separate post about something. \r\n\r\nThese shared items are then aggregated into <a href=\"http://www.google.com/reader/shared/11789539690037107716\">my shared page</a> and it has it\'s own <a href=\"http://www.google.com/reader/public/atom/user/11789539690037107716/state/com.google/broadcast\">RSS feed</a>. So if you like to see what I like, add the feed. \r\n\r\nAnd if you want me to see what you like, send me an e-mail and I\'ll add your feed. This is exciting. ','Google reader does sharing!',0,'','publish','open','open','','google-reader-does-sharing','','','2006-12-14 16:56:07','2006-12-14 23:56:07','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/14/google-reader-does-sharing/',0,'post','',2),
	(1003,1,'2006-12-14 19:34:26','2006-12-15 02:34:26','I\'m on the phone with Pizza Hut trying to order a pizza. The fact that i\'m making a blog post <em>while</em> I\'m on the phone should tell you something is wrong...\r\n\r\nIt took me about five minutes to give them my phone number, no joke. Now he\'s trying to figure out that I want to order a pizza. Yes a pizza. No not ten pizzas. Yes a pizza. What size? A Large. No not a medium. OK he hasn\'t put me on hold, but the phone is squealing and he\'s helping someone at the counter. This has happened two times before. GOOD GOD.\r\n\r\nOK he finally handed the phone to someone else. Wow, that was easy. \r\n\r\nThe timer on my phone says 7:56 to order a friggin\' pizza for take out. That\'s not even deliver. The guy ignored the phone three times without even telling me I was \"on hold,\" and had me repeat things at least three times. You gotta have the right people answering the phones.\r\n\r\nThat\'s really crap service. I\'m not even sure why I stayed on the line. ','Oh man, pizza hut...',0,'','publish','open','open','','oh-man-pizza-hut','','','2006-12-14 19:35:55','2006-12-15 02:35:55','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/14/oh-man-pizza-hut/',0,'post','',0),
	(1004,1,'2006-12-15 12:28:42','2006-12-15 19:28:42','Engadget <a href=\"http://www.engadget.com/2006/12/15/wiimote-straps-recalled-yeah-all-of-them/\">tells me</a> that in response to all the breaking TVs from flung WiiMotes and other disastrous consequences of giving normally inactive gamers things to do with their bodies, Nintendo is recalling the Wii straps. \r\n\r\nHonestly, I like Nintendo and good for them, but this seems a little ridiculous. \r\n\r\nMy roomate and I have been playing the Wii since it came out, and while I\'ve knocked over some furniture myself, it\'s not because I <em>let go</em> of the remote. I can\'t think of a game where you\'re supposed to twirl the mote around by the strap. I\'m pretty sure such a game isn\'t going to exist. \r\n\r\nSo when people break TVs or windows by flinging the mote around, it\'s <em>because they let go of the thing</em>. Sure, the strap\'s there in case you accidentally drop it. But it\'s not <em>supposed</em> to hold a fastball. Honestly, you have to be a little slow to break something by flinging a \'mote. ','Nintendo nice enough to help out idiot gamers',0,'','publish','open','open','','nintendo-nice-enough-to-help-out-idiot-gamers','','','2006-12-15 12:28:42','2006-12-15 19:28:42','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/15/nintendo-nice-enough-to-help-out-idiot-gamers/',0,'post','',2),
	(1005,1,'2006-12-18 10:59:52','2006-12-18 17:59:52','I like to fly coach. \r\n\r\nI think it\'s because I like to fly with other people and because I like to have something to bitch about. But mostly I just don\'t like to be pretentious. \r\n\r\nDon\'t get me wrong, if someone offers me a free first class upgrade, I\'ll move right up, but I\'m perfectly happy sitting with most people on a plane. It\'s really not that bad: a lot of plane flights are either really short or come with movies (or now, games), and it\'s easy enough to bring a laptop on board. \r\n\r\nIf you need leg room, like I do, you can stand up and walk around. \r\n\r\nI don\'t know. There\'s something about coach that\'s really \"flying,\" which I like. ','Flying coach',0,'','publish','open','open','','flying-coach','','','2006-12-18 10:59:52','2006-12-18 17:59:52','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2006/12/18/flying-coach/',0,'post','',2);
