	(1319,1,'2007-07-19 09:35:19','2007-07-19 16:35:19','Interesting conversation at <a href=\"http://liberalcollegekid.com/2007/07/18/abstinence-only-education-because-not-talking-about-sex-means-kids-wont-have-it/\">Liberal College Kid</a>, where some of my friends post. Lots of good stuff in the comments. \r\n\r\nSomeone just compared sex to gun use:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>Iâ€™m fine for sex education in the class room, as long as it also incorporates mandatory weapons training, responsible wine tastings, and the rules for low-speed games of vehicular â€œchicken.â€</blockquote>\r\n\r\nTongue somewhat-in-cheek, I realize, but I\'m not sure it\'s a valid analogy. People are generally born with a set of equipment that they\'re physically and emotionally tied to throughout their life. Stands to reason they should learn about it. \r\n\r\nGuns...are not as ubiquitous or necessary. ','Abstinance only education',0,'','publish','open','open','','abstinance-only-education','','','2007-07-19 09:36:31','2007-07-19 16:36:31','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/07/19/abstinance-only-education/',0,'post','',0),
	(1321,1,'2007-07-20 13:27:09','2007-07-20 20:27:09','<img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/07/potterhallows.jpg\' alt=\'Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows\' />I figure now, mere hours before the widespread release of the last Harry Potter book, is a good time to make my official predictions. \r\n\r\nI haven\'t read any of the books since the last one came out, which is when I read the last one, and so on backwards. \r\n\r\nAs a result I don\'t have many, so I\'m going to make a few up arbitrarily, just to keep things interesting. \r\n\r\nThe list:\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Snape is a good guy (duh)</li>\r\n<li>Sirius Black is actually dead&gone</li>\r\n<li>Draco will somehow be involved in Voldemort\'s death</li>\r\n<li>Snape will die, Harry will probably kill him</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\nExcellent. Let\'s see how I do. ','My official list of Harry Potter predictions',0,'','publish','open','open','','my-official-list-of-harry-potter-predictions','','','2007-07-20 13:27:09','2007-07-20 20:27:09','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/07/20/my-official-list-of-harry-potter-predictions/',0,'post','',0),
	(1320,1,'2007-07-19 14:06:28','2007-07-19 21:06:28','The Wordpress.com news blog, which I never read, recently <a href=\"http://wordpress.com/blog/2007/07/18/facebook/\">made a post</a> announcing a Wordpress.com plug-in for Facebook. \r\n\r\nI never blog on Wordpress.com, although I do have an account so that I can use Akismet. I went ahead and installed the Facebook Plugin, but I haven\'t been able to get it to work yet. There are tabs for posting and stats and whatnot, but whatever I click just sends me to a page that says:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>You\'ve already added WordPress to your Facebook applications.\r\nVisit the My Applications page to adjust your settings or remove this app.</blockquote>\r\n\r\nOh well. I really just wanted to see if it would let me post to a WP install that I hosted myself. The answer appears to be no. ','Wordpress.com plugin for facebook',0,'','publish','open','open','','wordpresscom-plugin-for-facebook','','\nhttp://wordpress.com/blog/2007/07/18/facebook/','2007-07-19 14:06:28','2007-07-19 21:06:28','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/07/19/wordpresscom-plugin-for-facebook/',0,'post','',2),
	(1322,1,'2007-07-20 13:15:23','2007-07-20 20:15:23','','Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows',0,'','inherit','open','open','','harry-potter-and-the-deathly-hallows','','','2007-07-20 13:15:23','2007-07-20 20:15:23','',18446744072524589747,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/07/potterhallows.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(1328,1,'2007-07-24 14:15:10','2007-07-24 21:15:10','Have you guys seen <a href=\"http://jayslacks.blogspot.com/2007/07/to-sony-from-jayslacks-stop-it.html\">the news</a> that CNN is going to host a debate where presidential candidates will be forced to evade amateur, softball questions posed by YouTube users?\r\n\r\n<blockquote>More than 2,000 video questions have been submitted, representing a cross-section of issues and coming from as far away as Spain, Panama and Chad.\r\n\r\nCNN editors, including tonight\'s debate moderator, CNN host Anderson Cooper, will select as many as four dozen to air in the two-hour broadcast from Charleston, S.C. But the submissions, which must be 30 seconds or less, can be viewed at Youtube.com. </blockquote>\r\n\r\nThat\'s a pretty sweet debate idea. Bringing the debate back to the masses instead of having some boring, pre-arranged posing contest where candidates spend too much time thanking the host for such an excellent question. Let\'s have some stupid questions, so they can skip that part and go straight to the answer!','YouTube debate questions? That\'s freaking cool',0,'','publish','open','open','','youtube-debate-questions-thats-freaking-cool','','','2007-07-24 14:54:07','2007-07-24 21:54:07','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/07/24/youtube-debate-questions-thats-freaking-cool/',0,'post','',1),
