	(1349,1,'2007-08-02 10:52:52','2007-08-02 17:52:52','In preparation for <a href=\"http://www.seafair.com/\">SeaFair</a> the Blue Angels are doing some practice flying right over my house. Snapped a quick picture:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/blueangle07.jpg\' alt=\'blueangle07.jpg\' />','Blue Angels practice',0,'','publish','open','open','','blue-angels-practice','','','2007-08-02 10:52:52','2007-08-02 17:52:52','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/02/blue-angels-practice/',0,'post','',0),
	(1350,1,'2007-08-02 16:18:46','2007-08-02 23:18:46','Way back when I first picked up my MacBookPro, I scoured the net for cool downloadables, and drew up my own list of <a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/01/20/10-essential-apps-for-the-new-mac-user/\">10 essential apps for the new mac user</a>. Today I spotted a list of <a href=\"http://www.applegazette.com/software/5-free-os-x-apps-every-blogger-should-have/\">5 free apps for bloggers</a>, which linked to an app called <a href=\"http://bargiel.home.pl/iGTD/\">iGTD</a>.\r\n\r\nI have no idea what the \"Getting Things Done\" method is, but I\'m am frequently, hopelessly disorganized. I live my life by stickies. \r\n\r\nIf you want me to do something really bizarre, all you have to do is paste it into one of my \"To Do Today\" Stickies and I\'ll find myself on an airplane to Zimbabwe with six thousands dollars cash before I realize anything odd has happened. \r\n\r\nIn any case, I\'m going to download this thing and give it a whirl. Maybe it\'ll help me out.  \r\n\r\nUPDATE: This looks far too complicated for me. I checked the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Getting_Things_Done\">Wikipedia article</a> and some stranger with no credibility confirms my suspicions. \r\n\r\nNow if you\'ll excuse me, there\'s apparently some business in Zimbabwe I need to take care of.','Another list of free Mac apps',0,'','publish','open','open','','another-list-of-free-mac-apps','','http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/01/20/10-essential-apps-for-the-new-mac-user/\nhttp://www.applegazette.com/software/5-free-os-x-apps-every-blogger-should-have/','2007-08-02 18:43:05','2007-08-03 01:43:05','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/02/another-list-of-free-mac-apps/',0,'post','',0),
	(1351,1,'2007-08-03 12:22:33','2007-08-03 19:22:33','The Far Cry 2 dev team is smart to have a blog. They\'re smarter to post the link in the <a href=\"http://www.evilavatar.com/forums/showthread.php?p=902750#post902750\">Evil Avatar</a> forums, which I am known to haunt on occasion: \r\n\r\n<blockquote>Like our producer Louis-Pierre Pharand says on the intro page, the purpose of the video blogs is to show you guys all the cool things the team is doing, whether it\'s in a video, an audio clip or pictures, but keep in mind that it won\'t be game information all the time. We also want to show you guys the people behind the game how it all comes together it the end to make a kick-ass game</blockquote>\r\n\r\nI give the team props for going about the game-o-sphere and engaging.\r\n\r\nYou can check out their first videoblog post which I\'ve embedded after the jump\r\n\r\n<!--more--><object width=\"425\" height=\"350\"><param name=\"movie\" value=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/mDRhl1ipfWg\"></param><param name=\"wmode\" value=\"transparent\"></param><embed src=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/mDRhl1ipfWg\" type=\"application/x-shockwave-flash\" wmode=\"transparent\" width=\"425\" height=\"350\"></embed></object>\r\n\r\nI have to add, though, that it\'s a little unclassy to post in a forum and then ask for people to leave comments and feedback on your own:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>BTW - If you REALLY have SUGGESTIONS and COMMENTS, DO post them in the BLOG\'S COMMENTS or on our FarCry 2 FORUM (and say \'hi\' to Kimi while you\'re at it ). We really do read those and we REALLY appreciate your feedback.</blockquote>\r\n\r\ntsk tsk. \r\n','Far Cry 2 has a video blog',0,'','publish','open','open','','far-cry-2-has-a-video-blog','','','2007-08-03 12:22:33','2007-08-03 19:22:33','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/03/far-cry-2-has-a-video-blog/',0,'post','',0),
	(1352,1,'2007-08-03 17:01:12','2007-08-04 00:01:12','<img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/doom.png\' alt=\'doom.png\' />I know that sometimes it might seem like I sit here and regurgitate Valve press releases, but the reality of it is that I only regurgitate the awesome ones, like this one:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>DOOM, HeXen, QUAKE, and More Legendary Titles Launch Today \r\n\r\nQUAKECON 2007-MESQUITE, TX-AUGUST 3, 2007-id Software has teamed with Valve to bring some of the most successful game franchises in history to Steam, a leading platform for the delivery and management of PC games and digital content with over 13 million accounts around the world.\r\n\r\nStarting today, Steam users may download full versions of these best-selling and critically-acclaimed games, including the complete DOOM series and QUAKE I - III, including mission packs, as well as id\'s pioneering PC side-scroller, Commander Keen and vintage favorites Wolfenstein 3D, Spear of Destiny, Heretic, and HeXen. As part of the id Welcome Celebration on Steam, select id packages are being offered with a 10%, limited-time discount.</blockquote>\r\n\r\nIt\'s looking more and more like Steam is going to become the Wii Virtual Console of the PC, carrying all my favorite games from <a href=\"http://steampowered.com/v/index.php?area=game&AppId=6910&cc=US\">Deus Ex</a> (if you haven\'t yet played it, you should do so immediately) to <a href=\"http://steampowered.com/v/index.php?area=game&AppId=2310&cc=US\">QUAKE</a>. Excuse me while I go cry with happiness. \r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://digg.com/pc_games/DOOM_QUAKE_everything_else_from_Id_now_available_on_Steam\">Digg</a>','Valve just announced that Steam will carry Id Software games: yes, that means DOOM',0,'','publish','open','open','','valve-just-announced-that-steam-will-carry-id-software-games-yes-that-means-doom','','','2007-08-03 17:23:52','2007-08-04 00:23:52','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/03/valve-just-announced-that-steam-will-carry-id-software-games-yes-that-means-doom/',0,'post','',2),
	(1353,1,'2007-08-03 16:58:32','2007-08-03 23:58:32','','doom.png',0,'','inherit','open','open','','doompng','','','2007-08-03 16:58:32','2007-08-03 23:58:32','',18446744072523366630,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/doom.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),
	(1354,1,'2007-08-04 10:41:00','2007-08-04 17:41:00','<img align = \"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/stcover.jpg\' alt=\'starship troopers\' />I bought Starship Troopers about two months ago right after I finished reading <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Moon_Is_A_Harsh_Mistress\">The Moon is a Harsh Mistress</a>. That was actually the first Heinlein book I\'d ever read, despite the fact that I tend to like my Sci-Fi. \r\n\r\nI know it\'s hard to go so long without at least accidentally reading one of his best-sellers, but hey, it wasn\'t so long ago that Tony <a href=\"http://buttonmashing.com/2007/05/01/what-im-consuming/\">hadn\'t read Ender\'s Game</a>, either ;)\r\n\r\nI started ST as we boarded the plane last night, and I plugged through a really ejoyable hundred pages before I had to get in a car (and put the book down - never could read in the car). \r\n\r\nThere\'s an industrial quality to Heinlein\'s writing, his vocabulary seems clunky but spot-on, as though he never got past the first draft but the first draft is perfect anyway. It\'s fascinating. So far, I\'d recommend it to anyone who thinks they might like it: you probably will.\r\n\r\nHere\'s an ironically (or perhaps appropriately) good quote:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\r\nBasic truths cannot change and once a man of insight expresss one of them it is never necessary, no matter how much the world changes, to reformulate them.</blockquote>\r\n\r\nOne thing about vacation is I\'ll get plenty of time to catch up on my reading. Looking forward to it. \r\n','Finally reading Starship Troopers',0,'','publish','open','open','','finally-reading-starship-troopers','','\nhttp://buttonmashing.com/2007/05/01/what-im-consuming/','2007-08-04 10:45:40','2007-08-04 17:45:40','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/04/finally-reading-starship-troopers/',0,'post','',0),
	(1355,1,'2007-08-04 10:40:12','2007-08-04 17:40:12','','starship troopers',0,'','inherit','open','open','','starship-troopers','','','2007-08-04 10:40:12','2007-08-04 17:40:12','',18446744072523303037,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/stcover.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(1356,1,'2007-08-04 23:44:35','0000-00-00 00:00:00','My brain is wired to connect obscure facts and references. I do it all the time without thinking about it. \r\n\r\nIf you\'ve ever had a conversation with me, chances are I quoted a movie or a TV show, and usually its because something I see or do reminds of some weird joke in season two of Futurama.\r\n\r\nIn High School English class I would routinely fabricate good analysis without the slightest idea of where it came from or how to support my position. Eventually my English teachers learned that I really didn\'t have any idea where in the book I could find evidence. My brain did it for me, so I never bothered to learn. \r\n\r\nI think Eddie Izzard\'s <em><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dress_to_kill\">Dress To Kill</a></em> is the single funniest stand up comedy set ever. I think the funniest parts are where he refers back to jokes he made earlier in the show. Two mediocre jokes, one bizarre connection = a much better joke. \r\n\r\n<!--more-->That\'s just how my brain is wired. I see connections all over the place. Conversely, I can\'t ever think of good names. My poor children are going to named \"Gertrude\" and \"Steak,\" unless I marry someone with better naming skills. \r\n\r\nHow is your brain wired?','How is your brain wired?',0,'','draft','open','open','','','','','2007-08-04 23:44:35','2007-08-05 06:44:35','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=1356',0,'post','',0),
	(1357,1,'2007-08-05 12:58:24','2007-08-05 19:58:24','','Alberta Falls',0,'','inherit','open','open','','alberta-falls','','','2007-08-05 12:58:24','2007-08-05 19:58:24','',1358,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/albertafalls.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(1358,1,'2007-08-05 12:58:44','2007-08-05 19:58:44','<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/albertafalls.jpg\' alt=\'Alberta Falls\' />','Hiked to Alberta Falls today',0,'','publish','open','open','','hiked-to-alberta-falls-today','','','2007-08-05 12:58:44','2007-08-05 19:58:44','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/05/hiked-to-alberta-falls-today/',0,'post','',0),
	(1359,1,'2007-08-05 13:16:15','2007-08-05 20:16:15','This is maybe the first Playstation-related release that it is possible to miss. If you live in the US you can now run over to Gamestop and <a href=\"http://www.gamestop.com/product.asp?cookie%5Ftest=1&product%5Fid=020279\">buy an 80GB version</a> for the original, way-too-much price. \r\n\r\nOr, as I just found out, it\'s entirely possible to just buy a hard drive from newegg and <a href=\"http://www.gamespot.com/features/6176090/index.html?tag=topslot;title;1\">attach it to any version of the PS3</a>. Save yourself some cash and buy a 20GB version from ebay. \r\n\r\nFrankly, I got a PS3 months ago and it\'s basically served its time since I finished <em>Resistance</em> as a Blu-Ray player only. ','PS3 80GB edition now available, or you can just add a hard drive to a smaller PS3',0,'','publish','open','open','','ps3-80gb-edition-now-available-or-you-can-just-add-a-hard-drive-to-a-smaller-ps3','','','2007-08-05 13:17:30','2007-08-05 20:17:30','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/05/ps3-80gb-edition-now-available-or-you-can-just-add-a-hard-drive-to-a-smaller-ps3/',0,'post','',1),
	(1360,1,'2007-08-06 14:16:14','2007-08-06 21:16:14','<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/hellgatephoto.jpg\' alt=\'hellgate london\' />\r\n\r\nI like keeping an eye on video game press releases because I get juicy tidbits like these. I\'ve been <a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2005/09/20/hellgate-london/\">salivating</a> over Hellgate: London ever since I spotted it in PCGamer last year. \r\n\r\nBasically, this game is what happens when you take the majority of the group that worked on Diablo and Diablo II, and you let them make one game for the next five years. It promises to be one hell of a game, meshing up the RPG elements I loved from Diablo with a touch of the FPS feel that always works best for me in games. \r\n\r\nEA just announced an October 31st release date for the game in the US and, November 2nd for Europe:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\r\nHellgateâ„¢: London, the premier title from Flagship Studios, will start hitting retail stores in North America on October 31, 2007 and in Europe on November 2, 2007 for the PC. Hellgate: London represents the next leap in the evolution of the action RPG genre, combining the depth and addictive gameplay of traditional RPGs with the visceral action of first-person shooters.</blockquote>','Hellgate: London slated for October 31 release',0,'','publish','open','open','','hellgate-london-slated-for-october-31-release','','\nhttp://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2005/09/20/hellgate-london/','2007-08-06 15:39:47','2007-08-06 22:39:47','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/06/hellgate-london-slated-for-october-31-release/',0,'post','',0),
	(1361,1,'2007-08-06 14:14:34','2007-08-06 21:14:34','','hellgate london',0,'','inherit','open','open','','hellgate-london','','','2007-08-06 14:14:34','2007-08-06 21:14:34','',18446744072523117754,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/hellgatephoto.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(1362,1,'2007-08-06 18:49:50','2007-08-07 01:49:50','<img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/steaming_logo.jpg\' alt=\'Steam Logo Smaller\' />I\'m going to excuse my constant regurgitation of Steam news by saying that I\'m \"following Steam\'s development with interest, because it represents the future of game distribution and online play.\" It\'s true, but it\'s still kind of an excuse. \r\n\r\nValve just announced a beta set of features in their next update for Steam that allows players to do the following:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>The new Steam community features are designed to connect gamers with friends and other gamers, create and join groups, and organize matches and tournaments. The initial batch of features rolled out in the beta version include: \r\n<ul><li>Steam ID. Create a personal profile-complete with a photo or avatar, biographical details, favorites, and more-viewable on the Web and within the Steam client. </li>\r\n<li>Friends. Add peers to a personal Friends List that shows in real-time who\'s online and available to chat or play a game. Accessible from within the Steam client or while playing a game, the Friends List makes it easy to invite friends to chat, play a game, or join a group.</li></ul>  \r\n</blockquote>\r\n<!--more--><blockquote><ul><li>Groups. Create and join public and private groups comprised of gamers who share a common interest, such as fans of a particular game, map or mod, or competitive teams. The Group Profile page displays information about the group, recent activities,  news and announcements, and a schedule of upcoming events. Groups can quickly initiate a text or voice chat; plan a game, tournament, LAN party, or any other event; and track group gameplay statistics. </li>\r\n<li>Statistics. From both a personal Steam ID or Group profile, users can view a range of gameplay statistics, such as most played games or maps and average playing time. </li>\r\n<li>Chat. Initiate a chat with friends and groups using integrated instant messaging, text chat, and voice features.</li>\r\n<li>Events. Schedule matches, tournaments, and in-person gatherings, such as LAN parties. Upcoming events are displayed in both a list and calendar view, and members can receive reminders that help keep everyone on schedule.</li>  </blockquote>\r\n\r\nOne of these days I\'m going to dig up the two-page document I wrote up years ago when I applied at Valve hoping to be a marketing intern. They weren\'t advertising that they needed the position, but I figured that I was a bright guy and that might be enough. \r\n\r\nSo as an application I wrote out a two page piece on all the awesome things they could do with Steam. As far as I can tell, they\'ve used all of them. Which is awesome, because, my idea or theirs, it means I was right on with my market analysis ;)\r\n\r\nRegardless, I\'ve been thinking about sending a letter to Valve about stats, since they\'re ideally positioned to track games stats (a la xbox live) and to provide a gamer profile (a la xbox live), and they\'re much less likely to charge for it. It looks like they\'re finally doing it. \r\n\r\nI\'m hoping they plan to track FPS stats like <a href=\"http://www.theclq.com/\">The CLQ</a> used to. I still have saved pages of my rank way back when I jumped up into the 2,000s from playing way too much Counter-Strike. I also hope they give us a widget we can post on our blog (a la xbox live). \r\n\r\nAlso, as someone who signed up for Steam way back when they didn\'t ask for a username, they only asked for your e-mail address, it will be nice to set up a profile that gives me something other than nekro13 (at) yahoo.com. \r\n\r\nOK so basically I want them to co-opt the Xbox Live features and give them to me for free, since Steam is already my gaming hub anyways. \r\n\r\nOh, and the friends list and chat aren\'t new. I don\'t know why they\'re in the list. ','Steam announces social networking features',0,'','publish','open','open','','steam-announces-social-networking-features','','','2007-08-06 18:50:46','2007-08-07 01:50:46','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/06/steam-announces-social-networking-features/',0,'post','',0),
	(1363,1,'2007-08-06 18:43:57','2007-08-07 01:43:57','','Steam Logo',0,'','inherit','open','open','','steam-logo','','','2007-08-06 18:43:57','2007-08-07 01:43:57','',1362,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/steaming_logo.gif',0,'attachment','image/gif',0),
