	(1393,1,'2007-08-13 17:33:18','2007-08-14 00:33:18','One of the things that I had a hard time letting go of when I switched over to using Mac Mail instead of Outlook - which is basically all I\'ve used for years - was the horizontal layout that you get in Outlook. \r\n\r\nI was poking around Google this morning looking for a plugin to do something else entirely in Mail (which I still haven\'t found, and might try to make myself), when I stumbled across this plugin called <a href=\"http://harnly.net/software/letterbox/\">Letterbox</a>, made by Aaron Harnly, and if you download the latest version of the plugin and run the installer, you\'ll end up with a nice widescreen split-crazy-cool mail window that looks like this:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/mailwide.png\' alt=\'mail wide\' />\r\n\r\nEnjoy!','Letterbox makes Mac Mail like Outlook (in a good way)',0,'','publish','open','open','','letterbox-makes-mac-mail-like-outlook-in-a-good-way','','','2007-08-13 17:33:18','2007-08-14 00:33:18','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/13/letterbox-makes-mac-mail-like-outlook-in-a-good-way/',0,'post','',1),
	(1365,1,'2007-08-07 10:39:12','2007-08-07 17:39:12','Yesterday I drove up <a href=\"http://maps.google.com/maps?f=q&hl=en&geocode=&q=trail+ridge+road,+estes+park,+CO&sll=37.0625,-95.677068&sspn=39.729049,62.929687&ie=UTF8&ll=40.419769,-105.67337&spn=0.299015,0.491638&z=11&iwloc=addr&om=1\">Trail Ridge Road</a> with my dad and took about 150 pictures of scenery and wildlife. Between the two of us we had about four lenses to choose from, and I got some good pictures with all the ones I used. \r\n\r\nI haven\'t had time to really go through and convert the RAW files for most of them, but here are a few of my favorites:\r\n\r\n<em>The Range</em>\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/the_range_web.jpg\' alt=\'The Range\' />\r\n\r\n<!--more-->On the way up we got lucky enough to spot some Elk standing right next to the road. You don\'t usually find them this close:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/elk_1_web.jpg\' alt=\'elk 1\' />\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/elk_3_web.jpg\' alt=\'Elk 3\' />\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/elk_2_web.jpg\' alt=\'Elk 2\' />\r\n\r\nAnd we also saw a Coyote:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/coyote_1_web.jpg\' alt=\'coyote\' />\r\n\r\nThen of course, there\'s <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long%27s_Peak\">Long\'s Peak</a>, the 14,255-foot beast of a mountain that took me four tries before I made the summit:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/longs_1.jpg\' alt=\'The Peak\' />\r\n\r\nAnd my favorite shot:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/08/longs_2_web.jpg\' alt=\'Longâ€™s Peak\' />','Pictures from Rocky Mountain National Park',0,'','publish','open','open','','pictures-from-rocky-mountain-national-park','','','2007-08-07 10:39:12','2007-08-07 17:39:12','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/08/07/pictures-from-rocky-mountain-national-park/',0,'post','',0),
