	(1572,1,'2007-12-24 16:28:49','2007-12-24 23:28:49','A couple of years ago I spent a semester studying abroad in Brighton, England. \r\n\r\nIt was a very defining experience in my life, but it was that way for a myriad of reasons that are nearly impossible to count up and put together. \r\n\r\nWhile I was there I took some time to write a piece of \"creative nonfiction\" about my time there. It\'s called <strong><a href=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/12/hatw.pdf\' title=\'Halfway Across the World\'>Halfway Across the World</a></strong>.\r\n\r\nAnd because I\'m on a \"I\'m playing with InDesign\" kick (which I\'ll explain later), I\'ve laid it out in a PDF which you can download. I\'m reasonably proud of it. \r\n\r\nThe writing, not the layout ;)','Halfway Across the World',0,'','publish','open','open','','halfway-across-the-world','','','2007-12-24 23:26:57','2007-12-25 06:26:57','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/12/23/halfway-across-the-world/',0,'post','',0),
	(1573,1,'2007-12-23 23:41:18','2007-12-24 06:41:18','','Halfway Across the World',0,'','inherit','open','open','','halfway-across-the-world','','','2007-12-23 23:41:18','2007-12-24 06:41:18','',1572,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/12/hatw.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),
	(1574,1,'2007-12-24 23:36:20','2007-12-25 06:36:20','As I write this it\'s 12:30 am in Texas, which makes it Christmas morning (technically). \r\n\r\nFor me, Christmas has always meant my younger brother waking our entire family up at 6am so that we can stare groggily while he unwraps presents at speeds that make Speedy Gonzalez look like Regular Gonzalez. \r\n\r\nI\'m also not the type to try and figure out what my presents are before I open them; for me the surprise of finding out is almost as important as what it is I\'m unwrapping.\r\n\r\nBut beyond the presents, Christmas here in Texas means spending time with my whole immediate family, my grandmother, and my cousins. It\'s going to be a great day. \r\n\r\nI hope yours is just as awesome, whether you\'re celebrating Christmas or not. \r\n\r\nTo that end, I leave you this (just audio, really):\r\n<object width=\"425\" height=\"355\"><param name=\"movie\" value=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/wOR7sceBy20&rel=1\"></param><param name=\"wmode\" value=\"transparent\"></param><embed src=\"http://www.youtube.com/v/wOR7sceBy20&rel=1\" type=\"application/x-shockwave-flash\" wmode=\"transparent\" width=\"425\" height=\"355\"></embed></object>','Merry Christmas',0,'','publish','open','open','','merry-christmas-2','','','2007-12-24 23:36:20','2007-12-25 06:36:20','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/12/24/merry-christmas-2/',0,'post','',0),
	(1575,1,'2007-12-25 13:28:49','2007-12-25 20:28:49','<div id=\"quote\">I did have the one element necessary to all early creativity: naivetÃ©, that fabulous quality that keeps you from knowing just how unsuited you are for what you are about to do</div>\r\n\r\nFrom Steve Martin, in <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Born-Standing-Up-Comics-Life/dp/1416553649/ref=pd_bbs_sr_1?ie=UTF8&s=books&qid=1198614504&sr=8-1\">Born Standing Up</a>','Quote',0,'','publish','open','open','','quote-13','','','2007-12-25 13:28:49','2007-12-25 20:28:49','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/12/25/quote-13/',0,'post','',0),
	(1576,1,'2007-12-27 17:13:27','2007-12-28 00:13:27','I\'ve noticed that in the criminal absence of in-flight wi-fi connections, a lot of people are starting to write blog posts while they\'re on the plane and then post them later when they get home. I\'m doing that now as I sit on my flight between Phoenix (an airport with free wi-fi) and SeaTac (one without---get with it, Seattle!). \r\n\r\nI\'ve also just finished catching up on a good 3-400 blog entries. While I was stopped over in Phoenix I used <a href=\"http://gears.google.com/\">Google Gears</a> to pull an (apparently random) sample of blog posts down to my hard drive so that I could cruise through them on the flight. \r\n\r\nSo between Google Gears and TextEdit, I\'m pretty well set up for the flight. \r\n\r\nI also finished reading Steve Martin\'s \"memoir\" <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Born-Standing-Up-Comics-Life/dp/1416553649/ref=pd_bbs_sr_1?ie=UTF8&s=books&qid=1198800786&sr=8-1\">Born Standing Up</a>. It has an excellent title, and is a very easy read. I\'m sure the traveling helps, but I don\'t normally go through 200 pages in two days. \r\n\r\nSteve Martin has been one of my favorite comedians, if not my favorite comedian, for a very long time. I am, however, a big believer in \"passive research.\" Passive research involves me sitting around and waiting for interesting fact to find their way into my head of their own accord. \r\n\r\nWhich explains why most of what I learned about Martin\'s career and work in this book was completely new to me. \r\n\r\nI won\'t claim that I was any good at it, but I had a short-lived stint doing stand-up comedy in two or three coffee shops and comedy clubs. There are some things from his experiences that I find similar to my own, and plenty more that were completely alien to me. I found it fascinating, and if you have any interest in Steve Martin in particular, or stand-up comedy in general, I think you\'ll find it a good read. \r\n\r\nIn any case, I\'m rambling, which I assume is something that Just Happens on planes. I\'ll be home soon, and it\'ll be good to be back. ','Going back home',0,'','publish','open','open','','going-back-home','','','2007-12-27 17:13:27','2007-12-28 00:13:27','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/12/27/going-back-home/',0,'post','',0),
	(1577,1,'2007-12-31 11:02:41','2007-12-31 18:02:41','Posting has been light partly because of my shiny brand new Xbox 360. I haven\'t had one in my home for about four months now, and the return of next-gen console gaming has been glorious. \r\n\r\nHalo 3 is, however, a disappointment to me. It\'s basically the same as the previous two games. Here\'s my one-line review:\r\n\r\n<div id=\"quote\">Oh hey it\'s Halo, why is Cortana acting weird, and what\'s that flashy thing OH COME ON I WAS JUST TRYING TO RELOAD!!</div>\r\n\r\nwhy they changed that button I do not know. That was gloriously stupid of them. ','Halo 3 one-line review',0,'','publish','open','open','','halo-3-one-line-review','','','2007-12-31 11:02:41','2007-12-31 18:02:41','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/12/31/halo-3-one-line-review/',0,'post','',0),
	(1578,1,'2007-12-31 17:36:55','2008-01-01 00:36:55','My old roomie <a href=\"http://www.rabidspacedog.com\">Ethan</a> introduced me to this awesome move called <a href=\"http://imdb.com/title/tt0076637/\">Rolling Thunder</a>. That\'s right. Tommy Lee Jones. \r\n\r\nUnfortunately it\'s not available on DVD, and every attempt I have made to snag a copy has failed for some reason or another. Until now. Look what came in the mail:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/12/rollingthunder.jpg\' alt=\'rolling thunder\' />\r\n\r\nAwww jeah.','Rolling Thunder has arrived',0,'','publish','open','open','','rolling-thunder-has-arrived','','','2007-12-31 17:36:55','2008-01-01 00:36:55','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2007/12/31/rolling-thunder-has-arrived/',0,'post','',0),
	(1579,1,'2007-12-31 17:36:35','2008-01-01 00:36:35','','rolling thunder',0,'','inherit','open','open','','rolling-thunder','','','2007-12-31 17:36:35','2008-01-01 00:36:35','',1578,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2007/12/rollingthunder.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(1580,1,'2008-01-02 18:12:43','2008-01-03 01:12:43','According to the <a href=\"http://io9.com/339660/george-lucas-explains-why-youll-hate-indy-iv\">Sci-Fi blog io9</a> (worth checking out), George Lucas recently made a fool of himself talking about the new Indiana Jones movie that comes out in May. \r\n\r\nThey picked a few juicy quotes, and what nobody seems to have realized is that he has also accidentally explained why the \"new\" Star Wars movies are crap. Read carefully:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\"The fans are all upset. They\'re always going to be upset. \'Why did he do it like this? And why didn\'t he do it like this?\' They write their own movie, and then, if you don\'t do their movie, they get upset about it. So you just have to stand by for the bricks and the custard pies, because they\'re going to come flying your way.\"</blockquote>\r\n\r\nNow allow me to paraphrase:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\"When you write a crap movie, all you get is criticism. So you just have to ignore all the criticism.\"</blockquote>\r\n\r\nWhaaaa? Lucas, come on, you <em>have</em> to be smarter than that. \r\n\r\nYes some hardcore fans will whine if you don\'t include their favorite bit from their favorite fanfic, but you can\'t delude yourself into thinking that ALL FAN CRITICISM is inherently worthless just because it comes from fans. \r\n\r\n','George Lucas accidentally explains why Star Wars Episodes I, II, & III suck so bad',0,'','publish','open','open','','george-lucas-accidentally-explains-why-star-wars-episodes-i-ii-iii-suck-so-bad','','','2008-01-02 18:13:34','2008-01-03 01:13:34','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2008/01/02/george-lucas-accidentally-explains-why-star-wars-episodes-i-ii-iii-suck-so-bad/',0,'post','',0),
	(1581,1,'2008-01-03 15:13:34','2008-01-03 22:13:34','','firefox 3',0,'','inherit','open','open','','firefox-3','','','2008-01-03 15:13:34','2008-01-03 22:13:34','',1582,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/01/ff3.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
