	(1601,1,'2008-01-19 14:23:45','2008-01-19 21:23:45','As many of you may already know from my tweets or text messages, I broke down and bought an iphone on Thursday. It was a snap to set up an it has been a lot of fun to play with so far.\r\n\r\nI am, in fact, writing this post from the phone right now.\r\n\r\nHere is a list of my impressions so far:\r\n\r\n<ul><li>The keyboard works wonderfully. I\'ve written seveal long emails on I\'d and, obviously, this post. No sweat.</li>\r\n<li>The battery: considering what I do with the phone I am *very* impressed with the battery. Right now I\'m trying to get two full days out of one charge and I\'m right on track.</li>\r\n<li>Email is clunky. You can\'t aggregate multiple accounts into one inbox, and \"sync\" doesn\'t really do anything. They are missing some essential functinality here that I hope they fix in the future. It can\'t be that hard, and it would make the phone A LOT more ueful.</li>\r\n<li>Text messaging is really really fun. My plan comes with 200 of them, but the ichat-like interface makes it really easy to eat up 5 or 10 messages without noticing. I might have to bite the bullet and spend the extra $10 per month for 1500 texts.</li></ul> \r\n\r\n[Edit: also, there is apparently no scroll bar in the post window for the iPhone, so I can\'t edit any text from my phone if it\'s below the point where I\'d need to scroll to see it. Lame.]\r\n','My new iPhone',0,'','publish','open','open','','my-new-iphone','','','2008-01-19 14:29:48','2008-01-19 21:29:48','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2008/01/19/my-new-iphone/',0,'post','',1),
	(1602,1,'2008-01-20 13:55:28','2008-01-20 20:55:28','What if there were a device that combined the features and looks of both the iPhone and the Kindle? Something that was about the size of a magazine, but had a touch screen interface?\r\n\r\nWhat if you could get one for free, and for $10 a year you could get your favorite magazine delivered to it digitally? \r\n\r\nI wonder if that\'s a workable business model. I would use it.','The iphindle',0,'','publish','open','open','','the-iphindle','','','2008-01-20 13:55:28','2008-01-20 20:55:28','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2008/01/20/the-iphindle/',0,'post','',0),
	(1603,1,'2008-01-20 23:10:04','2008-01-21 06:10:04','What kind of horseshit is this? \r\n\r\nMy girlfriend asked me today if I could do her a favor and record the Lewis Black special on Comedy Central because she was going to be out at a movie with a friend when it came on. Silly me, I said no problem, because my media center is set up for exactly this sort of situation. \r\n\r\nWhen the show came on at 9, I flipped over to the media center to make sure everything was A-OK. This is what I saw:\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/01/restricted.jpg\' alt=\'restricted\' />\r\n\r\nEverything is very much NOT A-OK. \r\n\r\nI don\'t know if this is because Comedy Central is blocking recordings. I don\'t know if it\'s because Comcast want you to buy their DVR. I don\'t know if it\'s an HDCP compliance issue (yeah, like I\'m going to buy a multi-thousand dollar projector when I\'ve got one that works just fine). \r\n\r\nI do know that it is complete horseshit. I\'ve spend hundreds of dollars putting together a Media Center that lets me play my music, browse my pictures, call up my DVDs on demand, <strong>AND RECORD TV SHOWS.</strong>\r\n\r\nAllow me to repeat: I\'ve been sold hundreds of dollars of hardware designed SPECIFICALLY FOR ONE PURPOSE, which has then been arbitrarily shut off BECAUSE I BOUGHT SAID HARDWARE AS OPPOSED TO OTHER HARDWARE. \r\n\r\nIt is their right to do that, yes. Technically. But then why the f*&k do they sell shit on the market that doesn\'t work?\r\n\r\nI probably wouldn\'t have bought a $200 tuner card and a copy of Vista if I thought that they would just sit there and refuse to record TV. I might as well have bought that useless piece of crap AppleTV (oh, snap!)\r\n\r\nThis is the kind of crap that hardware companies and content delivery companies pull all the time, and I\'m getting really tired of it. \r\n\r\nYeah, I get it, some people are stealing your shows. But everyone who is stealing this show <strong>is stealing it anyway</strong>. The only thing that this does it make it so honest consumers like myself can\'t record the damn show so they can watch it later. \r\n\r\nOh, and coincidentally, it makes:\r\n\r\n   a) Windows Media Center a worthless piece of crap\r\n   b) Consumers spend more money on proprietary cable company \"services\" because WMC is a worthless piece of crap\r\n\r\nMicrosoft? You should be upset about this.\r\n\r\nSo now that I\'ve literally paid hundreds of dollars (thousands if you count past and recurring monthly cable bill fees) to get access to this content, I\'m being arbitrarily blocked. \r\n\r\nUp yours. If I had a blank tape in the house, I\'d be recording it on my VCR. As soon as the show is over and the special is up all over BitTorrent and YouTube and everywhere else, I\'m going to link to as many of those sites as I can. \r\n\r\n[ Update: I found a tape and am valiantly trying to get the last half hour of the show onto it. ]\r\n\r\n[ Update 2: If you\'re like me, with a DVR that wouldn\'t record it, and you want to download the video of Lewis Black: Red, White, and Screwed, you can try the torrents at either of these two links:\r\n\r\n<ul><li><a href=\"http://thepiratebay.org/tor/3521453/Comedy_-_Stand-Up_-_Lewis_Black_(Red__White__amp__Screwed).trg.avi\">Here</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.mybittorrent.com/info/102773/\">Or here</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n]','Lewis Black blocked on my Media Center',0,'','publish','open','open','','lewis-black-blocked-on-my-media-center','','','2008-01-21 17:44:20','2008-01-22 00:44:20','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2008/01/20/lewis-black-blocked-on-my-media-center/',0,'post','',0),
	(1604,1,'2008-01-20 22:47:47','2008-01-21 05:47:47','','restricted',0,'','inherit','open','open','','restricted','','','2008-01-20 22:47:47','2008-01-21 05:47:47','',1603,'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/01/restricted.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
	(1605,1,'2008-01-22 11:02:41','2008-01-22 18:02:41','<img align=\"right\" hspace=\"10\" vspace=\"4\" src=\'http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/01/motorcycle3.jpg\' alt=\'sidecar\' />Video Games have always been hitched oddly to the internet and tech advances, sort of like the guy in a motorcycle sidecar. \r\n\r\nThe first reason I ever used a modem was to play Warcraft II with my friend (and current roommate) Loren. Now Steam lets you buy and play videogames without leaving your computer chair. Blogging and web 2.0 are happening all over the place, and the PCGamer <a href=\"http://pcgamer.com/\">web site</a> still looks like the inside of the Hindenburg after it \"landed.\"\r\n\r\nSo now somebody in the mobile gaming space decided that this \"viral marketing\" might be for them too.\r\n\r\nYesterday\'s GamesPress had a press release about it:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\r\nViral marketing continues to grow in popularity as new services such as MoConDiâ€™s MeYou platform continues to expand its worldwide reach in Europe and the U.S. MeYou allows and encourages content purchases to be shared with friends and social networks for incentives via mobile devices and is one to watch in 2008.\r\n\r\nWith MeYou, users are rewarded for purchases and recommendations, which result in a purchase with redeemable credits. Friends receive mobile message recommendations that contain a message from users, a download link for the content and a link to install the MeYouTM application.</blockquote>\r\n\r\nTo be honest, that sounds like a really good idea to me. If I played mobile games, I\'d be all over a system like this, where I can recommend games to my friends and if games are recommended to me, I can choose to download it right there on my phone, no worries. I even get rewards for doing what I\'d do normally. \r\n\r\nI think more gaming companies and services should embrace the gamer recommendation system. I\'m betting that nothing will drive your sales like making it really easy for gamers to pick up the games that their friends are playing. \r\n\r\n','Viral Video Game Marketing',0,'','publish','open','open','','viral-video-game-marketing','','','2008-01-22 11:02:41','2008-01-22 18:02:41','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2008/01/22/viral-video-game-marketing/',0,'post','',0),
	(1606,1,'2008-01-22 04:23:20','2008-01-22 11:23:20','I worry that, as with their past platforms, apple will decide to make it difficult for devlopers to make games foe the iPhone.\r\n\r\nI\'ve already heard rumors that the SDK they\'re releasing in February isn\'t going to open up the kind of functionality that would really let games succeed on the device. That\'s a damn shame. Pretty much ever since I\'ve had my hands on this thing I\'ve been thinking about the hundreds of different ways it could be great for gaming.\r\n\r\nIt doesn\'t take a genius to figure most of it out. That\'s why there are so Manu games for jailbroken iphones. I hope that come February I hear about a lot of new games for my phone. Otherwise I\'m going to have I seriously consider jailbreaking it.\r\n\r\nNot to mention the battery lifeon this thing I\'d nuts, I\'ve been trying to run it down foe about 40 minutes by playing music and writing a post at the same time, but it\'s still going strong. I charged it two days ago.','The iPhone is an awesome gaming platform',0,'','publish','open','open','','the-iphone-is-an-awesome-gaming-platform','','','2008-01-22 04:23:20','2008-01-22 11:23:20','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2008/01/22/the-iphone-is-an-awesome-gaming-platform/',0,'post','',0),
