	(1868,1,'2009-01-27 18:20:40','2009-01-28 01:20:40','I\'m very happy to say that <a href=\"http://eatsleeppublish.com/why-the-future-of-news-brands-hinges-on-net-neutrality/\">my post</a> about net neutrality and the future of newsbrands <a href=\"http://voices.allthingsd.com/20090127/why-the-future-of-news-brands-hinges-on-net-neutrality/\">made it to the Voices section</a> in AllThingsD, the incredibly forward-thinking and WordPress-based digital arm of the Wall Street Journal. \r\n\r\nAs a result, Eat Sleep Publish is currently being crushed under the weight of zillions of eyeballs. At least, I assume that\'s what\'s going on, because Google analytics doesn\'t give me live traffic stats, and I can\'t think of any other reason why the site would load like a snail and the back-end won\'t even let me approve comments, let alone make a new post today. \r\n\r\nOh, if only I were <em>really</em> that popular...','AllThingsD links - and crushes - Eat Sleep Publish',0,'','publish','open','open','','allthingsd-links-and-crushes-eat-sleep-publish','','\nhttp://voices.allthingsd.com/20090127/why-the-future-of-news-brands-hinges-on-net-neutrality/','2009-01-27 18:20:40','2009-01-28 01:20:40','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=1868',0,'post','',0),
