	(1912,1,'2008-11-11 16:31:10','2008-11-11 23:31:10','<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/me.jpg\" alt=\"\" title=\"me\" width=\"460\" height=\"307\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-1811\" />\r\n\r\nJason Preston is the New Media Manager at the <a href=\"http://www.parnassusgroup.com\">Parnassus Group</a>. \r\n\r\nJason has worked with clients on shaping blogger engagement strategies, creating blogs, conceptualizing Facebook applications, and has spoken about Social Media at the <a href=\"http://www.webcommunityforum.com\">Web Community Forum</a> and at <a href=\"http://podcamp.pbwiki.com/PodcampSeattle\">PodCamp Seattle</a>. He has been quoted on social media and online communication technologies in the <a href=\"http://www.smh.com.au/\">Sydney Morning Herald</a> and in <a href=\"http://observer.guardian.co.uk/\">The Observer</a>. \r\n\r\nJason is also the founding editor of <a href=\"http://eatsleeppublish.com\">Eat Sleep Publish</a>, a blog and event series about the future of publishing. \r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in having Jason speak at your event, please contact him <a href=\"mailto:jREMOVE@MEjason-preston.com\">via e-mail</a> (take out the \"REMOVE ME\" in the e-mail addy). ','Speaking',0,'','inherit','open','open','','1810-revision','','','2008-11-11 16:31:10','2008-11-11 23:31:10','',1810,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2008/11/11/1810-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2056,1,'2009-05-21 21:40:39','2009-05-22 04:40:39','Jason is an accomplished public speaker and a recognized expert in both social media and journalism. He has presented for the Web Community Forum, the Redmond Chamber of Commerce, the Greater Seattle Chamber of Commerce, SCORE, the Social Networking for Business Conference, and Ignite Seattle.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in having Jason speak at your event, please contact him <a href=\"mailto:jREMOVE@MEjason-preston.com\">via e-mail</a> (take out the \"REMOVE ME\" in the e-mail addy). \r\n\r\n<strong>Examples of Jason\'s work:</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Ignite Seattle: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTY9PjrFOhA\">How to Say Anything in 140 Characters or Less</a></li>\r\n	<li>Seattle Chamber: <a href=\"http://vimeo.com/3442553\">Buzz Monitoring in Social Media</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<strong>Upcoming Gigs:</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>May 26-27: <a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com/twitterconference/?jp\">The Twitter Conference</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a name=\"bio\"></a><h3>Longer Bio</h3>\r\n\r\n<h3>Shorter Bio</h3>\r\n\r\nJason has worked with clients on shaping blogger engagement strategies, creating blogs, conceptualizing Facebook applications, and has spoken about Social Media at the <a href=\"http://www.webcommunityforum.com\">Web Community Forum</a> and at <a href=\"http://podcamp.pbwiki.com/PodcampSeattle\">PodCamp Seattle</a>. He has been quoted on social media and online communication technologies in the <a href=\"http://www.smh.com.au/\">Sydney Morning Herald</a> and in <a href=\"http://observer.guardian.co.uk/\">The Observer</a>. \r\n\r\nJason is also the founding editor of <a href=\"http://eatsleeppublish.com\">Eat Sleep Publish</a>, a blog and event series about the future of publishing. \r\n\r\n<h3>Pictures (right-click to download):</h3>\r\n','Speaking',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','1810-revision-4','','','2009-05-21 21:40:39','2009-05-22 04:40:39','',1810,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/05/21/1810-revision-4/',0,'revision','',0),
	(1913,1,'2009-03-04 16:50:29','2009-03-04 23:50:29','John Gruber <a href=\"http://daringfireball.net/linked/2009/03/04/kindle-burnette\">linked</a> to the Ed Burnette <a href=\"http://blogs.zdnet.com/Burnette/?p=834\">ZDNet article</a> wondering if Amazon intentionally crippled the Kindle iPhone app.\r\n\r\nIn particular, he wonders why Amazon makes you order books from their web store instead of through the iPhone app:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>Take shopping for a new book, for example. When you try that from the iPhone reader, the software simply opens up the web browser on the Kindle store at amazon.com. Itâ€™s practically impossible to actually order something from there, because the site is not very friendly to the small screen. The real Kindle has a real store that you can use right from the device. Obviously Amazon would rather you do your purchases from there.</blockquote>\r\n\r\nMy guess is that Amazon wants to avoid giving Apple the 30% commission on sales through the app store, which I\'m guessing that Apple would insist on, if Amazon were to build a book buying UI into the iPhone app. \r\n\r\n\r\n','Kindle iPhone app: Not crippled, just saving money',0,'','publish','open','open','','kindle-iphone-app-not-crippled-just-saving-money','','','2009-03-04 16:50:29','2009-03-04 23:50:29','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=1913',0,'post','',0),
	(1914,1,'2009-03-04 16:50:13','2009-03-04 23:50:13','John Gruber <a href=\"http://daringfireball.net/linked/2009/03/04/kindle-burnette\">linked</a> to the Ed Burnette <a href=\"http://blogs.zdnet.com/Burnette/?p=834\">ZDNet article</a> wondering if Amazon intentionally crippled the Kindle iPhone app.\n\nIn particular, he wonders why Amazon makes you order books from their web store instead of through the iPhone app:\n\n<blockquote>Take shopping for a new book, for example. When you try that from the iPhone reader, the software simply opens up the web browser on the Kindle store at amazon.com. Itâ€™s practically impossible to actually order something from there, because the site is not very friendly to the small screen. The real Kindle has a real store that you can use right from the device. Obviously Amazon would rather you do your purchases from there.</blockquote>\n\nMy guess is that Amazon wants to avoid giving Apple the 30% commission on sales through the app store, which I\'m guessing that Apple would insist on, if Amazon were to build a book buying UI into the iPhone app. \n\n\n','Kindle iPhone app: Not crippled, just saving money',0,'','inherit','open','open','','1913-revision','','','2009-03-04 16:50:13','2009-03-04 23:50:13','',1913,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/03/04/1913-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(1915,1,'2009-03-10 17:23:44','2009-03-11 00:23:44','I\'m finally reading Gladwell\'s Outliers (on my iPhone, through the Kindle app), and I\'ve realized the huge flaw in the 10,000 hours chapter - I\'ve easily spent that many hours writing, and I can\'t write for shit. ;)','10,000 hours late to the Outliers conversation',0,'','publish','open','open','','10000-hours-late-to-the-outliers-conversation','','','2009-03-10 17:23:44','2009-03-11 00:23:44','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=1915',0,'post','',0),
