	(1942,1,'2009-03-16 16:17:57','2009-03-16 23:17:57','<p>Steve Broback debunks the idea that price control is a good argument against oil use:</p>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<p>Even a measly 1.1 percent increase in output enabled a price collapse to around $40.00 a barrel. A deep worldwide recession didn’t hurt either. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>The problem is that even with demand down, the price has stabilized at what is still double the historical average, and four times what it was as recently as 1998 ($11.64 a barrel.) We are still susceptible to huge, debilitating price surges based on hypothetical interruptions half a world away.</p>\r\n</blockquote>','<a href=\"http://stevebroback.com/2009/markets-speak-drill-drill-drill-philosophy-validated-duh/\">Steve Broback on \"Drill, Drill, Drill\" philosophy</a>',0,'<p><a href=\"http://stevebroback.com/2009/markets-speak-drill-drill-drill-philosophy-validated-duh/\">Steve Broback on \"Drill, Drill, Drill\" philosophy</a></p>','publish','closed','open','','steve-broback-on-drill-drill-drill-philosophy','','\nhttp://stevebroback.com/2009/markets-speak-drill-drill-drill-philosophy-validated-duh/','2009-03-17 13:51:54','2009-03-17 20:51:54','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=1942',0,'post','',0),
