lso, say, \"I\'m a \n\nI can also understand why you\'d think that business use of Twitter is a lame theme. It sounds a little lame. But the fact of the matter is that Twitter is a very powerful community building tool, and simply tweeting is just the beginning of the story. \n\nIf you think that Twitter use in business is so simple it isn\'t worth talking about, then you probably haven\'t thought about how a company might want to experiment: does it make sense to dig into the API yourself? what tools are out there to help brand managers? How can you effectively visualize Twitter data? \n\nBelieve it or not, the signups <em>are</em> rolling in quickly. We\'re getting low on the early-bird $199 seats. The community is here...and I hope you\'ll join us. ','No Joke: 140 | The Twitter Conference',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','1979-revision-5','','','2009-03-24 15:37:08','2009-03-24 22:37:08','',1979,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/03/24/1979-revision-5/',0,'revision','',0),
