	(1997,1,'2009-04-06 11:18:35','2009-04-06 18:18:35','<blockquote>But then we got to thinking that we’re not really all that clever, especially compared to all of you. So we thought it’d be best to throw it open to everyone in the Twitterverse: come up with a better phrase for the back of the T-shirt, win a free seat at the conference. </blockquote>','<a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com/twitterconference/2009/win-a-free-conference-ticket-the-twitter-conference-t-shirt-challenge/\">Win a free ticket for 140 | The Twitter Conference</a>',0,'<p><a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com/twitterconference/2009/win-a-free-conference-ticket-the-twitter-conference-t-shirt-challenge/\">Win a free ticket for 140 | The Twitter Conference</a></p>','inherit','closed','open','','1995-autosave','','','2009-04-06 11:18:35','2009-04-06 18:18:35','',1995,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/04/06/1995-autosave/',0,'revision','',0),
	(1998,1,'2009-04-11 16:36:08','2009-04-11 23:36:08','This page is basically a rolling list of everything I come across that looks cool and that I think I might want.\r\n\r\nI\'ve decided to bold the things that I know I want, and leave everything else in the \"I wouldn\'t mind having this\" category in normal text.\r\n\r\nSo, (friends and family I assume), here\'s the list of everything I think I might want. Naturally, there\'s nothing I particularly need to have, but lists are always helpful.\r\n\r\nAnyways, here goes:\r\n\r\n<h3>The List</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>A <a href=\"http://gopro.com/\">GoPro</a> or <a href=\"http://contour.com/products/contour-roam\">Contour</a> mountable HD camera</li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://donkeykong.nintendo.com/\">Donkey Kong Country Returns</a> (omfg)</li>\r\n	<li>A Network-Attached-Storage device, preferably <a href=\"http://www.tigerdirect.com/applications/SearchTools/item-details.asp?EdpNo=3952307&Sku=D700-2364\">this one</a></li>\r\n	<li>A 500GB SATA 3.5\" HDD to go with it...</li>\r\n	<li>Good books</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Surprises</strong>!</li>\r\n	<li>An all-in one printer that connects to a network and does scanning, like <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/HP-LaserJet-M1212nf-CE841A-BGJ/dp/B0036TGGJQ\">this one</a>.</li>\r\n<li>Some spring clothes</li>\r\n<li>Another BESTA cabinet from IKEA - one section, two glossy black swinging doors</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Wishes for the future</h3>\r\n\r\nThat is, things I want, but that it doesn\'t make sense for me to have now:\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>A nice, comfy leather (or, theoretically, not leather, if it\'s comfy enough) couch that\'s just the right size and shape to sleep on all day.</li>\r\n	<li>Houseplants - maybe fake</li>\r\n\r\n</ul>','Jason\'s Wish List',0,'','publish','closed','open','','jasons-wish-list','','','2011-09-19 15:25:34','2011-09-19 22:25:34','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?page_id=1998',0,'page','',0),
	(2642,1,'2011-10-01 13:29:03','2011-10-01 20:29:03','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://uncrunched.com/2011/10/01/brutal-honesty/\">Arrington on Brutal Honesty</a></div>\r\n\r\nArrington quotes Vinod Khosla on brutal honesty, and agrees with it:\r\n\r\n<blockquote>“We prefer brutal honesty to hypocritical politeness.”</blockquote>\r\n\r\nI know I\'m not alone in admiring Arrington for his directness, but it seems to me like the ability to be brutally honest is a luxury you have to earn by getting to a place where you do not need people to like you. \r\n\r\n\r\n','Arrington on Brutal Honesty ',0,'','publish','open','closed','','arrington-on-brutal-honesty','','','2011-10-17 13:59:18','2011-10-17 20:59:18','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2642',0,'post','',1),
	(2354,1,'2010-05-31 18:04:17','2010-06-01 01:04:17','Or any other browser with a built in searchbox. I always type in \"google.com\" to the address bar and search from Google\'s own home page. \n\nAnd the <em>reason</em> I go to all this trouble every time I want to search is that it annoys me <em>to no end</em> that the last search string is retained in the searchbox after the search is performed. \n\nWhy in the world do I want everyone and anyone who looks at my browser or computer screen to see my most recent search string? \n\n','I don\'t use the Google Searchbox in Firefox',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2353-revision','','','2010-05-31 18:04:17','2010-06-01 01:04:17','',2353,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/31/2353-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(1999,1,'2009-04-11 16:28:37','2009-04-11 23:28:37','This page is basically a rolling list of everything I come across that looks cool and that I think I might want.\n\nI\'ve decided to bold the things that I know I want, and leave everything else in the \"I wouldn\'t mind having this\" category in normal text.\n\nSo, (friends and family I assume), here\'s the list of everything I think I might want. Naturally, there\'s nothing I particularly need to have, but lists are always helpful.\n\nAnyways, here goes:\n\n<h3>The List</h3>\n\n<ul>\n	<li>Feel free to get me another year of any of the following addictions: FlickR, Netflix, Cell phone, or PC Gamer...</li>\n	<li>Subscription to Fast Company or Wired</li>\n	<li>Clothes</li>\n	<li>The Empress of Mars (book) by Kage Baker</li>\n	<li>A record player?</li>\n	<li>An AppleTV? (It\'s cheaper refurbished)</li>\n	<li>A relatively cheap IP-print server</li>\n	<li>Set of wireless speakers that can be connected to a standard amp</li>\n	<li>Can\'t say I\'d complain about a Nintendo Wii</li>\n	<li>A new-generation Kindle</li>\n	<li>A wine cooler?</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Wishes for the future</h3>\n\nThat is, things I want, but that it doesn\'t make sense for me to have now:\n\n<ul>\n	<li>A nice, comfy leather (or, theoretically, not leather, if it\'s comfy enough) couch that\'s just the right size and shape to sleep on all day.</li>\n\n</ul>','Jason\'s Wish List',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','1998-revision','','','2009-04-11 16:28:37','2009-04-11 23:28:37','',1998,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/04/11/1998-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
