	(2002,1,'2009-04-11 19:02:14','2009-04-12 02:02:14','<blockquote>Apple designers come up with 10 entirely different mock ups of any new feature. Not, Lopp said, \"seven in order to make three look good\", which seems to be a fairly standard practice elsewhere. They\'ll take ten, and give themselves room to design without restriction. Later they whittle that number to three, spend more months on those three and then finally end up with one strong decision.</blockquote>','Apple\'s design process',0,'<p><a href=\"http://www.businessweek.com/the_thread/techbeat/archives/2008/03/apples_design_p.html\">Apple\'s design process</a></p>','publish','closed','open','','apples-design-process','','','2009-04-11 19:04:45','2009-04-12 02:04:45','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2002',0,'post','',0),
