	(2133,1,'2009-10-28 10:37:17','2009-10-28 17:37:17','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://whatever.scalzi.com/2009/10/27/what-obamas-doing-with-fox-news/\">The Fox News play</a></div>\n\nScalzi explains why the Obama administration is <em>not</em> making a mistake by calling out Fox News:\n\n<blockquote>Meanwhile the noise is all covered by multiple other news outlets, which in aggregate reach a much larger audience, which show Fox News anchors and personalities in the middle of ideological conniptions, confirming to the general population the proposition that, indeed, Fox News is more interested in politics than news, and reinforcing the impression that Fox News and the GOP are reading off the same page. </blockquote>\n\n','The Fox News play',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2130-revision-3','','','2009-10-28 10:37:17','2009-10-28 17:37:17','',2130,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/10/28/2130-revision-3/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2134,1,'2009-10-28 14:57:07','2009-10-28 21:57:07','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://movies.nytimes.com/2009/10/29/movies/29this.html?hp\">This Is It</a></div>\n\nManohla Dargis of the NYTimes on Jackson\'s concert movie:\n\n<blockquote>At once a greatest-hits compendium and a suggestive glance at what might have been, the movie — which had its premiere Tuesday and opened Wednesday on a staggering 18,000 screens worldwide — has been so nakedly designed to serve so many different agendas that it seemed unlikely anything would be left for Mr. Jackson’s fans beyond the sheer spectacle of such colossal posthumous exploitation. </blockquote>\n\nOuch.\n','This Is It ',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','this-is-it','','','2009-10-28 14:57:10','2009-10-28 21:57:10','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2134',0,'post','',0),
	(2135,1,'2009-10-28 14:57:07','2009-10-28 21:57:07','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://movies.nytimes.com/2009/10/29/movies/29this.html?hp\">This Is It</a></div>\n\nManohla Dargis of the NYTimes on Jackson\'s concert movie:\n\n<blockquote>At once a greatest-hits compendium and a suggestive glance at what might have been, the movie — which had its premiere Tuesday and opened Wednesday on a staggering 18,000 screens worldwide — has been so nakedly designed to serve so many different agendas that it seemed unlikely anything would be left for Mr. Jackson’s fans beyond the sheer spectacle of such colossal posthumous exploitation. </blockquote>\n\nOuch.\n','This Is It ',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2134-revision','','','2009-10-28 14:57:07','2009-10-28 21:57:07','',2134,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/10/28/2134-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2136,1,'2009-10-29 12:34:43','2009-10-29 19:34:43','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://scobleizer.posterous.com/why-i-dont-use-google-reader-anymore\">Scoble quits Google Reader</a></div>\n\nI quit Google Reader over a year ago, but for an entirely different reason than any of the ones Scoble offers -- I like to see web sites. The designs and colors are fun to see, and I feel like going through GR is, you know, <em>work</em>.\n\n','Scoble quits Google Reader',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','scoble-quits-google-reader','','','2009-10-29 12:34:45','2009-10-29 19:34:45','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2136',0,'post','',0),
	(2137,1,'2009-10-29 12:34:43','2009-10-29 19:34:43','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://scobleizer.posterous.com/why-i-dont-use-google-reader-anymore\">Scoble quits Google Reader</a></div>\n\nI quit Google Reader over a year ago, but for an entirely different reason than any of the ones Scoble offers -- I like to see web sites. The designs and colors are fun to see, and I feel like going through GR is, you know, <em>work</em>.\n\n','Scoble quits Google Reader',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2136-revision','','','2009-10-29 12:34:43','2009-10-29 19:34:43','',2136,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/10/29/2136-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2138,1,'2009-10-30 09:16:38','2009-10-30 16:16:38','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.joystiq.com/2009/10/29/screen-actors-guild-rejects-video-game-voice-deal/\">Screen Actors Guild rejects video game voice deal</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>The main opposition in the contract appears to revolve around the \"atmospheric\" provision, which allows employers to use actors in 20 voice roles, for up to 300 words, at the \"daily base rate\" of $782 for four hours of work. That means Nolan North might not just be the lead in your next video game, but play every character in the adventure -- we wonder how his falsetto is for female voices.</blockquote>\n\n','Screen Actors Guild rejects video game voice deal',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','screen-actors-guild-rejects-video-game-voice-deal','','','2009-10-30 09:16:43','2009-10-30 16:16:43','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2138',0,'post','',0),
	(2139,1,'2009-10-30 09:16:38','2009-10-30 16:16:38','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.joystiq.com/2009/10/29/screen-actors-guild-rejects-video-game-voice-deal/\">Screen Actors Guild rejects video game voice deal</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>The main opposition in the contract appears to revolve around the \"atmospheric\" provision, which allows employers to use actors in 20 voice roles, for up to 300 words, at the \"daily base rate\" of $782 for four hours of work. That means Nolan North might not just be the lead in your next video game, but play every character in the adventure -- we wonder how his falsetto is for female voices.</blockquote>\n\n','Screen Actors Guild rejects video game voice deal',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2138-revision','','','2009-10-30 09:16:38','2009-10-30 16:16:38','',2138,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/10/30/2138-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
