ity Forum, The Tweet House, and Ignite Seattle. He has written about social media and emerging technologies in <a href=\"http://crosscut.com\">Crosscut</a> and <a href=\"http://www.seattlebusinessmonthly.com/\">Seattle Business Magazine</a>.\r\n\r\nA lifelong gamer, Jason is the President and co-founder of the <a href=\"http://l33tsauce.com\">L33tsauce.com</a>, a videogame site that provides easy-to-use tools for gamers to publish their knowledge in online pages called Dojos. Gamers earn 50% of the ad revenue generated from their Dojos.\r\n\r\nHe graduated from Occidental College in 2007 with a Bachelor\'s degree in Diplomacy and World Affairs, which is a fancy way of saying \"Economics, Business, Politics, and Philosophy.\"\r\n\r\n<a name=\"short\"></a>\r\n<h3>Shorter Bio</h3>\r\n\r\nJason Preston is the Vice President of Product Management and Strategy at the Parnassus Group, a social media intelligence company based in Redmond. Jason has spoken at numerous local and national conferences including the Web Community Forum, The Tweet House, and Ignite Seattle. He has written about social media and emerging technologies in <a href=\"http://crosscut.com\">Crosscut</a> and <a href=\"http://www.seattlebusinessmonthly.com/\">Seattle Business Magazine</a>.\r\n\r\nA lifelong gamer, Jason is the President and co-founder of the <a href=\"http://l33tsauce.com\">L33tsauce.com</a>, a videogame site that provides easy-to-use tools for gamers to publish their knowledge in online pages called Dojos. \r\n\r\n<h3>Pictures (right-click to download):</h3>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-460.jpg\" alt=\"jp-widescreen-460\" title=\"jp-widescreen-460\" width=\"460\" height=\"114\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2059\" />\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-large.jpg\">Widescreen - Large Image</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads