	(2261,1,'2010-04-07 16:04:17','2010-04-07 23:04:17','<div class=\'posterous_autopost\'><span style=\"\">\"Basically, the OMB has issued a memo which waives cumbersome paperwork requirements for government communications that solicit or enable responses or feedback from private citizens. This paperwork was, ironically enough, required under the terms of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1980.\"</span><p /><div>Huuuuuge, no?</div><p /><div><a href=\"http://www.mediapost.com/publications/?fa=Articles.showArticle&amp;art_aid=125727\">http://www.mediapost.com/publications/?fa=Articles.showArticle&amp;art_aid=125727</a></div><p /><div><p /><div>- J</div><p />Sent from my iPad</div>      <p style=\"font-size: 10px;\">  <a href=\"http://posterous.com\">Posted via email</a>   from <a href=\"http://jasonp107.com/feds-say-bring-on-the-comments\">Jason Preston\'s posterous</a>  </p>  </div>','Feds Say Bring On The Comments',0,'','publish','closed','open','','feds-say-bring-on-the-comments','','','2010-04-07 16:04:17','2010-04-07 23:04:17','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/04/07/feds-say-bring-on-the-comments/',0,'post','',0),
