	(2294,1,'2010-05-10 12:43:36','2010-05-10 19:43:36','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://online.wsj.com/article/SB10001424052748704173804575233390919534652.html?mod=WSJ_Tech_LEADTop\">Rise of Zynga Pressures Videogame Incumbents</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Faced with shrinking sales in console and computer games, big game publishers are now starting to wade into social games themselves. EA last November acquired Zynga rival Playfish Ltd. in a deal valued at as much as $400 million. THQ Inc., best known for wrestling and fighting games, has created a development team focused on social games and plans to release three games this year that can be played through Facebook.</blockquote>\n\nWe\'re also looking at the rise of ad-powered video games. \n','Rise of Zynga Pressures Videogame Incumbents',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','rise-of-zynga-pressures-videogame-incumbents','','','2010-05-10 12:43:39','2010-05-10 19:43:39','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2294',0,'post','',0),
