	(2307,1,'2010-05-11 15:37:35','2010-05-11 22:37:35','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2010/05/11/opinion/11brooks.html?hp\">\"Organization Kids\"</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>I have to confess my first impression of Kagan is a lot like my first impression of many Organization Kids. She seems to be smart, impressive and honest — and in her willingness to suppress so much of her mind for the sake of her career, kind of disturbing.</blockquote>\n\nI definitely catch myself avoiding opinions in favor of having everyone like me. I don\'t think it\'s about career, though, as much as not wanting to be disliked. I\'m a big softy like that. ','\"Organization Kids\"',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','organization-kids','','','2010-05-11 15:37:38','2010-05-11 22:37:38','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2307',0,'post','',0),
	(2308,1,'2010-05-11 15:37:35','2010-05-11 22:37:35','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2010/05/11/opinion/11brooks.html?hp\">\"Organization Kids\"</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>I have to confess my first impression of Kagan is a lot like my first impression of many Organization Kids. She seems to be smart, impressive and honest — and in her willingness to suppress so much of her mind for the sake of her career, kind of disturbing.</blockquote>\n\nI definitely catch myself avoiding opinions in favor of having everyone like me. I don\'t think it\'s about career, though, as much as not wanting to be disliked. I\'m a big softy like that. ','\"Organization Kids\"',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2307-revision','','','2010-05-11 15:37:35','2010-05-11 22:37:35','',2307,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/11/2307-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2309,1,'2010-05-11 16:17:44','2010-05-11 23:17:44','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2010/05/10/tracking-the-science-of-commitment/?src=me&ref=general\">Even relationships are selfish (apparently)</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>But it may not be feelings of love or loyalty that keep couples together. Instead, scientists speculate that your level of commitment may depend on how much a partner enhances your life and broadens your horizons — a concept that Arthur Aron, a psychologist and relationship researcher at Stony Brook University, calls \"self-expansion.\"</blockquote>\n\nIt\'s that old argument that there is no altruism, because when you are doing good you are doing good in order to feel better about yourself. ','Even relationships are selfish (apparently)',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','even-relationships-are-selfish-apparently','','','2010-05-11 16:17:46','2010-05-11 23:17:46','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2309',0,'post','',0),
	(2310,1,'2010-05-11 16:17:44','2010-05-11 23:17:44','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2010/05/10/tracking-the-science-of-commitment/?src=me&ref=general\">Even relationships are selfish (apparently)</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>But it may not be feelings of love or loyalty that keep couples together. Instead, scientists speculate that your level of commitment may depend on how much a partner enhances your life and broadens your horizons — a concept that Arthur Aron, a psychologist and relationship researcher at Stony Brook University, calls \"self-expansion.\"</blockquote>\n\nIt\'s that old argument that there is no altruism, because when you are doing good you are doing good in order to feel better about yourself. ','Even relationships are selfish (apparently)',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2309-revision','','','2010-05-11 16:17:44','2010-05-11 23:17:44','',2309,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/11/2309-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2311,1,'2010-05-12 12:34:45','2010-05-12 19:34:45','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://store.steampowered.com/freeportal/\">Portal is free (as in beer) until May 24</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Portal used to cost money. Until May 24th, it\'s free. End of story.\n\nWell, technically speaking, there are some strings attached. Fortunately, they\'re entirely decorative. We just like the way they look, swaying in the gentle breeze created by a million people simultanously fainting from shock at the news that Portal is free. Now you have no reason not to try Portal.\n\n\"I have a reason,\" some of you are probably typing into an angry email. \"You see, sir, I own a Mac.\"\n\nWell guess what: For the first time ever, Portal is also available for the Mac. </blockquote>\n\n','Portal is free (as in beer) until May 24',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','portal-is-free-as-in-beer-until-may-24','','','2010-05-12 12:34:47','2010-05-12 19:34:47','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2311',0,'post','',0),
	(2312,1,'2010-05-12 12:34:45','2010-05-12 19:34:45','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://store.steampowered.com/freeportal/\">Portal is free (as in beer) until May 24</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Portal used to cost money. Until May 24th, it\'s free. End of story.\n\nWell, technically speaking, there are some strings attached. Fortunately, they\'re entirely decorative. We just like the way they look, swaying in the gentle breeze created by a million people simultanously fainting from shock at the news that Portal is free. Now you have no reason not to try Portal.\n\n\"I have a reason,\" some of you are probably typing into an angry email. \"You see, sir, I own a Mac.\"\n\nWell guess what: For the first time ever, Portal is also available for the Mac. </blockquote>\n\n','Portal is free (as in beer) until May 24',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2311-revision','','','2010-05-12 12:34:45','2010-05-12 19:34:45','',2311,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/12/2311-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
