	(2321,1,'2010-05-13 15:01:09','2010-05-13 22:01:09','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2010/05/13/a-new-entry-into-the-world-of-location-based-games/?ref=technology\">Scvngr</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Scvngr hopes some of its mobile features — a points system and ease of use — will distinguish it from other location-based social networks.</blockquote>\n\nErr...what? Did they miss the <a href=\"http://playfoursquare.com\">Foursquare</a> memo?\n\nAlthough I have to admin, this sounds pretty cool:\n\n<blockquote>He added that he hoped to make Scvngr “a game layer on top of the world,” where anyone could create and play games.</blockquote>\n','Scvngr',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','scvngr','','','2010-05-13 15:01:11','2010-05-13 22:01:11','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2321',0,'post','',0),
	(2322,1,'2010-05-13 15:01:09','2010-05-13 22:01:09','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2010/05/13/a-new-entry-into-the-world-of-location-based-games/?ref=technology\">Scvngr</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Scvngr hopes some of its mobile features — a points system and ease of use — will distinguish it from other location-based social networks.</blockquote>\n\nErr...what? Did they miss the <a href=\"http://playfoursquare.com\">Foursquare</a> memo?\n\nAlthough I have to admin, this sounds pretty cool:\n\n<blockquote>He added that he hoped to make Scvngr “a game layer on top of the world,” where anyone could create and play games.</blockquote>\n','Scvngr',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2321-revision','','','2010-05-13 15:01:09','2010-05-13 22:01:09','',2321,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/13/2321-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2323,1,'2010-05-13 19:05:57','2010-05-14 02:05:57','As I was just checking in on Foursquare at la cucina del puerco (good Mexican in Bellevue) I realized why Twitter will never kil Foursquare: because 4sq is actually just another portal/interface to Twitter. \r\n\r\nWhy do I check in? It\'s not for the points, and I don\'t really care if I\'m the mayor unless the mayor gets a discount. I check in so that I can share my location conveniently with my friends on Twitter. \r\n\r\nWith Foursquare, I navigate to the venue, compose my tweet, and it comes pre populated with a host of geo information about the *venue* - not just about me. \r\n\r\nSo really when I use Foursquare I\'m just using Twitter, enhanced. \r\n\r\nI also suspect that a significant portion of 4sq\'s value is tied to Twitter right now, because they don\'t have a great built in \"stream\" audience (yet). Who knows whether they\'ll be successful in creating that independent community. \r\n\r\nBut as long as Foursquare is providing an enhacwd interface to Twitter, and driving use of the Twitter network, they won\'t kill Twitter.','Why Foursquare won\'t kill Twitter',0,'','publish','closed','open','','why-foursquare-wont-kill-twitter','','','2010-05-17 19:25:44','2010-05-18 02:25:44','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/13/why-foursquare-wont-kill-twitter/',0,'post','',0),
	(2327,1,'2010-05-17 19:25:02','2010-05-18 02:25:02','As I was just checking in on Foursquare at la cucina del puerco (good Mexican in Bellevue) I realized why Twitter will never kil Foursquare: because 4sq is actually just another portal/interface to Twitter. <p /> Why do I check in? It\'s not for the points, and I don\'t really care if I\'m the mayor unless the mayor gets a discount. I check in so that I can share my location conveniently with my friends on Twitter. <p /> With Foursquare, I navigate to the venue, compose my tweet, and it comes pre populated with a host of geo information about the *venue* - not just about me. <p /> So really when I use Foursquare I\'m just using Twitter, enhanced. <p /> I also suspect that a significant portion of 4sq\'s value is tied to Twitter right now, because they don\'t have a great built in \"stream\" audience (yet). Who knows whether they\'ll be successful in creating that independent community. <p /> But as long as Foursquare is providing an enhacwd interface to Twitter, and driving use of the Twitter network, they won\'t kill Twitter.','Why Foursquare won\'t kill Twitter',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2323-revision-3','','','2010-05-17 19:25:02','2010-05-18 02:25:02','',2323,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/17/2323-revision-3/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2326,1,'2010-05-17 19:24:43','2010-05-18 02:24:43','<div class=\'posterous_autopost\'>As I was just checking in on Foursquare at la cucina del puerco (good Mexican in Bellevue) I realized why Twitter will never kil Foursquare: because 4sq is actually just another portal/interface to Twitter. <p /> Why do I check in? It\'s not for the points, and I don\'t really care if I\'m the mayor unless the mayor gets a discount. I check in so that I can share my location conveniently with my friends on Twitter. <p /> With Foursquare, I navigate to the venue, compose my tweet, and it comes pre populated with a host of geo information about the *venue* - not just about me. <p /> So really when I use Foursquare I\'m just using Twitter, enhanced. <p /> I also suspect that a significant portion of 4sq\'s value is tied to Twitter right now, because they don\'t have a great built in \"stream\" audience (yet). Who knows whether they\'ll be successful in creating that independent community. <p /> But as long as Foursquare is providing an enhacwd interface to Twitter, and driving use of the Twitter network, they won\'t kill Twitter.','Why Foursquare won\'t kill Twitter',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2323-revision-2','','','2010-05-17 19:24:43','2010-05-18 02:24:43','',2323,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/17/2323-revision-2/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2324,1,'2010-05-13 14:05:25','2010-05-13 21:05:25','<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\" alt=\"jason-bnw-border\" title=\"jason-bnw-border\" width=\"240\" height=\"297\" class=\"alignright size-full wp-image-2055\" /><strong>Jason Preston</strong> is an accomplished public speaker and a recognized expert in both social media and publishing. \r\n\r\nHe has presented for the Web Community Forum, the Redmond Chamber of Commerce, the Greater Seattle Chamber of Commerce, SCORE, the Social Networking for Business Conference, Ignite Seattle, and 140 | The Twitter Conference.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in having Jason speak at your event, please contact him via e-mail: j AT jason-preston.com. \r\n\r\n<strong>Video of Jason\'s work:</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n        <li>The Twitter Conference: <a href=\"http://vimeo.com/7148408\">The Comedy Session - Being Funny, In Short</a></li>\r\n	<li>Ignite Seattle: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTY9PjrFOhA\">How to Say Anything in 140 Characters or Less</a></li>\r\n	<li>Seattle Chamber: <a href=\"http://vimeo.com/3442553\">Buzz Monitoring in Social Media</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a name=\"long\"></a>\r\n<h3>Longer Bio</h3>\r\n\r\nJason Preston is the Vice President of Product Management and Strategy for the <a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com\">Parnassus Group</a>, a Redmond-based company that produces conferences and parties around emerging technologies, and provides social media intelligence to clients and partners seeking to effectively participate in online communities. \r\n\r\nJason has worked with clients on shaping blogger engagement strategies, creating blogs, and understanding the business value of social media tools like Twitter and Facebook. He has spoken at numerous local and national conferences including the Web Community Forum, The Tweet House, and Ignite Seattle. He has written about social media and emerging technologies in <a href=\"http://crosscut.com\">Crosscut</a> and <a href=\"http://www.seattlebusinessmonthly.com/\">Seattle Business Magazine</a>.\r\n\r\nA lifelong gamer, Jason is the President and co-founder of <a href=\"http://l33tsauce.com\">L33tsauce.com</a>, a videogame site that provides easy-to-use tools for gamers to publish their knowledge in online pages called Dojos. Gamers earn 50% of the ad revenue generated from their Dojos.\r\n\r\nHe graduated from Occidental College in 2007 with a Bachelor\'s degree in Diplomacy and World Affairs, which is a fancy way of saying \"Economics, Business, Politics, and Philosophy.\"\r\n\r\n<a name=\"short\"></a>\r\n<h3>Shorter Bio</h3>\r\n\r\nJason Preston is the Vice President of Product Management and Strategy at the Parnassus Group, a social media intelligence and events production company based in Redmond. Jason has spoken at numerous local and national conferences including the Web Community Forum, The Tweet House, and Ignite Seattle. He has written about social media and emerging technologies in <a href=\"http://crosscut.com\">Crosscut</a> and <a href=\"http://www.seattlebusinessmonthly.com/\">Seattle Business Magazine</a>.\r\n\r\nA lifelong gamer, Jason is the President and co-founder of <a href=\"http://l33tsauce.com\">L33tsauce.com</a>, a videogame site that provides easy-to-use tools for gamers to publish their knowledge in online pages called Dojos. \r\n\r\n<h3>Pictures (right-click to download):</h3>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-460.jpg\" alt=\"jp-widescreen-460\" title=\"jp-widescreen-460\" width=\"460\" height=\"114\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2059\" />\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-large.jpg\">Widescreen - Large Image</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-460.jpg\">Widescreen - 460px wide</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-200.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-200.jpg\" alt=\"jp-200\" title=\"jp-200\" width=\"200\" height=\"266\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2061\" /></a>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-large.jpg\">Regular headshot - Large Image</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-200.jpg\">Regular headshot - 200px wide</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-100.jpg\">Regular headshot - 100px wide</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\"><img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\" alt=\"jason-bnw-border\" title=\"jason-bnw-border\" width=\"240\" height=\"297\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2055\" /></a>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\">Black & White - 240px wide</a></li>\r\n</ul>','Speaking',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','1810-revision-20','','','2010-05-13 14:05:25','2010-05-13 21:05:25','',1810,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/13/1810-revision-20/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2325,1,'2010-05-13 19:05:57','2010-05-14 02:05:57','<div class=\'posterous_autopost\'>As I was just checking in on Foursquare at la cucina del puerco (good Mexican in Bellevue) I realized why Twitter will never kil Foursquare: because 4sq is actually just another portal/interface to Twitter. <p /> Why do I check in? It\'s not for the points, and I don\'t really care if I\'m the mayor unless the mayor gets a discount. I check in so that I can share my location conveniently with my friends on Twitter. <p /> With Foursquare, I navigate to the venue, compose my tweet, and it comes pre populated with a host of geo information about the *venue* - not just about me. <p /> So really when I use Foursquare I\'m just using Twitter, enhanced. <p /> I also suspect that a significant portion of 4sq\'s value is tied to Twitter right now, because they don\'t have a great built in \"stream\" audience (yet). Who knows whether they\'ll be successful in creating that independent community. <p /> But as long as Foursquare is providing an enhacwd interface to Twitter, and driving use of the Twitter network, they won\'t kill Twitter. <p /> - J <p /> Typos sent from (206) 235-8981      <p style=\"font-size: 10px;\">  <a href=\"http://posterous.com\">Posted via email</a>   from <a href=\"http://jasonp107.com/why-foursquare-wont-kill-twitter\">Jason Preston\'s posterous</a>  </p>  </div>','Why Foursquare won\'t kill Twitter',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2323-revision','','','2010-05-13 19:05:57','2010-05-14 02:05:57','',2323,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/13/2323-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2328,1,'2010-05-12 12:47:19','2010-05-12 19:47:19','Hell yes.\n\n<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/Picture-1.png\" alt=\"Picture 1.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"455\" height=\"209\" />','Steam on Mac',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2314-revision-2','','','2010-05-12 12:47:19','2010-05-12 19:47:19','',2314,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/12/2314-revision-2/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2329,1,'2010-05-10 12:58:49','2010-05-10 19:58:49','<div class=\'posterous_autopost\'><img src=\"http://posterous.com/getfile/files.posterous.com/jasonp107/eIJ43EyorjyqCI5a3qrDpbcGAVrmT2RIIh2NBFD8O5JjKUEdzGkHgRiIPcu3/facebooklike.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"244\"/> <p>Heh.</p>      <p style=\"font-size: 10px;\">  <a href=\"http://posterous.com\">Posted via email</a>   from <a href=\"http://jasonp107.com/facebook-shirt\">Jason Preston\'s posterous</a>  </p>  </div>','Facebook shirt',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2296-revision','','','2010-05-10 12:58:49','2010-05-10 19:58:49','',2296,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/10/2296-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2331,1,'2010-05-19 14:42:42','2010-05-19 21:42:42','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Society/2010/0518/Greyson-Chance-What-is-real-in-an-age-of-media-manipulation\">Greyson Chance could be a \"fake\"</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Indeed, London-based media expert Alan Stevens ticks off all the ways the tale fits a carefully managed “populist” rise to stardom:\n\n    <ul><li>Professional video techniques such as cutaways and edit.</li>\n    <li>A lack of complaints about copyright infringement from big names whose work is being copied.</li>\n    <li>Associated Facebook pages and Twitter feeds that appear suddenly.</li>\n    <li>Swift access to top news and other media outlets and immediate availability of talent to travel and be interviewed.</li> </blockquote>\n\n','Greyson Chance could be a \"fake\"',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','greyson-chance-could-be-a-fake','','','2010-05-19 14:42:45','2010-05-19 21:42:45','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2331',0,'post','',0),
	(2330,1,'2010-05-17 19:28:42','2010-05-18 02:28:42','<div class=\'posterous_autopost\'><img src=\"http://posterous.com/getfile/files.posterous.com/jasonp107/eIJ43EyorjyqCI5a3qrDpbcGAVrmT2RIIh2NBFD8O5JjKUEdzGkHgRiIPcu3/facebooklike.png\" alt=\"facebook shirt\" width=\"300\" height=\"244\"/> <p>Heh.</p>      <p style=\"font-size: 10px;\">  <a href=\"http://posterous.com\">Posted via email</a>   from <a href=\"http://jasonp107.com/facebook-shirt\">Jason Preston\'s posterous</a>  </p>  </div>','Facebook shirt',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2296-revision-2','','','2010-05-17 19:28:42','2010-05-18 02:28:42','',2296,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/17/2296-revision-2/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2332,1,'2010-05-19 14:42:42','2010-05-19 21:42:42','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Society/2010/0518/Greyson-Chance-What-is-real-in-an-age-of-media-manipulation\">Greyson Chance could be a \"fake\"</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Indeed, London-based media expert Alan Stevens ticks off all the ways the tale fits a carefully managed “populist” rise to stardom:\n\n    <ul><li>Professional video techniques such as cutaways and edit.</li>\n    <li>A lack of complaints about copyright infringement from big names whose work is being copied.</li>\n    <li>Associated Facebook pages and Twitter feeds that appear suddenly.</li>\n    <li>Swift access to top news and other media outlets and immediate availability of talent to travel and be interviewed.</li> </blockquote>\n\n','Greyson Chance could be a \"fake\"',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2331-revision','','','2010-05-19 14:42:42','2010-05-19 21:42:42','',2331,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/19/2331-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2333,1,'2010-05-23 12:55:11','2010-05-23 19:55:11','Look at the spacing between \"T\" and \"ransition.\" And the papyrus. Welcome to Austin. #fontfail\r\n\r\n<a href=\'http://posterous.com/getfile/files.posterous.com/jasonp107/LC2wtozsLiKMB91m6N4S2vOoDEwXbE4vgpHBbbQKYCLgwE8tSd0Fo5GnHB4X/photo.jpg\'><img src=\"http://posterous.com/getfile/files.posterous.com/jasonp107/OaTyfEhKbTBleMKxvYC13vCiqAf8T0bZirASG6cdBbTUoCr7Wd0J5GmTGpOB/photo.jpg.scaled.500.jpg\" width=\"500\" alt=\"\" height=\"667\"/></a>','My...eyeballs...hurt',0,'','publish','closed','open','','my-eyeballs-hurt','','','2010-05-25 16:49:02','2010-05-25 23:49:02','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/23/my-eyeballs-hurt/',0,'post','',0),
	(2339,1,'2010-05-25 21:45:26','2010-05-26 04:45:26','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://blog.seattlepi.com/thebigblog/archives/207331.asp\">Monica moves to Intersect</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>In June I\'ll begin a new job with a startup called <a href=\"http://intersect.com\">Intersect</a>. I can\'t say much about what it is or what I\'m going to be doing there, but suffice it to say I\'m thrilled. When the opportunity came to join the team, I couldn\'t say no. </blockquote>\n\nCouldn\'t be more proud and excited.','Monica moves to Intersect',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','monica-moves-to-intersect','','','2010-05-25 21:45:29','2010-05-26 04:45:29','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2339',0,'post','',0),
	(2334,1,'2010-05-25 12:33:27','2010-05-25 19:33:27','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/05/popcap_bolsters_board.html\">Why bother?</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>The Seattle maker of hit games such as Bejeweled and Plants vs. Zombies has long been considered a potential IPO candidate. That\'s partly because the 275-person company is profitable and operating in a high-growth industry.</blockquote>\n\nI think PopCap is perfectly placed for organic growth. If you don\'t need public money and public company rules, why bother?','Why bother?',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','why-bother','','','2010-05-25 12:33:31','2010-05-25 19:33:31','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2334',0,'post','',0),
