	(2352,1,'2010-04-12 12:06:37','2010-04-12 19:06:37','This page is basically a rolling list of everything I come across that looks cool and that I think I might want.\r\n\r\nI\'ve decided to bold the things that I know I want, and leave everything else in the \"I wouldn\'t mind having this\" category in normal text.\r\n\r\nSo, (friends and family I assume), here\'s the list of everything I think I might want. Naturally, there\'s nothing I particularly need to have, but lists are always helpful.\r\n\r\nAnyways, here goes:\r\n\r\n<h3>The List</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Feel free to get me another year of any of the following addictions: Zune, Netflix, Cell phone, or PC Gamer...</li>\r\n        <li><strong><a href=\"http://braid-game.com/\">Braid</a> - (Video game)</strong></li>\r\n	<li>Subscription to Fast Company, Wired, Esquire</li>\r\n        <li>Down comforter for the bed</li>\r\n        <li>USB CF card reader with no cord, <a href=\"http://www.google.com/products/catalog?hl=en&source=hp&q=usb+cf+card+reader&um=1&ie=UTF-8&cid=5552213667371327134&ei=IeAlS53XGY3UsQPz38ngDg&sa=X&oi=product_catalog_result&ct=image&resnum=2&ved=0CDQQ8gIwAQ#\">like this one</a></li>\r\n        <li>Cutting board, <a href=\"http://www.surlatable.com/product/epicurean+cutting+surfaces.do?keyword=cutting+board&sortby=ourPicks\">this kind</a>, maybe 15\"x11\"</li>\r\n	<li>Clothes: new shorts, surprises... </li>\r\n	<li>Clothes: pair of slim-cut Khakis that look summer-y</li>\r\n        <li>Ray Ban aviators</li>\r\n	<li>iPad dock connector to VGA output adapter</li>\r\n        <li>Apple iPad case (the one that stands the device up)</li> \r\n        <li>iPhone apps: a good Starmap, etc</li>\r\n	<li>A record player</li>\r\n	<li>A relatively cheap IP-print server</li>\r\n	<li>Good books</li>\r\n        <li>a thing that I wanted to add to the list but forgot... (grr)</li>\r\n	<li>A cool looking decanter (you know, that thing for scotch with a stopper in the top?)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Surprises</strong>!</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Wishes for the future</h3>\r\n\r\nThat is, things I want, but that it doesn\'t make sense for me to have now:\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>A nice, comfy leather (or, theoretically, not leather, if it\'s comfy enough) couch that\'s just the right size and shape to sleep on all day.</li>\r\n	<li>Houseplants - maybe fake</li>\r\n	<li>Set of wireless speakers that can be connected to a standard amp via speaker cable or headphone jack.</li>\r\n         <li>Queen size mattress and bed frame</li>\r\n\r\n</ul>','Jason\'s Wish List',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','1998-revision-20','','','2010-04-12 12:06:37','2010-04-12 19:06:37','',1998,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/04/12/1998-revision-20/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2355,1,'2010-06-01 15:26:30','2010-06-01 22:26:30','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/05/microsoft_plans_seattle-area_store_bringing_home_its_retail_battle_with_apple.html\">Microsoft is not a consumer company</a></div>\n\nMicrosoft makes most of it\'s money from businesses, selling OS licenses to Dell and other computer manufacturers, or enterprise software to enterprise businesses. And so far, they suck at B2C - which is why it\'s surprising that they really want to pick a turf battle with the company running the most successful retail space (by square foot) in existence:\n\n<blockquote>Microsoft plans to open a store at the Bellevue Square mall, bringing its budding retail rivalry with Apple to its own backyard, according to building permits filed with the city.</blockquote>\n\nIf MSFT wants to play in this game, they need to learn to serve the consumer instead of - or as well as - the business. ','Microsoft is not a consumer company',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','microsoft-is-not-a-consumer-company','','','2010-06-01 15:26:32','2010-06-01 22:26:32','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2355',0,'post','',0),
	(2356,1,'2010-06-01 15:26:30','2010-06-01 22:26:30','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/05/microsoft_plans_seattle-area_store_bringing_home_its_retail_battle_with_apple.html\">Microsoft is not a consumer company</a></div>\n\nMicrosoft makes most of it\'s money from businesses, selling OS licenses to Dell and other computer manufacturers, or enterprise software to enterprise businesses. And so far, they suck at B2C - which is why it\'s surprising that they really want to pick a turf battle with the company running the most successful retail space (by square foot) in existence:\n\n<blockquote>Microsoft plans to open a store at the Bellevue Square mall, bringing its budding retail rivalry with Apple to its own backyard, according to building permits filed with the city.</blockquote>\n\nIf MSFT wants to play in this game, they need to learn to serve the consumer instead of - or as well as - the business. ','Microsoft is not a consumer company',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2355-revision','','','2010-06-01 15:26:30','2010-06-01 22:26:30','',2355,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/06/01/2355-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
