	(2360,1,'2010-06-02 10:56:57','2010-06-02 17:56:57','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://video.allthingsd.com/video/d8-comcast-coo-steve-burke-on-google-apple/4E91D565-9BD2-4A46-ADD2-20DC36FDBFAE/\">Comcast COO: It\'s not about the consumer</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>There\'s very little evidence that people are giving up their subscription television. If someone wants ESPN, or they want USA, or they want CNBC, they\'re going to subscribe.</blockquote>\n\nIn other words: \"internet TV-watching is not a problem so long as the consumer has no choice but to pay package prices for a few premium channels.\"\n\n','Comcast COO: It\'s not about the consumer',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','comcast-coo-its-not-about-the-consumer','','','2010-06-02 10:57:00','2010-06-02 17:57:00','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2360',0,'post','',0),
	(2361,1,'2010-06-02 10:56:57','2010-06-02 17:56:57','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://video.allthingsd.com/video/d8-comcast-coo-steve-burke-on-google-apple/4E91D565-9BD2-4A46-ADD2-20DC36FDBFAE/\">Comcast COO: It\'s not about the consumer</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>There\'s very little evidence that people are giving up their subscription television. If someone wants ESPN, or they want USA, or they want CNBC, they\'re going to subscribe.</blockquote>\n\nIn other words: \"internet TV-watching is not a problem so long as the consumer has no choice but to pay package prices for a few premium channels.\"\n\n','Comcast COO: It\'s not about the consumer',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2360-revision','','','2010-06-02 10:56:57','2010-06-02 17:56:57','',2360,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/06/02/2360-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2362,1,'2010-06-03 15:24:53','2010-06-03 22:24:53','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.dailytelegraph.com.au/news/opinion/boatloads-of-bloody-minded-pacifists/story-e6frezz0-1225874166305\">Boatloads of bloody-minded pacifists</a></div>\n\nThe Mavi Marmara, the aid ship where Israeli violence recently broke out, was apparently provided by Turkish charity IHH:\n\n<blockquote>In 2006, the Danish Institute for International Studies reported that Turkish security forces had raided the IHH\'s Istanbul bureau and found firearms, explosives and bomb-making instructions.\n\nThe Turkish investigators concluded this \"charity\" was sending jihadists to Bosnia, Chechnya and Afghanistan.\n\nIHH is a supporter of Hamas, listed in many countries as a terrorist group.</blockquote>\n\nHmmmm. \n\n<blockquote>Those on board refused offers by Israel that they dock at an Israeli port so their aid could be checked and forwarded to Gaza. They rejected warnings to turn back. They prepared instead for confrontation. Arab television showed a woman exulting: \"We await one of two good things - to achieve martyrdom or reach the shore of Gaza.\"</blockquote>\n\n','Boatloads of bloody-minded pacifists',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','boatloads-of-bloody-minded-pacifists','','','2010-06-03 15:24:55','2010-06-03 22:24:55','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2362',0,'post','',0),
	(2363,1,'2010-06-03 15:24:53','2010-06-03 22:24:53','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.dailytelegraph.com.au/news/opinion/boatloads-of-bloody-minded-pacifists/story-e6frezz0-1225874166305\">Boatloads of bloody-minded pacifists</a></div>\n\nThe Mavi Marmara, the aid ship where Israeli violence recently broke out, was apparently provided by Turkish charity IHH:\n\n<blockquote>In 2006, the Danish Institute for International Studies reported that Turkish security forces had raided the IHH\'s Istanbul bureau and found firearms, explosives and bomb-making instructions.\n\nThe Turkish investigators concluded this \"charity\" was sending jihadists to Bosnia, Chechnya and Afghanistan.\n\nIHH is a supporter of Hamas, listed in many countries as a terrorist group.</blockquote>\n\nHmmmm. \n\n<blockquote>Those on board refused offers by Israel that they dock at an Israeli port so their aid could be checked and forwarded to Gaza. They rejected warnings to turn back. They prepared instead for confrontation. Arab television showed a woman exulting: \"We await one of two good things - to achieve martyrdom or reach the shore of Gaza.\"</blockquote>\n\n','Boatloads of bloody-minded pacifists',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2362-revision','','','2010-06-03 15:24:53','2010-06-03 22:24:53','',2362,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/06/03/2362-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2364,1,'2010-05-30 16:45:25','2010-05-30 23:45:25','This page is basically a rolling list of everything I come across that looks cool and that I think I might want.\n\nI\'ve decided to bold the things that I know I want, and leave everything else in the \"I wouldn\'t mind having this\" category in normal text.\n\nSo, (friends and family I assume), here\'s the list of everything I think I might want. Naturally, there\'s nothing I particularly need to have, but lists are always helpful.\n\nAnyways, here goes:\n\n<h3>The List</h3>\n\n<ul>\n	<li>Feel free to get me another year of any of the following addictions: Zune, Netflix, Cell phone, or PC Gamer...</li>\n	<li>Subscription to Fast Company, Wired, Esquire</li>\n        <li>Down comforter for the bed</li>\n        <li>USB CF card reader with no cord, <a href=\"http://www.google.com/products/catalog?hl=en&source=hp&q=usb+cf+card+reader&um=1&ie=UTF-8&cid=5552213667371327134&ei=IeAlS53XGY3UsQPz38ngDg&sa=X&oi=product_catalog_result&ct=image&resnum=2&ved=0CDQQ8gIwAQ#\">like this one</a></li>\n	<li>A record player</li>\n	<li>Good books</li>\n	<li>A cool looking decanter (you know, that thing for scotch with a stopper in the top?)</li>\n	<li><strong>Surprises</strong>!</li>\n\n\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Wishes for the future</h3>\n\nThat is, things I want, but that it doesn\'t make sense for me to have now:\n\n<ul>\n	<li>A nice, comfy leather (or, theoretically, not leather, if it\'s comfy enough) couch that\'s just the right size and shape to sleep on all day.</li>\n	<li>Houseplants - maybe fake</li>\n	<li>Set of wireless speakers that can be connected to a standard amp via speaker cable or headphone jack.</li>\n         <li>Queen size mattress and bed frame</li>\n\n</ul>','Jason\'s Wish List',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','1998-revision-21','','','2010-05-30 16:45:25','2010-05-30 23:45:25','',1998,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/30/1998-revision-21/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2365,1,'2010-06-09 11:28:07','2010-06-09 18:28:07','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://weblogs.hitwise.com/heather-dougherty/2010/03/facebook_reaches_top_ranking_i.html\">Hitwise: Facebook traffic surpasses Google</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Facebook reached an important milestone for the week ending March 13, 2010 and surpassed Google in the US to become the most visited website for the week.</blockquote>\n\nWow.','Hitwise: Facebook traffic surpasses Google',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','hitwise-facebook-traffic-surpasses-google','','','2010-06-09 11:28:13','2010-06-09 18:28:13','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2365',0,'post','',0),
