	(2376,1,'2010-06-17 10:33:46','2010-06-17 17:33:46','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/06/microsofts_e3_xbox_bribery_makes_journalism_ethicists_squirm.html\">Microsoft\'s Xbox 360 \'bribery\' makes journalists squirm</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>\"Yes, Microsoft basically bribed the press,\" writes Stephen C. Webster in a post on the True/Slant blog that has been getting broader attention in business journalism circles.</blockquote>\n\nStrong words. To me bribery requires that bribing be the intent, and I doubt Microsoft went into this thinking \"I know, we\'ll bribe the press into writing good things about us by giving them Xbox 360s.\"\n\nI\'m guessing the thought process was more like: \"wouldn\'t it be cool if we pulled an Oprah and gave something cool to the audience?\"','Microsoft\'s Xbox 360 \'bribery\' makes journalists squirm',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','microsofts-xbox-360-bribery-makes-journalists-squirm','','','2010-06-17 10:33:48','2010-06-17 17:33:48','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2376',0,'post','',0),
	(2377,1,'2010-06-17 10:33:46','2010-06-17 17:33:46','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/06/microsofts_e3_xbox_bribery_makes_journalism_ethicists_squirm.html\">Microsoft\'s Xbox 360 \'bribery\' makes journalists squirm</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>\"Yes, Microsoft basically bribed the press,\" writes Stephen C. Webster in a post on the True/Slant blog that has been getting broader attention in business journalism circles.</blockquote>\n\nStrong words. To me bribery requires that bribing be the intent, and I doubt Microsoft went into this thinking \"I know, we\'ll bribe the press into writing good things about us by giving them Xbox 360s.\"\n\nI\'m guessing the thought process was more like: \"wouldn\'t it be cool if we pulled an Oprah and gave something cool to the audience?\"','Microsoft\'s Xbox 360 \'bribery\' makes journalists squirm',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2376-revision','','','2010-06-17 10:33:46','2010-06-17 17:33:46','',2376,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/06/17/2376-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2378,1,'2010-06-21 12:02:21','2010-06-21 19:02:21','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2010/06/20/the-anosognosics-dilemma-1/?hp\">Too incompetent to know</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>It became known as the Dunning-Kruger Effect — our incompetence masks our ability to recognize our incompetence. </blockquote>\n\nLove it.','Too incompetent to know',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','too-incompetent-to-know','','','2010-06-21 12:02:23','2010-06-21 19:02:23','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2378',0,'post','',0),
