	(2406,1,'2010-08-30 15:11:32','2010-08-30 22:11:32','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/08/also_in_allens_patent_pile_ideas_similar_to_twitter_foursquare.html\">Paul Allen\'s Twitter Patent</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>A patent application submitted by Paul Allen\'s Interval Research in 1998 envisioned groups of authenticated users sharing \"lightweight messages\" through a central server, using distributed client devices.</blockquote>\n\nTo borrow phraseology for some other common statments: The Patent system of protecting inventions is the worst system ever created to protect inventions, except for all the others. ','Paul Allen\'s Twitter Patent',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','paul-allens-twitter-patent','','','2010-08-30 15:11:37','2010-08-30 22:11:37','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2406',0,'post','',0),
	(2407,1,'2010-08-30 15:11:32','2010-08-30 22:11:32','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/08/also_in_allens_patent_pile_ideas_similar_to_twitter_foursquare.html\">Paul Allen\'s Twitter Patent</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>A patent application submitted by Paul Allen\'s Interval Research in 1998 envisioned groups of authenticated users sharing \"lightweight messages\" through a central server, using distributed client devices.</blockquote>\n\nTo borrow phraseology for some other common statments: The Patent system of protecting inventions is the worst system ever created to protect inventions, except for all the others. ','Paul Allen\'s Twitter Patent',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2406-revision','','','2010-08-30 15:11:32','2010-08-30 22:11:32','',2406,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/08/30/2406-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2408,1,'2010-09-01 14:48:21','2010-09-01 21:48:21','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.seattle20.com/startupday/\">StartupDay 2010</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>StartupDay 2010 is the conference for pre-entrepreneurs interested in founding or joining a tech startup. Learn what’s important for creating a tech business from scratch.</blockquote>\n\nOne the people in Seattle working hard to reinvent the technology events scene (it DOES need some reinventing) is Marcelo Calbucci. \n\nIf you\'re in the Seattle area and you\'re thinking about putting aside the daily grind and setting out into the vast, uncharted regions of startupland, I\'d recommend <a href=\"http://www.seattle20.com/startupday/register.aspx\">picking up a ticket</a> to this conference, scheduled for September 25th. \n\nI\'ll be hanging around, so be sure to say hi. \n','StartupDay 2010',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','startupday-2010','','','2010-09-01 15:44:13','2010-09-01 22:44:13','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2408',0,'post','',0),
