	(2428,1,'2010-09-10 12:45:57','2010-09-10 19:45:57','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://bobulate.com/post/1097690674/the-design-of-serendipity-is-not-by-chance\">The design of serendipity</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>There are, however, variations at play all the time. Smart services such as Dopplr, Foursquare, and EveryBlock have designed for chance encounters alongside of exact retrieval so users can have dual experiences. The designers have simply put forth opportunities for people to create their own pathways.</blockquote>\n\nIf you\'re not yet reading <a href=\"http://bobulate.com/\">Bobulate</a>, I suggest you start. ','The design of serendipity',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','the-design-of-serendipity','','','2010-09-10 12:46:00','2010-09-10 19:46:00','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2428',0,'post','',0),
	(2429,1,'2010-09-10 12:45:57','2010-09-10 19:45:57','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://bobulate.com/post/1097690674/the-design-of-serendipity-is-not-by-chance\">The design of serendipity</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>There are, however, variations at play all the time. Smart services such as Dopplr, Foursquare, and EveryBlock have designed for chance encounters alongside of exact retrieval so users can have dual experiences. The designers have simply put forth opportunities for people to create their own pathways.</blockquote>\n\nIf you\'re not yet reading <a href=\"http://bobulate.com/\">Bobulate</a>, I suggest you start. ','The design of serendipity',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2428-revision','','','2010-09-10 12:45:57','2010-09-10 19:45:57','',2428,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/10/2428-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2430,1,'2010-09-10 13:45:58','2010-09-10 20:45:58','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.quora.com/What-is-the-most-useful-shortest-and-most-generally-applicable-piece-of-wisdom-you-know\">What is the most useful, shortest, and most generally applicable piece of wisdom you know?</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>\"I suppose if we couldn\'t laugh at things that don\'t make sense, we couldn\'t react to a lot of life.\" - Bill Watterson (Calvin and Hobbes)</blockquote>\n\nI love finding little gems like this in answers to questions on Quora. Very <a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/10/the-design-of-serendipity/\">serendipitous</a>. ','What is the most useful, shortest, and most generally applicable piece of wisdom you know?',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','what-is-the-most-useful-shortest-and-most-generally-applicable-piece-of-wisdom-you-know','','','2010-09-10 13:46:01','2010-09-10 20:46:01','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2430',0,'post','',0),
	(2431,1,'2010-09-10 13:45:58','2010-09-10 20:45:58','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://www.quora.com/What-is-the-most-useful-shortest-and-most-generally-applicable-piece-of-wisdom-you-know\">What is the most useful, shortest, and most generally applicable piece of wisdom you know?</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>\"I suppose if we couldn\'t laugh at things that don\'t make sense, we couldn\'t react to a lot of life.\" - Bill Watterson (Calvin and Hobbes)</blockquote>\n\nI love finding little gems like this in answers to questions on Quora. Very <a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/10/the-design-of-serendipity/\">serendipitous</a>. ','What is the most useful, shortest, and most generally applicable piece of wisdom you know?',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2430-revision','','','2010-09-10 13:45:58','2010-09-10 20:45:58','',2430,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/10/2430-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2432,1,'2010-09-14 11:05:18','2010-09-14 18:05:18','I live in Seattle and work in Redmond (I\'m the one guy who works in Redmond, but <em>not</em> for Microsoft), which means that I spend about an hour and a half in my car every day. \n\nI\'ve developed a rotation of audio entertainment for my car, which goes through phases: cycling the radio stations, listening to books on tape from Audible.com, converting text news stories to audio in the morning and listening to the news on my way in to work, and of course - digging up my old CDs, or streaming music from my media center to my iPhone. \n\nThis morning I discovered a new, potentially bottomless source of \"morning drive\" entertainment: YouTube. It turns out that my iPhone\'s 3G connection is more than sufficient to stream the bazillions of panels, movies, clips, series, and otherwise useless entertainment on YouTube that is primarily audio anyway. \n\nSweet.','YouTube in my Car',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','youtube-in-my-car','','','2010-09-14 11:05:21','2010-09-14 18:05:21','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2432',0,'post','',0),
	(2433,1,'2010-09-14 11:05:18','2010-09-14 18:05:18','I live in Seattle and work in Redmond (I\'m the one guy who works in Redmond, but <em>not</em> for Microsoft), which means that I spend about an hour and a half in my car every day. \n\nI\'ve developed a rotation of audio entertainment for my car, which goes through phases: cycling the radio stations, listening to books on tape from Audible.com, converting text news stories to audio in the morning and listening to the news on my way in to work, and of course - digging up my old CDs, or streaming music from my media center to my iPhone. \n\nThis morning I discovered a new, potentially bottomless source of \"morning drive\" entertainment: YouTube. It turns out that my iPhone\'s 3G connection is more than sufficient to stream the bazillions of panels, movies, clips, series, and otherwise useless entertainment on YouTube that is primarily audio anyway. \n\nSweet.','YouTube in my Car',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2432-revision','','','2010-09-14 11:05:18','2010-09-14 18:05:18','',2432,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/14/2432-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2434,1,'2010-09-15 13:14:07','2010-09-15 20:14:07','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://minimalmac.com/post/1126901994/medieval-multitasking-did-we-ever-focus-culture\">On links and distractions</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>In contrast, the internet is vast and seemingly endless and it is very easy to follow a trail that takes you quickly away from the content and context in which you started. </blockquote>\n\n\"Going down the rabbit hole,\" as my boss calls it, has often led to some of my most productive brainstorms, greatest opportunities, and coolest nibblets of wisdom. \n\nDistraction? or <a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/10/the-design-of-serendipity/\">Seredipity</a>?','On links and distractions',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','on-links-and-distractions','','','2010-09-15 13:14:10','2010-09-15 20:14:10','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2434',0,'post','',0),
	(2435,1,'2010-09-15 13:14:07','2010-09-15 20:14:07','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://minimalmac.com/post/1126901994/medieval-multitasking-did-we-ever-focus-culture\">On links and distractions</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>In contrast, the internet is vast and seemingly endless and it is very easy to follow a trail that takes you quickly away from the content and context in which you started. </blockquote>\n\n\"Going down the rabbit hole,\" as my boss calls it, has often led to some of my most productive brainstorms, greatest opportunities, and coolest nibblets of wisdom. \n\nDistraction? or <a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/10/the-design-of-serendipity/\">Seredipity</a>?','On links and distractions',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2434-revision','','','2010-09-15 13:14:07','2010-09-15 20:14:07','',2434,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/15/2434-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2436,1,'2010-09-15 13:32:28','2010-09-15 20:32:28','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://billhillsblog.blogspot.com/2010/09/ipad-blows-kindle-out-of-water-but.html\">I Totally Disagree: Kindle vs. iPad</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>The Bottom Line: Since I got my iPad, I find reading books on it so good that I can no longer bear to use my Kindle - although the Kindle app is the best eBook reader on the iPad, and the only one I use. Picking up the Kindle - after using the iPad for several weeks - is like stepping back into the Dark Ages of eBooks - a small-screen world of poor contrast, in which you can read comfortably only in perfect, bright lighting. It looks somehow pathetic alongside the iPad.</blockquote>\n\nI could not disagree more. The iPad is my <em>least</em> favorite way to read long form content (magazine articles, instapaper, books). I even prefer my iPhone to my iPad. \n\nThe Kindle is best of all; it is lightweight, it doesn\'t hurt my eyes, I can read it in the sun, it has fewer distractions, it disappears when in use, it connects to the internet for free, and it is easier to turn pages. \n\n(link found via <a href=\"http://daringfireball.net/linked/2010/09/15/hill\">Gruber</a>)','I Totally Disagree: Kindle vs. iPad',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','i-totally-disagree-kindle-vs-ipad','','','2010-09-15 13:32:30','2010-09-15 20:32:30','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2436',0,'post','',0),
	(2437,1,'2010-09-15 13:32:28','2010-09-15 20:32:28','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://billhillsblog.blogspot.com/2010/09/ipad-blows-kindle-out-of-water-but.html\">I Totally Disagree: Kindle vs. iPad</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>The Bottom Line: Since I got my iPad, I find reading books on it so good that I can no longer bear to use my Kindle - although the Kindle app is the best eBook reader on the iPad, and the only one I use. Picking up the Kindle - after using the iPad for several weeks - is like stepping back into the Dark Ages of eBooks - a small-screen world of poor contrast, in which you can read comfortably only in perfect, bright lighting. It looks somehow pathetic alongside the iPad.</blockquote>\n\nI could not disagree more. The iPad is my <em>least</em> favorite way to read long form content (magazine articles, instapaper, books). I even prefer my iPhone to my iPad. \n\nThe Kindle is best of all; it is lightweight, it doesn\'t hurt my eyes, I can read it in the sun, it has fewer distractions, it disappears when in use, it connects to the internet for free, and it is easier to turn pages. \n\n(link found via <a href=\"http://daringfireball.net/linked/2010/09/15/hill\">Gruber</a>)','I Totally Disagree: Kindle vs. iPad',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2436-revision','','','2010-09-15 13:32:28','2010-09-15 20:32:28','',2436,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/15/2436-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2438,1,'2010-05-25 22:47:27','2010-05-26 05:47:27','<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\" alt=\"jason-bnw-border\" title=\"jason-bnw-border\" width=\"240\" height=\"297\" class=\"alignright size-full wp-image-2055\" /><strong>Jason Preston</strong> is an accomplished public speaker and a recognized expert in both social media and publishing. \r\n\r\nHe has presented for the Web Community Forum, the Redmond Chamber of Commerce, the Greater Seattle Chamber of Commerce, SCORE, the Social Networking for Business Conference, Ignite Seattle, and 140 | The Twitter Conference.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in having Jason speak at your event, please <strong>contact him</strong> via e-mail: \r\n<strong>\r\nj AT jason-preston.com. </strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Video of Jason\'s work:</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n        <li>The Twitter Conference: <a href=\"http://vimeo.com/7148408\">The Comedy Session - Being Funny, In Short</a></li>\r\n	<li>Ignite Seattle: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTY9PjrFOhA\">How to Say Anything in 140 Characters or Less</a></li>\r\n	<li>Seattle Chamber: <a href=\"http://vimeo.com/3442553\">Buzz Monitoring in Social Media</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a name=\"long\"></a>\r\n<h3>Longer Bio</h3>\r\n\r\nJason Preston is the Vice President of Strategy and Product Development for the <a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com\">Parnassus Group</a>, a Redmond-based company that produces conferences and parties around emerging technologies, and provides social media intelligence to clients and partners seeking to effectively participate in online communities. \r\n\r\nJason has worked with clients on shaping blogger engagement strategies, creating blogs, and understanding the business value of social media tools like Twitter and Facebook. He has spoken at numerous local and national conferences including the Web Community Forum, The Tweet House, and Ignite Seattle. He has written about social media and emerging technologies in <a href=\"http://crosscut.com\">Crosscut</a> and <a href=\"http://www.seattlebusinessmonthly.com/\">Seattle Business Magazine</a>.\r\n\r\nA lifelong gamer, Jason is the President and co-founder of <a href=\"http://l33tsauce.com\">L33tsauce.com</a>, a videogame site that provides easy-to-use tools for gamers to publish their knowledge in online pages called Dojos. Gamers earn 50% of the ad revenue generated from their Dojos.\r\n\r\nHe graduated from Occidental College in 2007 with a Bachelor\'s degree in Diplomacy and World Affairs, which is a fancy way of saying \"Economics, Business, Politics, and Philosophy.\"\r\n\r\n<a name=\"short\"></a>\r\n<h3>Shorter Bio</h3>\r\n\r\nJason Preston is the Vice President of Strategy and Product Development at the Parnassus Group, a social media intelligence and events production company based in Redmond. Jason has spoken at numerous local and national conferences including the Web Community Forum, The Tweet House, and Ignite Seattle. He has written about social media and emerging technologies in <a href=\"http://crosscut.com\">Crosscut</a> and <a href=\"http://www.seattlebusinessmonthly.com/\">Seattle Business Magazine</a>.\r\n\r\nA lifelong gamer, Jason is the President and co-founder of <a href=\"http://l33tsauce.com\">L33tsauce.com</a>, a videogame site that provides easy-to-use tools for gamers to publish their knowledge in online pages called Dojos. \r\n\r\n<h3>Pictures (right-click to download):</h3>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-460.jpg\" alt=\"jp-widescreen-460\" title=\"jp-widescreen-460\" width=\"460\" height=\"114\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2059\" />\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-large.jpg\">Widescreen - Large Image</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-widescreen-460.jpg\">Widescreen - 460px wide</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-200.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-200.jpg\" alt=\"jp-200\" title=\"jp-200\" width=\"200\" height=\"266\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2061\" /></a>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-large.jpg\">Regular headshot - Large Image</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-200.jpg\">Regular headshot - 200px wide</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jp-100.jpg\">Regular headshot - 100px wide</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\"><img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\" alt=\"jason-bnw-border\" title=\"jason-bnw-border\" width=\"240\" height=\"297\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2055\" /></a>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\">Black & White - 240px wide</a></li>\r\n</ul>','Speaking',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','1810-revision-23','','','2010-05-25 22:47:27','2010-05-26 05:47:27','',1810,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/05/25/1810-revision-23/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2439,1,'2009-04-14 13:01:40','2009-04-14 20:01:40','<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/11/me200w.jpg\" alt=\"me200w\" title=\"Me, smiling. Why are there ridiculous bags under my eyes?\" width=\"200\" height=\"232\" class=\"alignright size-full wp-image-2028\" />I\'m not a big fan of about pages. I don\'t think there\'s really any good way to fit myself into a hundred or so words and a snazzy photo, but I\'m going to give it a shot. \r\n\r\nI am currently the Director of New Media at <a href=\"http://www.parnassusgroup.com\">Parnassus Group</a>, the company responsible for the incredibly cool Blog Business Summit and Web Community Forum events. As with most work in the \"web 2.0\" world, exactly <em>what</em> I do is a little hard to define, but it involves a lot of fun things with a lot of cool people.\r\n\r\nIn my spare time I work for myself. I\'m currently writing a book and sitting on two brilliant business ideas that are sure to make me a millionaire by 30, and I\'m willing to bet I\'ll be saying that for the next 15 years. This site is where I play with ideas, expressions, and technical details - and I should probably mention that it has nothing to do with the fine folks at Parnassus. \r\n\r\nIf you want to find out more about who I am, by far the best way to do so is to subscribe to <a href=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/jasonpreston\">my RSS feed</a>. You\'ll get a much better picture of who I am by reading about my life and opinions piece by piece. This is the beauty of the blogosphere. \r\n\r\nOther places I exist online:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.eatsleeppublish.com\">Eat Sleep Publish</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com/blog/\">Parnassus Group Blog</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://oxy.facebook.com/profile.php?id=14500137\">Facebook Profile</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/profile?viewProfile=&key=7361027\">LinkedIn Profile</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/jasonp107\">Twitter</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/id/jasonp107/\">Steam</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://biznik.com/members/jason-preston\">Biznik</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nIf I\'m on anything else, chances are my username is Jasonp107\r\n\r\n','About',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','960-revision-2','','','2009-04-14 13:01:40','2009-04-14 20:01:40','',960,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2009/04/14/960-revision-2/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2440,1,'2010-09-17 18:22:56','2010-09-18 01:22:56','<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/jason-bnw-border.gif\" alt=\"jason-bnw-border\" title=\"jason-bnw-border\" width=\"240\" height=\"297\" class=\"alignright size-full wp-image-2055\" /><strong>Jason Preston</strong> is an accomplished public speaker and a recognized expert in both social media and publishing. \r\n\r\nHe has presented for the Web Community Forum, the Redmond Chamber of Commerce, the Greater Seattle Chamber of Commerce, SCORE, the Social Networking for Business Conference, Ignite Seattle, and 140 | The Twitter Conference.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested in having Jason speak at your event, please <strong>contact him</strong> via e-mail: \r\n<strong>\r\nj AT jason-preston.com. </strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Video of Jason\'s work:</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n        <li>The Twitter Conference: <a href=\"http://vimeo.com/7148408\">The Comedy Session - Being Funny, In Short</a></li>\r\n	<li>Ignite Seattle: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTY9PjrFOhA\">How to Say Anything in 140 Characters or Less</a></li>\r\n	<li>Seattle Chamber: <a href=\"http://vimeo.com/3442553\">Buzz Monitoring in Social Media</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a name=\"long\"></a>\r\n<h3>Longer Bio</h3>\r\n\r\nJason Preston is the Vice President of Strategy and Product Development for the <a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com\">Parnassus Group</a>, a Redmond-based company that produces conferences and parties around emerging technologies, and provides social media intelligence to clients and partners seeking to effectively participate in online communities. \r\n\r\nJason has worked with clients on shaping blogger engagement strategies, creating blogs, and understanding the business value of social media tools like Twitter and Facebook. He has spoken at numerous local and national conferences including the Web Community Forum, The Tweet House, and Ignite Seattle. He has written about social media and emerging tec