	(2441,1,'2010-09-17 18:23:05','2010-09-18 01:23:05','<img src=\"http://www.jason-preston.com/wp-content/uploads/2006/11/me200w.jpg\" alt=\"me200w\" title=\"Me, smiling. Why are there ridiculous bags under my eyes?\" width=\"200\" height=\"232\" class=\"alignright size-full wp-image-2028\" />I\'m not a big fan of about pages. I don\'t think there\'s really any good way to fit myself into a hundred or so words and a snazzy photo, but I\'m going to give it a shot. \r\n\r\nI am currently the Director of New Media at <a href=\"http://www.parnassusgroup.com\">Parnassus Group</a>, the company responsible for the incredibly cool Blog Business Summit and Web Community Forum events. As with most work in the \"web 2.0\" world, exactly <em>what</em> I do is a little hard to define, but it involves a lot of fun things with a lot of cool people.\r\n\r\nIn my spare time I work for myself. I\'m currently writing a book and sitting on two brilliant business ideas that are sure to make me a millionaire by 30, and I\'m willing to bet I\'ll be saying that for the next 15 years. This site is where I play with ideas, expressions, and technical details - and I should probably mention that it has nothing to do with the fine folks at Parnassus. \r\n\r\nIf you want to find out more about who I am, by far the best way to do so is to subscribe to <a href=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/jasonpreston\">my RSS feed</a>. You\'ll get a much better picture of who I am by reading about my life and opinions piece by piece. This is the beauty of the blogosphere. \r\n\r\nOther places I exist online:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.eatsleeppublish.com\">Eat Sleep Publish</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://parnassusgroup.com/blog/\">Parnassus Group Blog</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://oxy.facebook.com/profile.php?id=14500137\">Facebook Profile</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/profile?viewProfile=&key=7361027\">LinkedIn Profile</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/jasonp107\">Twitter</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/id/jasonp107/\">Steam</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://biznik.com/members/jason-preston\">Biznik</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nIf I\'m on anything else, chances are my username is Jasonp107\r\n\r\n','About',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','960-revision-3','','','2010-09-17 18:23:05','2010-09-18 01:23:05','',960,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/17/960-revision-3/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2442,1,'2010-09-22 12:35:14','2010-09-22 19:35:14','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://bobulate.com/post/1167329923/half-time\">Relativity</a></div>\n\nThis is awesome. Click through for the full treatment. \n\n<blockquote>In other words, if time is a series of consecutive instants, and motion means passing through consecutive points, then the Bs are passing the As at the fastest possible speed — one point per instant. How then is it that the Bs are passing the Cs at twice this rate? It seems, Aristotle noted, that “half the time is equal to its double.”</blockquote>\n\n','Relativity',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','relativity','','','2010-09-22 12:35:18','2010-09-22 19:35:18','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2442',0,'post','',0),
	(2443,1,'2010-09-22 12:35:14','2010-09-22 19:35:14','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://bobulate.com/post/1167329923/half-time\">Relativity</a></div>\n\nThis is awesome. Click through for the full treatment. \n\n<blockquote>In other words, if time is a series of consecutive instants, and motion means passing through consecutive points, then the Bs are passing the As at the fastest possible speed — one point per instant. How then is it that the Bs are passing the Cs at twice this rate? It seems, Aristotle noted, that “half the time is equal to its double.”</blockquote>\n\n','Relativity',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2442-revision','','','2010-09-22 12:35:14','2010-09-22 19:35:14','',2442,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/09/22/2442-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2444,1,'2010-09-23 11:14:59','2010-09-23 18:14:59','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/09/seattle_a_top_social_city_but_lacking_in_twitter_usage.html\">TechFlash on Twinfluence</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Seattle ranked 20th in the Twitter category, coming in behind places like Boise, Louisville and Miami. So, what gives? I certainly know a lot of Seattle business people who Tweet, but they may not be as influential as they think. The study -- conducted by NetProspex -- determined the Twitter score based on the number of Twitter accounts, number of followers and total Tweets.</blockquote>\n\nGood question. I can certainly see why New York and Los Angeles would, with their celebrity populations, jump ahead of Seattle. But Boise?\n\n\n\n','TechFlash on Twinfluence',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','techflash-on-twinfluence','','','2010-09-23 11:15:02','2010-09-23 18:15:02','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2444',0,'post','',0),
