	(2469,1,'2010-10-14 12:05:19','2010-10-14 19:05:19','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/10/starbucks_lets_people_buy_a_friend_coffee_on_facebook.html\">Starbucks lets people buy a friend coffee on Facebook</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Under a new Give a Gift feature on the Starbucks Card Facebook app, people can load cash directly onto a friend\'s Starbucks card — anything between $5 and $500 — sort of a digital stocking stuffer.</blockquote>\n\nThis could turn out to be a serious moneymaker for Starbucks, especially in time for the holiday season (weather is cold, people are generous). There\'s something much easier, in a way, about buying coffee for someone else than just buying coffee for yourself. \n\n','Starbucks lets people buy a friend coffee on Facebook',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','starbucks-lets-people-buy-a-friend-coffee-on-facebook','','','2010-10-14 12:05:22','2010-10-14 19:05:22','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2469',0,'post','',0),
	(2470,1,'2010-10-14 12:05:19','2010-10-14 19:05:19','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://techflash.com/seattle/2010/10/starbucks_lets_people_buy_a_friend_coffee_on_facebook.html\">Starbucks lets people buy a friend coffee on Facebook</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Under a new Give a Gift feature on the Starbucks Card Facebook app, people can load cash directly onto a friend\'s Starbucks card — anything between $5 and $500 — sort of a digital stocking stuffer.</blockquote>\n\nThis could turn out to be a serious moneymaker for Starbucks, especially in time for the holiday season (weather is cold, people are generous). There\'s something much easier, in a way, about buying coffee for someone else than just buying coffee for yourself. \n\n','Starbucks lets people buy a friend coffee on Facebook',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2469-revision','','','2010-10-14 12:05:19','2010-10-14 19:05:19','',2469,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/10/14/2469-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2471,1,'2010-10-18 18:42:08','2010-10-19 01:42:08','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://searchengineland.com/hard-news-pays-more-than-chasing-search-trends-53103\">Hard News Pays Publishers More Than Chasing Search Trends, Report Says</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Perfect Market, a company that works with publishers to help them make more money from search engine visitors, has just released its Vault Index, a list of the most valuable online news topics. The bottom line? Hot topics (like Tiger Woods’ troubles and other celebrity news) may bring in search traffic, but hard news brings in the most money.</blockquote>\n\nAwesome.\n','Hard News Pays Publishers More Than Chasing Search Trends, Report Says',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','hard-news-pays-publishers-more-than-chasing-search-trends-report-says','','','2010-10-18 18:42:10','2010-10-19 01:42:10','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2471',0,'post','',0),
	(2472,1,'2010-10-18 18:42:08','2010-10-19 01:42:08','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://searchengineland.com/hard-news-pays-more-than-chasing-search-trends-53103\">Hard News Pays Publishers More Than Chasing Search Trends, Report Says</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>Perfect Market, a company that works with publishers to help them make more money from search engine visitors, has just released its Vault Index, a list of the most valuable online news topics. The bottom line? Hot topics (like Tiger Woods’ troubles and other celebrity news) may bring in search traffic, but hard news brings in the most money.</blockquote>\n\nAwesome.\n','Hard News Pays Publishers More Than Chasing Search Trends, Report Says',0,'','inherit','closed','open','','2471-revision','','','2010-10-18 18:42:08','2010-10-19 01:42:08','',2471,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/10/18/2471-revision/',0,'revision','',0),
	(2473,1,'2010-10-21 13:14:04','2010-10-21 20:14:04','I think people go to events for several reasons. But the biggest reason people go to events is to be with the other people at the event.\n\nWhen you create an event, you are creating an ad-hoc network of people. A group of humans who are going to share an experience, and create relationships that would otherwise not be possible.\n\nHopefully they will learn something new, but you can teach courses online. If the point is to just learn about new techniques or tools, why travel?\n\nSo it matters who comes to your event. This is one reason we keep a guest list or our Tweet Houses. When we host a conference it costs several hundred dollars to attend, so the problem solves itself: the people who come are people who want to get something out of the experience, because they paid to attend. At a free event, we need to crete another gateway.\n\nJust remember, if you\'re putting together an event: the \"who\" is as important (or more) as the \"what\" and the \"where.\"','Why people go to events',0,'','publish','closed','open','','why-people-go-to-events','','','2010-10-21 13:14:04','2010-10-21 20:14:04','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/index.php/2010/10/21/why-people-go-to-events/',0,'post','',0),
	(2474,1,'2010-11-03 14:44:15','2010-11-03 21:44:15','<div class=\"ll\"><a href=\"http://tweet-house.com/2010/gm-robonaut-2-headed-for-the-international-space-station/\">GM \"Robonaut 2\" Headed for the International Space Station</a></div>\n\n<blockquote>During one of our tours, we got a chance to see the state of the art humanoid robot dubbed \"Robonaut 2\", or R2 for short (who’s the Star Wars fan?). And let me tell you, this thing is pretty cool.</blockquote>\n\nA quick post about my ongoing visit to Florida for the Space Shuttle launch.\n','GM “Robonaut 2? Headed for the International Space Station',0,'','publish','closed','closed','','gm-%e2%80%9crobonaut-2%e2%80%b3-headed-for-the-international-space-station','','','2010-11-03 14:53:33','2010-11-03 21:53:33','',0,'http://www.jason-preston.com/?p=2474',0,'post','',0),
